{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox","id":1555226,"title":"Bloodlines 2 And The Current State Of Paradox","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-11-07T19:00:19-08:00","id":1555226,"title":"Bloodlines 2 And The Current State Of Paradox","content":"Last year September Paradox's leadership <a href=\"https://www.pcgamer.com/games/rpg/paradox-wants-to-get-out-of-the-rpg-business-if-bloodlines-2-god-willing-is-successful-bloodlines-3-will-be-done-by-someone-else/\" target=\"_blank\">dropped a bit of a bombshell</a> in what they thought about the (then upcoming) release of Bloodlines 2:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;It is not in our strategic direction to make this kind of game,&quot; Lilja says. &quot;So if Bloodlines 2, God willing, is successful, Bloodlines 3 [will be] done by someone else, on the licence from us. I would say it's the sort of strategic way this would work. So it's still an outlier from what we're supposed to do, we don't know that stuff, so we should probably let other people do it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Paradox has its own small-scale experimental label, Paradox Arc, where it can try different things, but a big RPG doesn't remotely fit that. It would have to be something &quot;very different&quot;, says Lilja, like a CRPG, but even that's a &quot;big investment&quot;, and nowadays expectations are higher than ever thanks to Baldur's Gate 3. So &quot;regardless of outcome,&quot; he says, Bloodlines is a &quot;dead end&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Here we are, a little bit more than a year later and Bloodlines 2 has come out. I've mentioned in other threads what I've thought of the game but this is more about the stats. The game sits on Metacritic with a 63 (Mixed or Average), with the majority of reviews being in the Mixed-category. On Steam, it similarly has a Mixed-rating (57% of the Steam-user-reviews are positive).<br /> <br /> But what does that mean?<br /> <br /> Paradox's report of January - September 2025 has dropped a few weeks ago. Some highlights (source: <a href=\"https://wnhub.io/news/finance/item-49137\" target=\"_blank\">wnhub.com</a>);<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <ul><li>Paradox Interactive earned a total of 1.3 billion Swedish kronor (140.3 million dollars) over the nine months. This is 12% less than the previous year.</li> <li>Almost all the revenue came from PC games, which generated 1.14 billion Swedish kronor (122 million dollars) or 86.9% of the total revenue. Compared to last year, this amount dropped by 11%.</li> <li>Console games contributed another 119.7 million Swedish kronor (12.75 million dollars, down 21%). Mobile games accounted for 36.5 million Swedish kronor (3.9 million dollars, down 5.5%).</li> <li>Despite the decline in revenue, Paradox Interactive's operating profit increased by 20%. It amounted to 391.4 million Swedish kronor (41.7 million dollars).</li> <li>The company attributed the decline in revenue to the strengthening of the Swedish krona and fewer releases. Moreover, in the third quarter of 2025 (July-September), they heavily invested in marketing for Vampire: The Masquerade \u2014 Bloodlines 2 and Europa Universalis V.</li> <li>Paradox Interactive is not ready to draw conclusions about the release of Vampire: The Masquerade \u2014 Bloodlines 2 yet, as the game was released only a few days before the report's publication, making it too early to assess. However, the company is closely monitoring audience reactions. It should be noted that the game currently has a &quot;mixed&quot; rating on Steam, with only 55% of reviews being positive.</li> <li>Currently, Paradox Interactive is working on eight new games.</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div>But we also got some estimates for how much Paradox spent on Bloodlines 2's development. <a href=\"https://www.swedbank-aktiellt.se/analyser/2025/10/09/\" target=\"_blank\">Swedish analysts for Swedbank</a> (the subsidiary Swedbank Robur is a <a href=\"https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/investors/ownership-structure\" target=\"_blank\">shareholder of Paradox Interactive</a>) think that Paradox has spent somewhere around 60 million dollars on Bloodlines 2 (without marketing). According to <a href=\"https://app.sensortower.com/vgi/game/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2\" target=\"_blank\">VG Insights</a>, the game has earned 13 million dollars so far (that's also just a rough estimate). <br /> <br /> The question is that despite Paradox financing DLC for Bloodlines 2, whether they will stick to their mindset of &quot;Bloodlines 2 is a dead end.&quot; with these sales-figures in mind. Obviously, it was always a huge challenge for the TCR-version of this game to get them out of the financial hole that the years of development-hell had created. But it matters who Paradox-leadership will blame for having gotten them into this situation. And how does Paradox evaluate the WOD-license as a whole after they've found who's to blame for all of this? Will it just be visual novels and text-adventures for WOD-games for the rest of time? Or will they consider ever doing something on the level of a Bloodlines 2 (minus the development-hell-bit, of course) again?<br /> <br /> Personally, I think this quarter will reaffirm this &quot;Bloodlines 2 is a dead end&quot;-mindset because the real money-getter for Paradox will probably end up being Europa Universalis 5 (another typical Paradox grand strategy game) rather than Bloodlines 2. I guess we'll see what Paradox will end up saying about the Bloodlines 2 release but right now I don't see how the leadership won't just stick to the ideas they expressed last year.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-08T01:06:42-08:00","id":1555228,"title":"","content":"The problem is whose to blame for this is themselves so any assesment will be flawed.<br /> <br /> With that in mind. They may shelve m5 depending on w5 sales but continue low effort stuff from v5 and farming out the brand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-08T02:41:07-08:00","id":1555229,"title":"","content":"Paradox is a publicly traded company. They have shareholders to keep happy. While shareholders with enough stake to have meaningful impact regarding board votes are not paragons of unflawed assessments either, Bloodlines 2 is supposed to be the game that proves all the money (and time that money wasn't making more money as investors put it there to do) that shows the WoD brand is valuable to the Paradox portfolio instead of something to sell off to recoup as much as they can. The board has a fiduciary duty to the shareholders, and can't waste their money on the WoD just because the current CEO is an old VtM fan. At some point Paradox is going to have to make a sound economic argument to keep the WoD, or they're going to be pressured into selling it to someone else; and likely someone even less interested in the TTRPG side of things given the state of the video game industry right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-08T04:29:21-08:00","id":1555231,"title":"","content":"<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I tend to agree that the World of Darkness brand has been significantly diminished. Not only through Bloodlines' long and messy development, but also through years of inconsistent messaging and missed opportunities. What once carried a strong identity (dark, edgy, angst or mature and narratively ambitious) has been diluted into something that feels hesitant and risk averse.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I think we all agree that the problem is not that the IP lacks potential. It is that Paradox never found a coherent strategy for how to use it. They tried to fit the WoD into their existing publishing logic (small-scale AA projects, safe returns, outsourcing creative risk), but the setting demands something more unified and deliberate. Right now, it\u2019s stuck between prestige narrative ambitions and low-cost exploitation of brand nostalgia (which I would actually prefer, if they can not find something cool to do).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If Paradox wants to salvage what is left of the brand, I see a few possible paths:</span></span><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sell or license the IP to a partner that actually wants to develop it long-term. (Oh hi </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">onyxpath, what are you doing here at this time of the night?)</span></span> S<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">omeone that knows the IP and understands the fanbase better. Someone with the creative will to make WoD a modern gothic IP. <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If Paradox wants to mix stuff up I would think of Focus Entertainment (warhammer 40k Space marine 2) or even CDPR (witcher/cyberpunk) if they weren\u2019t already busy. It is better to have a smaller slice of a thriving brand than total control of a stagnant one.</span></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Reboot the WoD as a transmedia franchise again, but with clearer creative oversight.<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Let Bloodlines 2 mark the end of this chapter. Then start over with an integrated approach: align TTRPG, video games, and maybe even narrative media (Books, comics, etc.) under a single creative direction. Something like what Games Workshop finally learned to do with Warhammer after decades of chaos.</span></span></span></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Refocus on the TTRPG side and use it to rebuild trust.<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If they do not want to spend AAA money, they could still make WoD relevant by reinvesting in the tabletop ecosystem. New systems, digital tools, or narrative supplements that rebuild the fanbase's faith before touching big games again.</span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Oh a wild onyx path appears\u2026 again.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Go \u201cboutique\u201d. Treat WoD like a Paradox \u201csmall indie\u201d approach.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Smaller but high-quality but focussed narrative projects on kickstarter/backkit with expensive premium dice, books etc</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Or just mix between the points above.</span></span></li> </ol><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">To me, it is not about how much the WoD costs Paradox. It is about whether it still fits their identity. If they can not nurture it properly, the best move might be to pass the torch before the brand erodes any further. aight, i tried to find all the gramar mistakes as well as spelling. Everyone that find a mistake can keep it.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is me, just forgot my PW and changed my email<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25163-crytash2","name":"Crytash2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25163_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-08T04:58:30-08:00","id":1555233,"title":"","content":"A big problem, from both a consumer and investment perspective, is that every option but 1 relies on a path with no clear ways from A to Z. Rebooting, refocusing, or restructuring will need some major evidence that anyone should believe in the change when it's going to be the same CEO and likely many of the same internal Paradox staff working on the brand. It's easy to say, &quot;Oh, just thread this very thin needle with that very thick thread a dozen times in a row perfectly,&quot; but realistically counting on doing it isn't easy at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-08T05:09:35-08:00","id":1555234,"title":"","content":"One thing I forgot to add about the analysis from the Swedish bank is that they worry about the future outlook for Paradox is that aside from their core grand-strategy games their future release-schedule is a bit light. And that makes me wonder how happy the shareholders will be if Paradox-leadership really sticks with this &quot;Bloodlines 2 is a dead end&quot;-sentiment that essentially translates to &quot;Making anything aside from grand strategy games is too hard and not worth it.&quot;. That isn't an exactly optimistic premise for a videogame-company's outlook. And while these grand strategy games are popular and make a profit, they're also just a tiny niche on the videogame-market. The whole point of Paradox as a publisher in the last couple of years was to expand and publish games in a lot of other genres as well. Acquiring the WOD-license was part of that. So, to now go back to &quot;Let's just focus on grand strategy games&quot; has a whiff of &quot;We're back to square one.&quot;. And like with Bloodlines 2, saying things like &quot;Making RPGs after the release of Baldurs Gate 3 is too hard.&quot; is a poor excuse for mismanaging the WOD-license. <br /> <br /> But also hilariously, these Swedish analysts note Prison Architect 2 as the big 2026 release aside from their typical DLC releases for the grand strategy games. It's hilarious because the last update stated the game was delayed indefinitely. Maybe they know something as shareholders that the public doesn't but hey, maybe they're right. Maybe the game will come out next year...<br /> <br /> Notably, Prison Architect 2's development history will sound very familiar in the context of Bloodlines 2. Here's a summary of its development-history from <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prison_Architect_2\" target=\"_blank\">Wikipedia</a>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The game was revealed in January 2024 by Paradox Interactive, who acquired the title from Introversion Software in 2019. The game was initially developed by Double Eleven, who took over the developing duty of the first installment after the acquisition. However, a change in development studio was announced by Paradox Interactive on 13 May 2024, as Paradox Interactive and Double Eleven were unable to reach a commercial agreement. Kokku, who had been working alongside Double Eleven since mid 2023, were to take over development of the title.<br /> <br /> Initially slated for release on 26 March 2024, the game was announced with a delay to 7 May 2024 in order to &quot;fix more bugs and further optimize the game for all platforms&quot;. It was then further delayed to 3 September 2024 as the team encountered &quot;new technical challenges&quot;. On 2 August 2024, the game was delayed indefinitely in the aim to improve the game's performance and quality. </div> </div> </div>But it's been odd that since last year, it hasn't exactly felt like there's a change of direction in what they publish. Rather, it seems they're just focusing on releasing what was already on the release-schedule anyway without putting anything new on it. Their release-schedule really is quite light compared to a few years ago. Then again, when you look at the whole set of releases of the last couple of years who knows how much money they've burned on all these excursions into other genres that didn't pan out as they hoped or turned out to be outright disasters. But you get this sense of unease in how the analysts talk about Paradox. As shareholders, the obvious demand is simply &quot;Make line go up.&quot; but how is this supposed to happen when Paradox barely publishes any games in the upcoming years? At some point, Paradox really needs to deal with why they were unable to take the profits from their grand strategy games and expand like they planned. And the lack of success of the WOD-license is part of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-08T06:49:23-08:00","id":1555236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555233#post1555233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A big problem, from both a consumer and investment perspective, is that every option but 1 relies on a path with no clear ways from A to Z. Rebooting, refocusing, or restructuring will need some major evidence that anyone should believe in the change when it's going to be the same CEO and likely many of the same internal Paradox staff working on the brand. It's easy to say, &quot;Oh, just thread this very thin needle with that very thick thread a dozen times in a row perfectly,&quot; but realistically counting on doing it isn't easy at all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">True, but that is kind of the nature of the beast, isn't it? Investment is always risky. Nobody is going to get guaranteed returns on any creative brand similar to WoD, especially after years of mixed direction.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If Paradox decides to just sit on the IP and do nothing, there are short-term advantages: less financial risk, no more bad headlines, and shareholders stay calm because no new money is being burned. But long-term it is a slow bleed is it not? The brand loses relevance, the existing audience drifts away, and when they finally decide to do something again, they will be starting from zero instead of from a wounded but still-known name. </span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is me, just forgot my PW and changed my email<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25163-crytash2","name":"Crytash2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25163_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-08T06:59:32-08:00","id":1555237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555234#post1555234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The whole point of Paradox as a publisher in the last couple of years was to expand and publish games in a lot of other genres as well. Acquiring the WOD-license was part of that. So, to now go back to &quot;Let's just focus on grand strategy games&quot; has a whiff of &quot;We're back to square one.&quot;. And like with Bloodlines 2, saying things like &quot;Making RPGs after the release of Baldurs Gate 3 is too hard.&quot; is a poor excuse for mismanaging the WOD-license.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did not even see that before. That is an assanine statement. There are tons of RPGs going again, if you can not make it work this is on you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is me, just forgot my PW and changed my email<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25163-crytash2","name":"Crytash2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25163_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-08T08:44:08-08:00","id":1555242,"title":"","content":"I would like to think the numbers are misleading and that we're going to get a lot of better news come the next quarter but I'm not optimistic. We knew that the first studio, HSL, having the project shut down followed by the Hail Mary pass of Chinese Room was going to have a lot of expenses. Unfortunately, I don't see this game necessarily making a dramatic turnaround due to the massive negativity its had to struggle with despite the people pushing back against it. The preorders are all counted on that $14,000,000 and that was always going to be a massive chunk of the purchasing power.<br /> <br /> It's a grim figure and probably means the death of the V:TM license for anything resembling a &quot;proper&quot; video game, let alone Bloodlines 3. No one will touch it with the kind of budget this game got.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-08T13:57:07-08:00","id":1555246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crytash2</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555236#post1555236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, but that is kind of the nature of the beast, isn't it? Investment is always risky.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but this isn't a binary. Risk is something that gets evaluated in many ways and to many degrees.<br /> <br /> To go back to a tangent from one of the other threads about BL2: the idea of &quot;AAA&quot; &quot;AA&quot; and &quot;A&quot; video game studios? That's something that comes from investment lingo. Back in the brick &amp; mortar days were retailers had to decide what games they were going to stock and in what quantities, an informal rating system the mirrored investment ratings came about. AAA studios were ones where you carried even their experimental games that weren't existing IP/etc. because the studios had proven track records. Customers that might be iffy on a title could see &quot;Capcom&quot; or &quot;Rare&quot; on the package and that could shift their hesitancy into a sale because that used to be trustworthy enough.<br /> <br /> Just like customers have every right to be suspicious of a Paradox game that's not a grand strategy game (given their past few years) and avoid/wait for it to be one sale/etc., investors are going to get skittish around the risks after Paradox has burnt this much money on an IP with potential. You can't just tell either group, &quot;OK, I know we did bad the last few years, but trust us that we've completely learned the lesson, so give us more money and you'll totally get the games and profits everyone wants to see!&quot; It's one thing to take a risk before you've seen what Paradox will do with a Bloodlines game, and another after.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If Paradox decides to just sit on the IP and do nothing, there are short-term advantages: less financial risk, no more bad headlines, and shareholders stay calm because no new money is being burned. But long-term it is a slow bleed is it not? The brand loses relevance, the existing audience drifts away, and when they finally decide to do something again, they will be starting from zero instead of from a wounded but still-known name. </div> </div> </div>Correct. That's why in these cases the shareholders generally are going to push for a sale of the IP. Let it become someone else's problems and minimize the loses rather than wait years and spend lots of money (not just bleed money, fixing things is going to cost too) for a potential payout in... 10, 15, 20 years? The buyer is in a better position because they'll have their own track record to sell people on why they're going to do the IP right, and the price is already going to be about as good as it's realistically going to get (the brand irrelevance hurts it's potential to sell to someone else too). <br /> <br /> Keep in mind that &quot;buyer&quot; here doesn't have to be some completely different organization. Onyx Path bought Trinity and Scion when CCP was selling off the WW IPs, and Onyx Path started as a group of CCP employees looking as a company about to eliminate their jobs (as had just happened to many of their friends) as CCP decided to get out of the physical games side of things. Why this worked though, is because Onyx Path was started by Rich and co. who had positive fan and industry reputations. Nobody thought CCP's decisions were because the people that CCP hired while taking over WW were messing things up, so those same people could have the trust to do right by the IPs after spinning off a new company.<br /> <br /> Paradox could back a spinoff like Onyx Path, but the would need to be really careful about who might go to it from Paradox so the broken trust people have in Paradox's handling of the IP doesn't get carried into the spinoff company.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-08T14:08:31-08:00","id":1555248,"title":"","content":"I definitely understand why OPP made Curseborne to have intellectual freedom and financial security over it. They also presumably had plenty of ideas they could never implement within the existing frameworks.<br /> <br /> Maybe in ten years, we'll have the Curseborne video game RPG.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-08T15:22:52-08:00","id":1555250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crytash2</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555236#post1555236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">True, but that is kind of the nature of the beast, isn't it?</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>No, it isn't.<br /> <br /> Investment is about assessment of risks and likely returns. Going blind is gambling, and gamblers always lose in the end.<br /> <br /> Also, investment strategy is one thing, company strategy is another. They're tightly related, but not the same. The company has to have an actual strategy to get enough money in enough time as to pay its numerous bills, and then enough extra to appease stakeholders (in this case, mainly shareholders).<br /> <br /> Paradox just burned a shitton of money in <i>Bloodlines 2</i> to release it more to mitigate losses than make an actual profit. Who they blame on their problems doesn't really change that they can't make proper money out of this type of game.<br /> <br /> So yes, <i>Bloodlines 2</i> is <b>definitely</b> a dead-end. This has been the case with their every single foray into other genres and there's no reason to think otherwise, whatever the cause.<br /> <br /> Other common mistake is to think all those things have a lot to do with the TTRPG side of things, it doesn't. The RPG has meaningless costs and profit margins for them, by itself it's just to keep the IP relevant, and it does the job well enough as is, there's zero reason for them to invest more attention on that side of the business.<br /> <br /> They'll certainly close the <i>Bloodlines</i> avenue as something to put their money in, but they can still get something out of the IP depending on business strategy, but that's not about making a better game either TT or Video. They want to keep at the licensing strategy as long as they have the IP, so we'll depend exclusively from now on other people wanting to do something and pay Paradox a share of the profits (at margins they previously didn't knew how to negotiate, either).<br /> <br /> Will that pay enough to justify not selling the IP? Maybe. But shareholders will certainly want to know how much they can get selling it. If something may keep the IP in Paradox's hands it is a lack of buyers with deep enough pockets to pay the price they have to sell at. And I very much doubt Onyx Path will be that party, because Paradox spent quite some buck on it.<br /> <br /> For M5, the prospects aren't terrible. Unless Paradox is expecting selling the IP soon, there is no reason to not keep investing the small money a TTRPG needs and get <i>some</i> profit out of it instead of none. <i><b>Any</b></i> profit, whatsoever, is better than none (although marketing costs may be prohibitive at this point). It all depends, but they have a few avenues for changing gears that still have TTRPG books getting out. And yes, others that has it slow or stop altogether.<br /> <br /> My opinion is that they should make a Grand Strategy game with the IP. It is their strong suit, after all. And about not being able to do anything else, while it lessens their value a little it isn't a big problem. Doing what you know how to reliably make money with is far more important than being willing to do anything with random results. There's a problem with market risk, but they have to do with the tools they have, and investors can deal with this kind of risk in other ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-08T15:53:50-08:00","id":1555251,"title":"","content":"There already is another video game coming in <i>Heartless Symphony </i>in 2026.<br /> <br /> The demo-predecessor game is already available.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://store.steampowered.com/app/1926120/Vampire_The_Masquerade__Heartless_Lullaby/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://store.steampowered.com/app/1926120/Vampire_The_Masquerade__Heartless_Lullaby/\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://store.steampowered.com/app/1926120/Vampire_The_Masquerade__Heartless_Lullaby/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://store.steampowered.com/app/1926120/Vampire_The_Masquerade__Heartless_Lullaby/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So it's not going anywhere. Bloodlines II may have been a loss, though I'd love for it to rebound, but they made money on the visual novels and Swansong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-08T16:09:23-08:00","id":1555252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555251#post1555251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There already is another video game coming in <i>Heartless Symphony </i>in 2026.<br /> <br /> The demo-predecessor game is already available.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://store.steampowered.com/app/1926120/Vampire_The_Masquerade__Heartless_Lullaby/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://store.steampowered.com/app/1926120/Vampire_The_Masquerade__Heartless_Lullaby/\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://store.steampowered.com/app/1926120/Vampire_The_Masquerade__Heartless_Lullaby/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://store.steampowered.com/app/1926120/Vampire_The_Masquerade__Heartless_Lullaby/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So it's not going anywhere. Bloodlines II may have been a loss, though I'd love for it to rebound, but they made money on the visual novels and Swansong.</div> </div> </div> </div>There hasn't been any news on this &quot;Heartless Symphony&quot; project for three years now. And Heartless Lullaby was the first and only release that came from that studio. Who even knows what's going on over there...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-08T19:11:34-08:00","id":1555257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555251#post1555251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There already is another video game coming in <i>Heartless Symphony </i>in 2026.<br /> <br /> The demo-predecessor game is already available.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://store.steampowered.com/app/1926120/Vampire_The_Masquerade__Heartless_Lullaby/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://store.steampowered.com/app/1926120/Vampire_The_Masquerade__Heartless_Lullaby/\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://store.steampowered.com/app/1926120/Vampire_The_Masquerade__Heartless_Lullaby/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://store.steampowered.com/app/1926120/Vampire_The_Masquerade__Heartless_Lullaby/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So it's not going anywhere. Bloodlines II may have been a loss, though I'd love for it to rebound, but they made money on the visual novels and Swansong.</div> </div> </div> </div>This actually means nothing.<br /> <br /> Paradox works mostly through licensing anyway, and they have to honor any licensing contract already signed.<br /> <br /> So this only means someone was already working on a game and that's it. It has nothing to do with Paradox and their next decisions.<br /> <br /> Also, <i>how much</i> did they made with those other games? That matters, <i>a lot</i>. They have to cover the costs of keeping the IP and the whole TTRPG machine going, they have now to cover maybe 40 million USD in net loss from the <i>Bloodlines 2</i> project, and most importantly, they have to justify <i>not using this money elsewhere</i>.<br /> <br /> Licensing the IP for indie games is all nice and fun, but doesn't necessarily means things are okay, that's not how publicly traded companies work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-09T03:30:48-08:00","id":1555263,"title":"","content":"On reflection this whole thing feels like an example of the downsides of capitalism were the quality of the products are secondary to abstract long term plans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-09T04:51:39-08:00","id":1555265,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure that's really the case...<br /> <br /> Paradox bought the WoD IPs a decade ago. They threw a lot of money at it, and seemed like for the most part they let the creative teams take the wheel over investor driven short term thinking.<br /> <br /> The problem is that in any economic system, there has to be some sort of feedback system to ensure people aren't getting caught in a sunk-cost fallacy and keep putting resources into a project that's draining more than it can hope to add.<br /> <br /> Too a large extent Paradox is suffering the results of never really enacting an abstract or concrete long term plan for the WoD. Without that plan, product quality has been all over the place (at best) as there isn't a strong coherent creative vision at the helm of all of this leading the products being disjointed. Success has been nearly impossible to capitalize on because what was successful isn't being carried into how future products are made, while failures have racked up and driven potential audiences away. That plan is, basically, necessary to ensure that product quality in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-09T12:32:47-08:00","id":1555279,"title":"","content":"I be honest, after Bloodlines 2 I got Tattered Facade. Its a whatever book but the fact that turned Baali into completely different thing with only like 3 pages basically made me remember why I stopped their products.<br /> <br /> At the start V5 was acceptable, if only because I can just ignore baffling lore bits and modify the system I don't like. It was a continuation after all. <br /> H5 sucked. Between the fact that it doesn't deserve the Reckoning title, stupid stuff like jobbers and org hate, underwhelming Edges, it was a wash from the start.<br /> W5 is...W5, with its own brand of problems. Half the things that made WTA unique and charming removed, strawman Albrech, the whole Get of Fenris shenanigans, goldfish memory of Garou and even things like particular loresheets, looking at you Chinese astronaut who first changed during a mission inside a rocket and all the problems with it.<br /> <br /> At this point I just want this edition to be over and not just because I don't want them to touch other splats. It has been nearly a decade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-09T13:05:31-08:00","id":1555282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555263#post1555263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On reflection this whole thing feels like an example of the downsides of capitalism were the quality of the products are secondary to abstract long term plans.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I definitely understand the sentiment, that's not the case here.<br /> <br /> In addition to everything <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> said, Paradox is simply making a very bad job at diversifying their products and are reaping the consequences. Those certainly take a capitalist flair to them, but something would happen one way or another.<br /> <br /> There's no mincing words here, they simply don't know how to do things. They know how to make their particular brand of game and that's it. Their success is more the result of being good at the right task at the right time than knowing how to manage anything of their current size or doing anything at all besides their strategy games.<br /> <br /> V5 is actually a love project that could have been so much better, because it was given mostly free reign and far more money that it needed, really.<br /> <br /> But capitalism or not, you need to know how to manage things. You have to set realistic goals and assess your situation regularly. You have to study how things actually work when you try to do something new. You have to allocate resources with a minimum of logic. You have to know when to pull out of a failed experiment. You have to adjust and learn from mistakes and successes. And they failed at all those things.<br /> <br /> Capitalism is at fault when you have a good thing going on, on good hands, but those things derail because quality doesn't equate profits, and that's certainly a thing that happens a lot. But in this case it's was something good being delivered into incompetent hands 10 years ago, and that happens at any economic system. All the problems that ensued are 100% Paradox's fault for being fools, not because capitalism (quite the opposite, as their money actually sheltered the IP for 10 years from the consequences of bad management).<br /> <br /> And that sheltering may still happen. As I said before, TTRPGs are small change for a company their size. What happened now is that <i>Bloodlines 2</i> <u><b>is not</b></u> a TTRPG and brought a whole 'nother level of loss, so this sheltering is at risk, but they may be able to still hold to it if they can argue that keeping things at a lower profile (i.e. TTRPGs and licensing without compromise) is a safer deal than trying to sell it for a loss (which is exactly what will happen if they sell it now). They can still convince shareholders that if they don't waste that kind of money again, WoD5 is too little a thing compared to their margins. That just became a harder sell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":".  Removing extraneous content 11-09-2025, 07:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-09T15:44:46-08:00","id":1555292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Technoma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555279#post1555279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I be honest, after Bloodlines 2 I got Tattered Facade. Its a whatever book but the fact that turned Baali into completely different thing with only like 3 pages basically made me remember why I stopped their products.<br /> <br /> At the start V5 was acceptable, if only because I can just ignore baffling lore bits and modify the system I don't like. It was a continuation after all.<br /> H5 sucked. Between the fact that it doesn't deserve the Reckoning title, stupid stuff like jobbers and org hate, underwhelming Edges, it was a wash from the start.<br /> W5 is...W5, with its own brand of problems. Half the things that made WTA unique and charming removed, strawman Albrech, the whole Get of Fenris shenanigans, goldfish memory of Garou and even things like particular loresheets, looking at you Chinese astronaut who first changed during a mission inside a rocket and all the problems with it.<br /> <br /> At this point I just want this edition to be over and not just because I don't want them to touch other splats. It has been nearly a decade.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did they change Albrech from not existing in 5th Edition? I thought he was now just a name of a lineage.<br /> <br /> I couldn't really follow the changes after the book. Getting rid of the kinfolk and Garou born made it incompatible with the previous lines to the point I didn't follow new books.<br /> <br /> (I have the books now because of the bundle but haven't read them yet)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-09T16:05:01-08:00","id":1555295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555292#post1555292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did they change Albrech from not existing in 5th Edition? I thought he was now just a name of a lineage.<br /> <br /> I couldn't really follow the changes after the book. Getting rid of the kinfolk and Garou born made it incompatible with the previous lines to the point I didn't follow new books.<br /> <br /> (I have the books now because of the bundle but haven't read them yet)</div> </div> </div> </div>They have Albrech, they even give quotes from him. But he is so different from the previous editons Albrech that he might as well be an imposter doppelganger. <br /> Which might make sense as a headcanon, considering they braindamaged Garou to the point they consider 1980s to be ancient history with no clear record. Maybe no one noticed Albrech getting replaced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-09T16:29:09-08:00","id":1555298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555292#post1555292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did they change Albrech from not existing in 5th Edition? I thought he was now just a name of a lineage.<br /> <br /> I couldn't really follow the changes after the book. Getting rid of the kinfolk and Garou born made it incompatible with the previous lines to the point I didn't follow new books.<br /> <br /> (I have the books now because of the bundle but haven't read them yet)</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole thing is a new game, period, no relation to the old WtA at all.<br /> <br /> So there is <i>a</i> Albretch, who's just a sad old excuse of a leader that was there when everything went down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-09T16:34:18-08:00","id":1555299,"title":"","content":"My take on the subject is that the video game department is working at the expense of the tabletop game but it really isn't Paradox's FAULT despite disagreements fans may have. Hasbo showed that Dungeons and Dragons is entirely viable as a brand on its own (it's the only thing making profit for them) but the tabletop game of V:TM doesn't draw in that kind of name recognition or market share. I think that Paradox Interactive for all the criticism they take for 5th Edition did a good job of getting Vampire: The Masquerade and other World of Darkness products back in stores. They also were willing to license out the books to get all of the original fiction reprinted as well as audiobooks (there's 20 of the latter now)<br /> <br /> Do I think OPP is the better artistically? Yes, I do. I've been all over the Chicago by Night and Cults of the Blood Gods as well as the other supplements. I am a big lore addict and the decision to try to move away from the first four editions was not one I supported (and still don't). It's like buying the new Planescape supplement and finding out Faction War is just...not acknowledged. Same with Ravenloft and all the retcons. It shouldn't bother me they just retcon it all away but like an annoying comic book junkie, it does.<br /> <br /> HOWEVER, I don't actually think they badly handled reintroducing the IP to a whole new generation fans (a literal generation). The visual novels, Swansong, Earthblood, and the text games are all pretty fun plus they have made the product available internationally.<br /> <br /> Marketing wise, I give Paradox good points.<br /> <br /> BUT Bloodlines 2's development was a massive financial problem and I don't blame them for it. It was meant to be the crown jewel and whatever happened with Hardsuit Labs meant that fans got furious over the release and there wasn't really anything they could do about it. Paradox pulled the plug and Chinese Room saved the game but it was never going to go over well with the delays and change of genre. It was a problem outside of their control.<br /> <br /> I don't really know what they could have done with the amount of money on the line, especially when it was Hardsuit Labs who got rid of Brian Mitsoda.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-09-2025, 09:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-10T03:11:18-08:00","id":1555309,"title":"","content":"At the end of the day, the real value of the WOD-IP is in its ability to make videogames with it. Because no matter how successful the books might end up being, the money you're gonna make selling those will be peanuts compared to a successful videogame-release. And since Paradox is primarily a videogame-company anyway, I would assume focusing on videogames was always the goal. And that's why they wanted to start with the flashy idea of making a sequel to the cult-classic Bloodlines.<br /> <br /> But I think the way this then unfolded led to another leadership-failure by Paradox. Let's say it breaks down 50/50. They spent 30 million dollars on the Hardsuit Labs version and 30 million on the Chinese Room version. In reality, it probably breaks down differently and the 60 milion is also just an estimate from bank analysts anyway but for the sake of argument, let's go with that. During the entire time, they've been rolling out WOD-games, I'm sure it must have influenced Paradox's decisions that they were always thinking &quot;We spent 30 million on Bloodlines 2 - and we have nothing to show for it.&quot;. And I feel like that's why these WOD-games rarely went into AA-territory like Swansong or Earthblood and instead, it just has been mostly visual novels and text-adventures. You never got any really big releases that made a splash. And it didn't help, of course, any time someone wrote about a new WOD-videogame the &quot;Remember Bloodlines 2? What a mess...&quot;-talk came up - which put a bit of a damper on the whole affair. So I don't think that approach ended up helping the WOD-brand get more recognition. <br /> <br /> The WOD-videogame-lineup has been sitting this entire time in the shadow of Bloodline 2's development-hell-fiasco and now Bloodlines 2 has finally come out - just in time for Paradox to lose any interest in producing a WOD-videogame-lineup, it feels like. Originally, Bloodlines 2 was supposed to be the flagship-game that showed off the potential of the WOD-IP. But the way in which it was released now was more about Paradox getting a burden off their chest rather than being a signal for any greater plans. They've finally done it, they've released Bloodlines 2 and there's seemingly no interest to capitalize on that. Which just feels like yet another poor management-decision by Paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-10T09:56:02-08:00","id":1555318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555309#post1555309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the end of the day, the real value of the WOD-IP is in its ability to make videogames with it. Because no matter how successful the books might end up being, the money you're gonna make selling those will be peanuts compared to a successful videogame-release. And since Paradox is primarily a videogame-company anyway, I would assume focusing on videogames was always the goal. And that's why they wanted to start with the flashy idea of making a sequel to the cult-classic Bloodlines.<br /> <br /> But I think the way this then unfolded led to another leadership-failure by Paradox. Let's say it breaks down 50/50. They spent 30 million dollars on the Hardsuit Labs version and 30 million on the Chinese Room version. In reality, it probably breaks down differently and the 60 milion is also just an estimate from bank analysts anyway but for the sake of argument, let's go with that. During the entire time, they've been rolling out WOD-games, I'm sure it must have influenced Paradox's decisions that they were always thinking &quot;We spent 30 million on Bloodlines 2 - and we have nothing to show for it.&quot;. And I feel like that's why these WOD-games rarely went into AA-territory like Swansong or Earthblood and instead, it just has been mostly visual novels and text-adventures. You never got any really big releases that made a splash. And it didn't help, of course, any time someone wrote about a new WOD-videogame the &quot;Remember Bloodlines 2? What a mess...&quot;-talk came up - which put a bit of a damper on the whole affair. So I don't think that approach ended up helping the WOD-brand get more recognition.<br /> <br /> The WOD-videogame-lineup has been sitting this entire time in the shadow of Bloodline 2's development-hell-fiasco and now Bloodlines 2 has finally come out - just in time for Paradox to lose any interest in producing a WOD-videogame-lineup, it feels like. Originally, Bloodlines 2 was supposed to be the flagship-game that showed off the potential of the WOD-IP. But the way in which it was released now was more about Paradox getting a burden off their chest rather than being a signal for any greater plans. They've finally done it, they've released Bloodlines 2 and there's seemingly no interest to capitalize on that. Which just feels like yet another poor management-decision by Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>Essentially, it's the Scylla and Charybdis argument that I don't really give Paradox much crap for either and really I DONT want to give them huge credit but they're really not people I blame for this. Bloodlines 2 is the definition of a Broken Base game. The steam rankings have been on the lower end of things and a lot of the discussion of the game more or less goes, &quot;it's a good but flawed game&quot; when its positive but a huge chunk of other discussion is, &quot;It's not like Bloodlines 1 and thus sucks.&quot; People even commented on my review of the game being unusually negative and I had fun.<br /> <br /> Which is an elaborate way of saying that the game feels unpolished but they'd already delayed it as literally as much as humanly possible, giving the Chinese Room another year to get everything fixed when it was announced alongside Cyberpunk 2077.<br /> <br /> They could either release the product and get all the criticism it has gotten or not release it and continue pouring money into it with no guarantee it will be make any of that back. I have hopes for the game that it will continue to get tweaked by The Chinese Room over the course of the next year but I can understand why they consider White Wolf's brand not another thing to try to risk a big budget game on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-10T11:03:29-08:00","id":1555323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555299#post1555299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My take on the subject is that the video game department is working at the expense of the tabletop game but it really isn't Paradox's FAULT despite disagreements fans may have.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand why you're so unwilling to credit a company with the responsibility for the consequences of their decisions.<br /> <br /> Paradox literally decides what they do with the brand and who gets to do what.<br /> <br /> Companies need strategy and have the resources and obligation to do research. They are not individual artists.<br /> <br /> Sometimes you seem to ot understand that there's a huge difference between the work of an individual or small group and the work of a big company. And it isn't <i>only</i> a matter of how much money they have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555299#post1555299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hasbo showed that Dungeons and Dragons is entirely viable as a brand on its own (it's the only thing making profit for them)</div> </div> </div> </div>Small correction: while D&amp;D is currently considered the <i>main</i> thing making profit for them, it is still at best 1/9 of their profit margins, and probably less than 1/10. Hasbro, just like Paradox, has a lot more going on for them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555299#post1555299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but the tabletop game of V:TM doesn't draw in that kind of name recognition or market share.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't disentangle the results from the strategies. Hasbro and Paradox have completely different takes on those IPs.<br /> <br /> Paradox bought WoD hopping for licensees to show up spontaneously, and otherwise just did the TTRPG (with excessive oversight). Even marketing only became strong later on, trying to copy what Hasbro was doing with <i>Critical Role</i> and similar content. And their oversight over VtM was meant to make the game they wanted to play, not the game others wanted to play.<br /> <br /> Hasbro invested heavily in marketing from the get-go and in research for the best approach to develop the TTRPG, with an extremely solid core, since they wouldn't follow the previous approach of making a lot of books. They also built themselves a whole ecosystem of products around it, so they would have something to sell even if no one wanted the license.<br /> <br /> Even then D&amp;D 5e didn't became a success from the get go. Certainly it had a strong buy-in in the TTRPG community, but for the Nth time this is peanuts for those companies, TTRPGs don't make a lot of money. It took years for D&amp;D to really become the industry on itself it is today.<br /> <br /> What happened was that Hasbro had both a short term and a long term strategy. It was self-sufficient for the time they needed to show D&amp;D could do more. And even then it was after years of experience with the IP, they own D&amp;D since 1999, and through the acquisition of a company that had it since 1997, and on their part just bought the original company, so we have a direct, uninterrupted line of developers since the game was invented.<br /> <br /> Paradox followed a flawed strategy in which they expected fast returns and automatic recognition. They barely thought at first that they would need <i>Bloodlines 2</i> to show it was feasible to make big games. I was watching this side because I had at the time a project for a game and wanted the license, so I was following their take on this process, and I can say it had a lot of problems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555299#post1555299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that Paradox Interactive for all the criticism they take for 5th Edition did a good job of getting Vampire: The Masquerade and other World of Darkness products back in stores. They also were willing to license out the books to get all of the original fiction reprinted as well as audiobooks (there's 20 of the latter now)</div> </div> </div> </div>That they did, it just doesn't means a good job handling the IP overall, it's just one aspect among many.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555299#post1555299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do I think OPP is the better artistically? Yes, I do.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's not the point of the thread. The artistic choices are only tangentially related to the problems discussed here.<br /> <br /> Even if they did everything &quot;right&quot; with the setting, that was not the part that caused this mess.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555299#post1555299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">HOWEVER, I don't actually think they badly handled reintroducing the IP to a whole new generation fans (a literal generation). The visual novels, Swansong, Earthblood, and the text games are all pretty fun plus they have made the product available internationally.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it must be pointed out that they're not responsible for any of those games, Not a single one.<br /> <br /> Those are simple licenses by their basic contract, the people who made those games bought the right to make the games and that was most (not all, but most) of the participation of Paradox. They didn't put money in them, they didn't look for those people or were very selective, they just had a booklet with instructions on what you can or can't do with the setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555299#post1555299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Marketing wise, I give Paradox good points.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was good from a certain point, not from the beginning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555299#post1555299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BUT Bloodlines 2's development was a massive financial problem and I don't blame them for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you don't blame a big company for the very thing that's their entire responsibility.<br /> <br /> Calculating costs, risks and when to give up are the most fundamental decisions of a business.<br /> <br /> Seriously, I'm talking like a professional of finances now, there are situations when the company isn't at fault for their expenses in failed projects, but this is not one of those.<br /> <br /> Every single penny (or rather \u00f6ren) spent in this project was their direct decision, and knowing the risks was their basic obligation.<br /> <br /> All the things that happened are within the ballpark of risks they should have assessed and have a back-up plan for. Not that problems wouldn't arise, but it shouldn't have cost that much.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555299#post1555299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was meant to be the crown jewel and whatever happened with Hardsuit Labs meant that fans got furious over the release and there wasn't really anything they could do about it. Paradox pulled the plug and Chinese Room saved the game but it was never going to go over well with the delays and change of genre. It was a problem outside of their control.</div> </div> </div> </div>To a degree, yes, but not completely.<br /> <br /> Actually there were lots of things they could do, from better communication with the fans, pulling the plug earlier, renaming the game when it changed hands, there was a lot. Even if development problems were solely on HL (which isn't likely), managing the results was completely on Paradox and whatever they did or not.<br /> <br /> Paradox chose to keep the project going at any cost and hype it as most as they could as a proper sequel to <i>Bloodlines</i>. It is on them if the fans got furious.<br /> <br /> One of the big problems is that this crown jewel was left entirely for someone else to do, with Paradox just throwing money at it and hopping for the better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555299#post1555299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really know what they could have done with the amount of money on the line, especially when it was Hardsuit Labs who got rid of Brian Mitsoda.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was also Hardsuit Labs who hired Mitsoda, as far as that has anything to do with anything, which we simply don't know. And Paradox could have chimed in if it was that important.<br /> <br /> And it was Paradox who put this money on the line in the first place. As a company, if they did it and it didn't pay out, it's on them.<br /> <br /> Sixty million dollars in a single project for a company with an annual profit on the ballpark of 150 million is hard to swallow as anything but a bad decision. Although it certainly explains why the so desperately thought they had to price the game as an AAA game.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555309#post1555309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I feel like that's why these WOD-games rarely went into AA-territory like Swansong or Earthblood and instead, it just has been mostly visual novels and text-adventures. You never got any really big releases that made a splash.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the reason for this, and it's also a blunder from their part, is that they actually didn't made anything.<br /> <br /> Paradox relied exclusively in their standard licensing agreement and attached documents. Everything else was just people reaching to them wanting to buy the contract. Paradox didn't had the ideas, the projects, nothing, neither did it put any money on the games, unless their agreement changed for the latest games.<br /> <br /> From the beginning they were hopping for someone else to decide on their own that they wanted to make a game with the WoD IP, and then Paradox would be there with the license in hand and a fast licensing process.<br /> <br /> It failed, and in no small part because Paradox itself didn't do nothing at all besides TTRPGs that aren't even their core business.<br /> <br /> Even <i>Bloodlines 2</i> was born out of HL's initiative, although it was the single project Paradox would actually pay for.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-10T14:17:53-08:00","id":1555331,"title":"","content":"It seems worth bringing up that when Hardsuit Labs came on to do Bloodlines 2, Paradox also bought 1/3 of the shares of the company. Unlike many of the independent studios that have worked on WoD games via Paradox licenses, Paradox put a large financial stake into HL. Everything HL did on BL2 after that purchase cannot be pawned off as a license partner just making mistakes Paradox had no say in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-10T14:32:51-08:00","id":1555332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555331#post1555331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems worth bringing up that when Hardsuit Labs came on to do Bloodlines 2, Paradox also bought 1/3 of the shares of the company. Unlike many of the independent studios that have worked on WoD games via Paradox licenses, Paradox put a large financial stake into HL. Everything HL did on BL2 after that purchase cannot be pawned off as a license partner just making mistakes Paradox had no say in.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was always in my argument but as the reverse. Paradox gave a HUGGGGGGE amount of support to the game out of belief in what was being promised and their losses were MUCH larger when it was discovered that HSL was nowhere near releasing a finished product.<br /> <br /> Also, had fired Mitsoda and Avellone, which while you can argue the reasons for certainly crippled the game's writing credibility.<br /> <br /> If they hadn't bought such a massive share then Paradox might not have taken such a bath on the results. <br /> <br /> We don't know what happened but Paradox, with its history of releasing somewhat janky games, decided to take out the game to the back of the barn to shoot rather than release it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-10T16:25:46-08:00","id":1555339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555332#post1555332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was always in my argument but as the reverse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which makes no sense.<br /> <br /> You keep arguing that a company that wasn't participating in the artistic process shouldn't be blamed because they put their heart into it, while the actual artists seem to be the ones responsible for everything that went wrong. And when pointed to the fact that Paradox literally bought their way into having a direct say in those artists work, you're doubling down.<br /> <br /> Paradox is a publicly traded company valued at almost 2 billion USD. <u><b>THEY DON'T HAVE A HEART</b></u>. Nor should they.<br /> <br /> They aren't just pockets, either. Companies do strategy, oversight, planning, management, assessments, a whole lot of things.<br /> <br /> Hardsuit Labs' results are direct consequences of Paradox either doing something or deciding not to do something. They're not the ones making the game, but they're the ones doing business decisions. And it is quite possible that Paradox had far more say on what was going on in the project through whomever at HL that was their guy, as it wouldn't be hard to imagine that after 1/3 of the company got bought they gave oversight for the pet project to the new partner.<br /> <br /> It may well be that it was, in fact, Paradox whom fired Mitsoda, but through a liaison within HL.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-10T16:47:30-08:00","id":1555341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555339#post1555339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which makes no sense.<br /> <br /> You keep arguing that a company that wasn't participating in the artistic process shouldn't be blamed because they put their heart into it, while the actual artists seem to be the ones responsible for everything that went wrong. And when pointed to the fact that Paradox literally bought their way into having a direct say in those artists work, you're doubling down.<br /> <br /> Paradox is a publicly traded company valued at almost 2 billion USD. <u><b>THEY DON'T HAVE A HEART</b></u>. Nor should they.<br /> <br /> They aren't just pockets, either. Companies do strategy, oversight, planning, management, assessments, a whole lot of things.<br /> <br /> Hardsuit Labs' results are direct consequences of Paradox either doing something or deciding not to do something. They're not the ones making the game, but they're the ones doing business decisions. And it is quite possible that Paradox had far more say on what was going on in the project through whomever at HL that was their guy, as it wouldn't be hard to imagine that after 1/3 of the company got bought they gave oversight for the pet project to the new partner.<br /> <br /> It may well be that it was, in fact, Paradox whom fired Mitsoda, but through a liaison within HL.</div> </div> </div> </div>My apologies.<br /> <br /> I don't have any sympathy for Hardsuit Labs because it's a corporation too.<br /> <br /> There's no artists involved here in my anti-corporate anger. Only corporate decisions about how they were handled.<br /> <br /> Paradox gave them a bunch of resources and they didn't deliver. Paradox is not getting any sympathy from me because I don't think they were involved ENOUGH in the process since they seem to have given the HSL people way too much freedom and it ended up as a money sink. The only people I have any sympathy for in this is Chinese Room who seem to have poured their heart into salvaging this game and didn't get any real credit for it from the fans.<br /> <br /> I could be wrong in my interpretation but I'm mostly going off what the two most famous writers HSL fired said. I might also be looking to blame the people who fired them.<br /> <br /> In any case, I don't have any especial insight in this and am just sad the game doesn't look like it will be a big enough success to get more V:TM media out there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-10-2025, 07:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-10T21:40:41-08:00","id":1555346,"title":"","content":"The Quote button isn't working...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> [USER=&quot;12002&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">CTPhipps[/USER]]I don't have any sympathy for Hardsuit Labs because it's a corporation too.</div> </div> </div> </div>With 0,3% the size of Paradox and 1/10 it's total employees, not far from TCR, who's also a corporation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> [USER=&quot;12002&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">CTPhipps[/USER]]There's no artists involved here in my anti-corporate anger. Only corporate decisions about how they were handled.</div> </div> </div> </div>Paradox does corporate decisions too, far more than HL, and should own to them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> [USER=&quot;12002&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">CTPhipps[/USER]]Paradox gave them a bunch of resources and they didn't deliver.</div> </div> </div> </div>And <u>we don't know why</u>, or how much it was Paradox's fault, or even no one's fault.<br /> <br /> More importantly, Paradox isn't just a consumer here, this doesn't work by paying and just expecting delivery.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> [USER=&quot;12002&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">CTPhipps[/USER]]Paradox is not getting any sympathy from me because I don't think they were involved ENOUGH in the process since they seem to have given the HSL people way too much freedom and it ended up as a money sink.</div> </div> </div> </div>But getting involved was their responsibility, and that's the point. If Paradox chose to do nothing, the results are still on them for doing so.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> [USER=&quot;12002&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">CTPhipps[/USER]]The only people I have any sympathy for in this is Chinese Room who seem to have poured their heart into salvaging this game and didn't get any real credit for it from the fans.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't have a heart, either, they're a corporation with 55 direct employees plus who-knows-how-many contractors for the project.<br /> <br /> And all things considered I think they're in a better position after all that than you think. Not too great, though, but that's on them, too.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> [USER=&quot;12002&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">CTPhipps[/USER]]I could be wrong in my interpretation but I'm mostly going off what the two most famous writers HSL fired said.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing, they said nothing.<br /> <br /> They had fewer insight on what was going on than it first appeared, had a very small glimpse of management problems they can't contextualize, and otherwise know their work won't be used in the end.<br /> <br /> More importantly, they don't know who's to blame on anything.<br /> <br /> I personally think it very likely that they became too costly to keep around, because we're talking people who currently work at AAA projects, and HL may have become unable to keep up with the cost. But I don't and can't really know.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> [USER=&quot;12002&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">CTPhipps[/USER]]I might also be looking to blame the people who fired them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does seems to be the case, but you're loosing sight that Paradox is as much or more to blame than HL.<br /> <br /> Paradox could and should have chimed in. They either didn't, endorsed, or even took the decision. Mitsoda and company wouldn't be any the wiser.<br /> <br /> And blame in big projects isn't something you have in a limited quantity. They may be both to blame for a lot of things, Paradox is just the one I'm sure about.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> [USER=&quot;12002&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">CTPhipps[/USER]]In any case, I don't have any especial insight in this and am just sad the game doesn't look like it will be a big enough success to get more V:TM media out there.</div> </div> </div> </div>By the looks of it, it could, actually.<br /> <br /> Our current problem is less that the game can't get more VtM media done and more that Paradox won't capitalize on that.<br /> <br /> This game is only the latest in a series of blunders on their part, and they're burned. Every <b><i>business</i></b> decision they made with this IP was a fiasco, and not their only fiascoes during this time.<br /> <br /> However failed, though, the game got a lot of attention for the IP again, and it is serviceable. It's possible that even without them looking for interested parties, someone may approach Paradox with a project.<br /> <br /> Will that happen? Not likely, but not because the game was bad. It actually made a good dough if not for its abnormal cost, a solid AA title usually costs a third of what they got, so that's actually nice sells. There are just other considerations, and most of them have to do with Paradox, both current decisions and mismanagement history.<br /> <br /> Seriously though, they should just do a Grand Strategy based on VtM.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-11T04:04:55-08:00","id":1555356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555298#post1555298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The whole thing is a new game, period, no relation to the old WtA at all.<br /> <br /> So there is <i>a</i> Albretch, who's just a sad old excuse of a leader that was there when everything went down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honstly I think it sort of a matrix situation where Albretch was actually trapped in a sumulation with false memeores and the playes has to bust him out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-11T14:26:41-08:00","id":1555374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555356#post1555356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honstly I think it sort of a matrix situation where Albretch was actually trapped in a sumulation with false memeores and the playes has to bust him out.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would mean to still assume W5 is somehow a continuation of WtA.<br /> <br /> It just isn't, but you can use this headcanon if you really want to play W5 and reconcile both lore.<br /> <br /> Since I don't plan on playing w5 ever, I don't really care about their Albretch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-11T14:30:51-08:00","id":1555375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555374#post1555374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would mean to still assume W5 is somehow a continuation of WtA.<br /> <br /> It just isn't, but you can use this headcanon if you really want to play W5 and reconcile both lore.<br /> <br /> Since I don't plan on playing w5 ever, I don't really care about their Albretch.</div> </div> </div> </div>My issues with W5 are the same ones I have with Dark Sun, Ravenloft, and Planescape.<br /> <br /> I love all three/four settings.<br /> <br /> But the current editions are not continuations of the preexisting settings.<br /> <br /> And they don't pretend they are.<br /> <br /> But I LIKED the existing settings and wanted to see their stories continued with the characters I enjoyed.<br /> <br /> Then I open Planescape 5th Edition and go, &quot;Oh, Rowan Darkwood is back....and Faction War just didn't happen.&quot;<br /> <br /> It leaves me feeling the same sort of disconnect I feel with One More Day and Spider-Man and I suspect people who felt Crisis on Infinite Earths killed their love. It's not that I don't know these are fictional stories or that it can happen at any time but there's a momentum of character development and progress and events that just gets severed.<br /> <br /> It's why I liked V5 so much when it was being handled by OPP and why Chicago by Night 5E is my favorite supplement of the new line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-11-2025, 07:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-11T16:39:55-08:00","id":1555379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555375#post1555375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My issues with W5 are the same ones I have with Dark Sun, Ravenloft, and Planescape.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed and that sums up w5, you got it almost exactly.<br /> <br /> It is as much WtA as <i>Van Richten's Guide</i> is Ravenloft. And Albretch is as much the one you know as Elise Von Mordenheim is the Creature (or the original Elise).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-11T19:51:51-08:00","id":1555383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555374#post1555374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would mean to still assume W5 is somehow a continuation of WtA.<br /> <br /> It just isn't, but you can use this headcanon if you really want to play W5 and reconcile both lore.<br /> <br /> Since I don't plan on playing w5 ever, I don't really care about their Albretch.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555375#post1555375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My issues with W5 are the same ones I have with Dark Sun, Ravenloft, and Planescape.<br /> <br /> I love all three/four settings.<br /> <br /> But the current editions are not continuations of the preexisting settings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed on both. Which is why I Prefer WtE project since they lore could be read as follow up to legacy lore even if the Dates is a bit wonky.<br /> <br /> Like the default setting presumes that the (or at least a) apocalypse happened sometimes in the 80's and it's only stopped by king Albretch sealing him self in the umbra along side the super bane causing it (Which I personally think this provide a good narrative excuse for how he ended up in W5 which is basically Wryms personal spite fic towards the garou.)<br /> <br /> Moving on to something more on topic for thread I wonder why Paradox chose the chinse room instead of say Owl Bear for BL2. Like yes they're games are kinda janky but from what I've seen they're very competent RPGs and adpataion of the source materials. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-11T20:12:08-08:00","id":1555385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555383#post1555383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moving on to something more on topic for thread I wonder why Paradox chose the chinse room instead of say Owl Bear for BL2. Like yes they're games are kinda janky but from what I've seen they're very competent RPGs and adpataion of the source materials.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing were being laid out it that WoD/White Wolf was building a transmedia Empire and would say things like &quot;we're going to have a Netflix game in two years!&quot; They were planning TTRPGs, but movies, video games, novels, graphic-ts at Hot Topic - the whole shebang.<br /> <br /> The video games especially were going to bring Paradox into the next level.<br /> <br /> So all the decisions about where to go with V5 were made to support this planned expansion, along with simplifying the setting to bring in a new generation of fans which also reduced the exposition needed for a movie, show, or video game.<br /> <br /> Then Bloodlines, the crown jewel....never manifested.<br /> <br /> So much so they planned on cancelling the game outright and writing it off their taxes. The Chinese Room and their owners, however, approached them and gave them an offer to finish it.<br /> <br /> So the Chinese Room did.<br /> <br /> But it's too late. Paradox seems to have abandoned the transmedia empire and their original ambitions. White Wolf is BACK, baby, but White Wolf is now the 13th generation Nosferatu in the corner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-11T20:23:09-08:00","id":1555386,"title":"","content":"There's a giant list of reasons why a certain developer might not get a job: availability, desire, compatibility with Paradox, networking, willingness to commit the level of resources necessary (esp. if the project is beyond normal scope for the studio), not wanting to work under certain conditions (like forking over a 1/3 stake in your company), familiarity with desired design tools, deadline estimates, etc. etc. etc.<br /> <br /> The big impression given when TCR was announced by Paradox as basically that TCR wanted the project the most. That can mean a lot of things in corpo-speak from, &quot;they were the only people that would actually do it on our terms,&quot; to, &quot;they were willing to give us the best terms for what we considered the expected outcomes,&quot; to actually, &quot;we really felt like they understood the IP the best,&quot; and more.<br /> <br /> For relatively smaller studios looking to get a gig on a larger franchise there's a lot of selling yourself that the company needs to do. What the winning pitch is, is usually kept between the two companies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-11T20:37:36-08:00","id":1555387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555385#post1555385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thing were being laid out it that WoD/White Wolf was building a transmedia Empire and would say things like &quot;we're going to have a Netflix game in two years!&quot; They were planning TTRPGs, but movies, video games, novels, graphic-ts at Hot Topic - the whole shebang.<br /> <br /> The video games especially were going to bring Paradox into the next level.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean arguably Games Works shop beat Paradox in that regard since not only did they publish dozen of successful third party games using they Warhammer 40K setting but they even have a dedicated book label to publish stories in they universe and even a Whole streaming service. Granted that last one involve them nuking the fan animation community...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-11T21:39:08-08:00","id":1555389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555387#post1555387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean arguably Games Works shop beat Paradox in that regard</div> </div> </div> </div>Not hard.<br /> <br /> Long story short, Paradox thought the IP would sell itself and didn't bother.<br /> <br /> Even the original <i>Bloodlines 2</i> project mostly existed because Hardsuit Labs came to them, it seems they didn't reach out to look for contractors or anything.<br /> <br /> With the whole transmedia ambition it was the same, they just thought people would come willing to pay anything for te privilege of making stuff with their IP.<br /> <br /> Didn't work, then <i>Bloodlines 2</i> and they spend way more money than they should (like, 12 times the largest AA budget should be), compromising half a year worth of profits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-12T03:39:40-08:00","id":1555394,"title":"","content":"One thing that stands out about how Paradox has handled the book-side of things is how unstable the whole thing has been. If you go from the release of the V5 corebook to the current situation of bringing back White Wolf and starting the process of bringing everything in-house, trying to describe who did what when feels like looking at a bowl of spaghetti. That's why I've always been more a fan of simply giving it all to Renegade (both corebook and supplement development). Mostly to get it further away from Paradox. Because if anything, if this pattern holds, then in two years Paradox will have changed their mind again anyway and the whole thing will undergo yet another change.<br /> <br /> I do wonder about Paradox's relationship with developers and whether their general conduct as publishers has maybe dissuaded developers from approaching Paradox. I'm just thinking of various stories in the past. Like the situation with Lamplighter's League where Paradox leadership came out and called the game a disappointment and then an anonymous developer on a forum told people that Paradox had slashed the budget of the game because Paradox had lost faith in the project and so 80% of the staff had been let go before the launch of the game. Or one of the games from their &quot;indie&quot;-brand Paradox-Arc called Mechabellum had a successful 1.0 launch last year and got some good buzz from video-game-journalists. But what was the first thing the developer did with that success? They bought back the rights of the game from Paradox and went their separate ways. Or how Paradox used to work with Obsidian but as soon as their game Tyranny didn't meet expectations, Paradox complained about it and Obsidian left. Or the situation with Prison Architect 2 that I mentioned before. You just don't get the sense that Paradox has been very good in establishing relationships with developers over the years.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555379#post1555379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed and that sums up w5, you got it almost exactly.<br /> <br /> It is as much WtA as <i>Van Richten's Guide</i> is Ravenloft. And Albretch is as much the one you know as Elise Von Mordenheim is the Creature (or the original Elise).</div> </div> </div> </div>At this point, there's no consistency anymore. You can pretty much take any setting-element from previous editions and it feels like it's all up to chance whether it's still part of the setting unchanged, still part of the setting but it's changed in some fashion or it has been removed. For example, for the Ghost Council Tribe, the new version of the Older Brother Tribe, they brought back the idea of Banetenders being an important part of the Tribe. Or the history of the Bearshifters in W5 that one book vaguely hints at... is simply the same old backstory the Gurahl had. Or they brought back Zhyzhak as a notorious Black Spiral Dancer but they also slightly changed her backstory. But then you got stuff like the most recent W5 Umbra supplement Moonlit Path where one of the big ideas that book has is to portray the Umbra and Spirits in a way that has nothing to do with animism. According to that book, the Umbra is just a parallel universe fantasy-dimension and Spirits are just a bunch of fantasy-critters that populate it who do their own thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-12T06:49:05-08:00","id":1555404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555394#post1555394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing that stands out about how Paradox has handled the book-side of things is how unstable the whole thing has been.</div> </div> </div> </div>As many other things in this whole debacle, it comes from them not knowing what they're doing or how this industry works. Or strategy and planning, by the way. As always, they're good at making Grand Strategy games and that's it.<br /> <br /> But I think this whole WW return may not be something they really can change anymore. You know, the behavior they have with video game developers is likely also how they deal with TTRPG developers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555394#post1555394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do wonder about Paradox's relationship with developers and whether their general conduct as publishers has maybe dissuaded developers from approaching Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't say for sure, but I'm willing to bet money on it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555394#post1555394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At this point, there's no consistency anymore. You can pretty much take any setting-element from previous editions and it feels like it's all up to chance whether it's still part of the setting unchanged, still part of the setting but it's changed in some fashion or it has been removed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only here I'll disagree. At least with the idea that this is a problem or unexpected.<br /> <br /> As a &quot;spiritual successor&quot; with the same fucking name, w5 is unrelated and yet legitimate inheritor of everything WtA. This attitude is exactly what they announced from the get go. It's not that the setting is the same in any way, shape or form, but simply that they can bring any element from WtA without any change or shame.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-12T15:39:00-08:00","id":1555422,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure that last point really addresses the issue of consistency... sure it's a coherent message from Paradox's WoD team about how W5 is going to be handled, but it's also just affirming that we have no reason to trust in consistency because we never know what will come in from the previous editions, and if it does how much it will have changed in the process.<br /> <br /> A big part of how this fits into the overall pattern with Paradox, is that brands are built on consistency. Brands have value because the labels let you know what you're going to get; even negative things. Calling a product a spiritual successor to a previous work is still a promise of some level of consistency between the products despite not being a direct sequel (though labeling something as a direct sequel/iteration and calling it a spiritual successor is also not great marketing). If the new product isn't consistent enough with the previous product that the consumers feel that &quot;spirit&quot; then it's certainly a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-12T16:03:02-08:00","id":1555423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555389#post1555389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not hard.<br /> <br /> Long story short, Paradox thought the IP would sell itself and didn't bother.<br /> <br /> Even the original <i>Bloodlines 2</i> project mostly existed because Hardsuit Labs came to them, it seems they didn't reach out to look for contractors or anything.<br /> <br /> With the whole transmedia ambition it was the same, they just thought people would come willing to pay anything for te privilege of making stuff with their IP.<br /> <br /> Didn't work, then <i>Bloodlines 2</i> and they spend way more money than they should (like, 12 times the largest AA budget should be), compromising half a year worth of profits.</div> </div> </div> </div>And again it's nothing compared GW who has a respectable catalog of linced games consisting of not just the obvious 3 RTSs, 1 CRPG, 2 Left for Dead clones, an action game series and a retro FPS. Not to mention venerable catalog of Novels and TTRPG books they built up over the years. Not to mention the upcoming warhammer project starring Henry Cavill.<br /> <br /> Like I honestly think WOD would be better under GW. Ignoring all the skeletons in GW's own closet of course...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555404#post1555404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a &quot;spiritual successor&quot; with the same fucking name, w5 is unrelated and yet legitimate inheritor of everything WtA. This attitude is exactly what they announced from the get go. It's not that the setting is the same in any way, shape or form, but simply that they can bring any element from WtA without any change or shame.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well this is why WtE Project is a variable alternative since they also they goal. Only the team behind makes it clear that they are sticking close to legacy lore (Like they even have a Ex white wolf writer on they team for crying out loud.). Like the book is actually companionable with W5 rules for crying out lord.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-13T16:41:21-08:00","id":1555442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555422#post1555422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure that last point really addresses the issue of consistency... sure it's a coherent message from Paradox's WoD team about how W5 is going to be handled, but it's also just affirming that we have no reason to trust in consistency because we never know what will come in from the previous editions, and if it does how much it will have changed in the process.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it does because it basically means you shouldn't expect any of it, and anything that does get carried in any way should be treated as if it was just introduced for the first time. Because for this setting, it was.<br /> <br /> That said I just mean that this doesn't harm v5's internal consistency. It gave up legacy entirely while still keeping the name, and v5 may have other problems for its internal consistency. Overall it was a stupid move that literally killed the entire brand value for the new edition to begin anew.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555423#post1555423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And again it's nothing compared GW</div> </div> </div> </div>It's nothing compared to a lot of companies, because Paradox is straight up dumb in business. It isn't flattering to be compared to what they did with WoD. Or CofD, by that matter.<br /> <br /> But the thread is about the current state of Paradox, as they're the actual owners of the IP and the ones that may or may not decide to sell it to whomever.<br /> <br /> Onyx Path would be my choice for acquiring the IP, as they have experience to show working with the whole IP, not just WtA, plus the other WW IPs. But it's on Paradox's hands who'll be able to buy it in the end, and we don't know if either OP or GW will want or be able to make the purchase.<br /> <br /> WtE may be wonderful, but for now it only exists as long as the IP owner let them exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-13T16:56:43-08:00","id":1555443,"title":"","content":"I don't think it'll be acquired by any small independent company given the value of the various video games it has already produced. They may not be huge but they're huge compared to tabletop games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-13T18:04:53-08:00","id":1555447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555423#post1555423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I honestly think WOD would be better under GW. Ignoring all the skeletons in GW's own closet of course...</div> </div> </div> </div>GW's history of killing &quot;unprofitable&quot; products makes me not want anything to do with them. [Gestures at <i>Mordheim</i> and other such games] <br /> <br /> The big problem here is, surprise, capitalism. Publicly held companies are beholden to growth, not quality, and GW knows how to play that game. If you look at GW's Market Cap, it's <b>SOARED</b> over the last five years. That's why they never &quot;learn,&quot; because they aren't focused on their players but their stockholders.<br /> <br /> Paradox's market cap history is pretty stagnant compared to GW's, which makes me agree with the posters who say Paradox is just bad at business.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6423-higgipedia","name":"higgipedia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6423_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-13T18:39:43-08:00","id":1555448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>higgipedia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555447#post1555447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> GW's history of killing &quot;unprofitable&quot; products makes me not want anything to do with them. [Gestures at <i>Mordheim</i> and other such games]<br /> <br /> The big problem here is, surprise, capitalism. Publicly held companies are beholden to growth, not quality, and GW knows how to play that game. If you look at GW's Market Cap, it's <b>SOARED</b> over the last five years. That's why they never &quot;learn,&quot; because they aren't focused on their players but their stockholders.<br /> <br /> Paradox's market cap history is pretty stagnant compared to GW's, which makes me agree with the posters who say Paradox is just bad at business.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're waiting for the perfect and making themselves the enemy of the good.<br /> <br /> Ironically, whenever they ignore this, letting small companies do whatever, they get solid product that increases the public's access to material.<br /> <br /> LA by Night, the Onyx Path 5E books, the visual novels, Choice of Games, and so on.<br /> <br /> Let people do a cheap set of V:TM movies or even Youtube series. Allow much smaller indie lines of new novels. Build up the fanbase that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-13T21:22:54-08:00","id":1555455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555443#post1555443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it'll be acquired by any small independent company given the value of the various video games it has already produced. They may not be huge but they're huge compared to tabletop games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, although their weight in the matter is limited. The games are licensed, they don't actually belong with the IP, and their impact for a prospective buyer is limited to the contractual cut on future sales, not on anything already done. So most of them actually add very little.<br /> <br /> <i>Bloodlines 2</i> is the most important for now, as it still may make some reasonable money at least for the next year. Not enough to cover Paradox's costs, but certainly enough to weight in the IP's price. And, of course, <b>it is</b> part of the IP, for whatever it's worth. But that's about it, once its DLC support ends it'll be a matter of time for its weight on the matter to vanish, too.<br /> <br /> In the end the IP's market value is more about what can be done with it in the future than whatever has been done with it already, because new revenue from old material is very limited.<br /> <br /> Yet, I don't think this value will be low enough for most traditional TTRPG to buy, that's almost for certain. The best we can expect is for it to be bought by someone easier to license from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555448#post1555448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're waiting for the perfect and making themselves the enemy of the good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, a lot of that, yes.<br /> <br /> Paradox has, among other problems, a history of unrealistic expectations and disproportionate reactions to frustration and extreme resistance to compromise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-13T22:11:53-08:00","id":1555457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555442#post1555442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WtE may be wonderful, but for now it only exists as long as the IP owner let them exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well then it should be safe since for all of parawolves fault they tend to leave ST vault projects alone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555448#post1555448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let people do a cheap set of V:TM movies or even Youtube series. Allow much smaller indie lines of new novels. Build up the fanbase that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is what they're doing with <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=t1Kc0xuYnfQ&amp;list=PLyiDf91_bTEith9kJg3sJeBm2XSSL9EVv&amp;index=2\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter the Parenting</a> which frankly does H5 premise better than H5 it's self. Although that's because the creators wrote like a Hunter the Vergil with a\u200b OwoD reskin more than anything else (Like I'm getting some heavy Task Force VALKERY from what little I've seen of they portrayel of the SI)..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-13T23:43:07-08:00","id":1555462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555457#post1555457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well then it should be safe since for all of parawolves fault they tend to leave ST vault projects alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>For now.<br /> <br /> [Baneposting?]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which is what they're doing with <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=t1Kc0xuYnfQ&amp;list=PLyiDf91_bTEith9kJg3sJeBm2XSSL9EVv&amp;index=2\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter the Parenting</a> which frankly does H5 premise better than H5 it's self. Although that's because the creators wrote like a <b>Hunter the Vergil</b> with a OwoD reskin more than anything else (Like I'm getting some heavy Task Force VALKERY from what little I've seen of they portrayel of the SI).. </div> </div> </div>Best typo. Makes me <b>motivated</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-16T15:08:26-08:00","id":1555504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555404#post1555404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only here I'll disagree. At least with the idea that this is a problem or unexpected.<br /> <br /> As a &quot;spiritual successor&quot; with the same fucking name, w5 is unrelated and yet legitimate inheritor of everything WtA. This attitude is exactly what they announced from the get go. It's not that the setting is the same in any way, shape or form, but simply that they can bring any element from WtA without any change or shame.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that there's no vision of any kind. The process is more akin to joining a new group and the WtA-ST sitting you down and explaining their headcanon to you. The term &quot;headcanon&quot; is important here because it just comes off as people familiar with WtA picking and choosing things from the past and some things count and others don't. And above all, it's all personal. There's no grand vision. I may have my issues with Justin Achilli but I do believe he had a coherent vision of what he wanted WOD5E to be like. What W5 has turned into after he left is just rambling incoherence.<br /> <br /> The incoherence I'm referring to is that there's no rhyme or reason to when W5 dips into the well of &quot;continuation&quot; or when it does something completely different. It's all just random. If this continues, the contradictions will just mount in how the W5 version of the WtA-setting is described.<br /> <br /> Not that the WOD-books were great in that regard in the past but I figure you gotta expect people to do better in 2025 than in the 90s. Of course, Paradox matters here as well because it's not like writers can do whatever they want. And it was also Paradox who secretly cancelled the Chronicles of Darkness and the 20th Anniversary Editions. And even while these books were published, there were controversies about interference.<br /> <br /> For example, let's ask the question: Does Evan Heals-The-Past exist in W5? Maybe... or maybe not. It would also not surprise me if an upcoming W5 supplement proclaimed Albrecht had been in a Pack with Mara and... Andy, the Galestalker, that guy you never had heard of before. That's what W5 is like at this point. It's equally possible that it's just reproducing legacy-lore, presenting a changed version of legacy-lore or just doing something different altogether. <br /> <br /> And what makes it so incoherent is that there's no grand vision behind it. It's just up to the whim of whoever's writing it. Hence why it feels like simply listening to somebody's &quot;headcanon&quot;. <br /> <br /> There are all the weird things going on with old stuff but even the new stuff. The Koranyi sisters were introduced as exemplar Garou in Shattered Nation, then in Wyrmtide a major part of the frame-narrative was focused on them and then in Moonlit Path they were presented as... Ancestor Spirits. Mind you (Spoilers!), the tragedy of the narrative in Wyrmtide was that one (!) of the sisters had died. But according to Moonlit Path they're both dead now... somehow. <br /> <br /> The reason this inconsistency is becoming distracting is that there's no pattern between when W5 is regurgitating stuff from previous editions and when it's doing new stuff. This just seems like a recipe for disaster. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-16T15:40:58-08:00","id":1555505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555504#post1555504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem is that there's no vision of any kind. The process is more akin to joining a new group and the WtA-ST sitting you down and explaining their headcanon to you. The term &quot;headcanon&quot; is important here because it just comes off as people familiar with WtA picking and choosing things from the past and some things count and others don't. And above all, it's all personal. There's no grand vision. I may have my issues with Justin Achilli but I do believe he had a coherent vision of what he wanted WOD5E to be like. What W5 has turned into after he left is just rambling incoherence.<br /> <br /> The incoherence I'm referring to is that there's no rhyme or reason to when W5 dips into the well of &quot;continuation&quot; or when it does something completely different. It's all just random. If this continues, the contradictions will just mount in how the W5 version of the WtA-setting is described.<br /> <br /> Not that the WOD-books were great in that regard in the past but I figure you gotta expect people to do better in 2025 than in the 90s. Of course, Paradox matters here as well because it's not like writers can do whatever they want. And it was also Paradox who secretly cancelled the Chronicles of Darkness and the 20th Anniversary Editions. And even while these books were published, there were controversies about interference.<br /> <br /> For example, let's ask the question: Does Evan Heals-The-Past exist in W5? Maybe... or maybe not. It would also not surprise me if an upcoming W5 supplement proclaimed Albrecht had been in a Pack with Mara and... Andy, the Galestalker, that guy you never had heard of before. That's what W5 is like at this point. It's equally possible that it's just reproducing legacy-lore, presenting a changed version of legacy-lore or just doing something different altogether.<br /> <br /> And what makes it so incoherent is that there's no grand vision behind it. It's just up to the whim of whoever's writing it. Hence why it feels like simply listening to somebody's &quot;headcanon&quot;.<br /> <br /> There are all the weird things going on with old stuff but even the new stuff. The Koranyi sisters were introduced as exemplar Garou in Shattered Nation, then in Wyrmtide a major part of the frame-narrative was focused on them and then in Moonlit Path they were presented as... Ancestor Spirits. Mind you (Spoilers!), the tragedy of the narrative in Wyrmtide was that one (!) of the sisters had died. But according to Moonlit Path they're both dead now... somehow.<br /> <br /> The reason this inconsistency is becoming distracting is that there's no pattern between when W5 is regurgitating stuff from previous editions and when it's doing new stuff. This just seems like a recipe for disaster.</div> </div> </div> </div>It reminds me very much of DC after the New 52 reboot where some things were started over from scratch and other things were a continuation like Batman. There's a lot of competing artistic visions here.<br /> <br /> I know which I prefer but I understand people who don't want to be beholden to past continuity.<br /> <br /> But I also feel like that sort of thing should be spinoffs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-16T16:02:57-08:00","id":1555506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555505#post1555505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It reminds me very much of DC after the New 52 reboot where some things were started over from scratch and other things were a continuation like Batman. There's a lot of competing artistic visions here.<br /> <br /> I know which I prefer but I understand people who don't want to be beholden to past continuity.<br /> <br /> But I also feel like that sort of thing should be spinoffs.</div> </div> </div> </div>In that regard, what I've come to really appreciate is things like Sean Murphy's White Knight mini-series. Just give it to a team of creatives and in this limited run they have their own little universe. And it already starts to feel like the whole &quot;Absolute&quot;-series-thing is heading for a cliff in that regard. Originally, it was just these series about the traditional DC-heroes with very different origins but thanks to its success it already feels like we're gonna sit here in 2030 and Absolute Batman issue # 150 has come out. But with those limited runs, creatives can just do whatever and above all don't have to interrupt their planned storylines for crossover-events (aka &quot;Hey, kid! If you wanna know the full story, why don't you buy 10 comics this month?&quot;). <br /> <br /> And I think WOD has been in this boat for a while. Maybe if everything had worked out, the V5 corebook coming out, no scandal, Bloodlines 2 coming out as planned and you could've reestablished the 5th edition version as the new starting point for the WOD. But that didn't happen.<br /> <br /> And I think the next best thing would've been to go for expansive and modular. This would also have allowed to okay more releases for Chronicles of Darkness and 20th Anniversay Edition. Because it's all about giving up the notion, there's one authority that has to set the tone. WOD has grown so much that a lot of different people have a lot of different opinions about it. You'll never satisfy all of them, no matter what you do. Hence, expansive and modular. <br /> <br /> But instead, Paradox went for the worst of both worlds: It meddles in what people write about in these RPG-books but also has no coherent vision for what it wants those games to be like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-16T18:14:45-08:00","id":1555508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555504#post1555504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem is that there's no vision of any kind.</div> </div> </div> </div>And my point is that their take on Legacy has nothing to do with it.<br /> <br /> The problem is that they have no vision, no planning and no consistency. Well, it's actually that and a few more things, but lets focus on that.<br /> <br /> But those things have nothing <i>directly </i>to do with their take on Legacy, or rather, it's not because of what they're doing with its pieces.<br /> <br /> What would it change if someone gave them an actual framework on what to take from Legacy? They'd still be clueless about where they're going and have no consistency on the actual new stuff, as you said yourself. Without Legacy they would be churning material even slower, because they wouldn't have a trove of already written material. With a straight continuation, they'd be maiming Legacy as they advance in their directionless and inconsistent way.<br /> <br /> I stand by the point that their take with Legacy is clear, and it is not the source of inconsistency. They said it is a new setting that can reference the old setting in whichever way they want, and it is exactly that. They never promised old content to come back and every time it does is within a new context anyway.<br /> <br /> Nothing I said means W5 is consistent or anything, it clearly isn't, it's just that this bewilderment with their take on Legacy distracts from the actual problems. I'm also not saying those things are completely unrelated either, the reason they're doing that is certainly because they have no vision or direction and do an inconsistent and incoherent work, but it is the lack of vision and incoherence that causes both the problems and the take on Legacy.<br /> <br /> Under similar circumstances one could theoretically have an actual coherent vision and still have a reason to take and choose from Legacy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555505#post1555505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It reminds me very much of DC after the New 52 reboot</div> </div> </div> </div>Believe me, it's way worse.<br /> <br /> New 52 had a few things for it. First, many titles got good writers sooner or later. Sure, some were <i>Red Hood And The Outlaws</i>, but a mixed bag is a mixed bag.<br /> <br /> Second, it gave artist the space to do their stuff. Indeed, that's the reason behind a lot of the awful stuff, but also the good things, regardless if they followed &quot;legacy&quot; or not.<br /> <br /> Third, it was willing to correct course as it went on. Drop bad titles, review bad changes, kill the new Lobo, that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> W5 isn't a mixed bag, it is a single incoherent and bad piece in the bag. It has constant interference with no goal beyond a vague sense of what they like for a given bit, but disconnected from the other bits. And it doesn't correct course in any recognizable way.<br /> <br /> Imagine if the whole inconsistency and incoherence of the first 2 years of New 52 were concentrated into a single title, frequently in the same book. That's W5.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555506#post1555506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But instead, Paradox went for the worst of both worlds: It meddles in what people write about in these RPG-books but also has no coherent vision for what it wants those games to be like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically the problem is that it goes by a romantic vision of the game, in the actual sociological sense.<br /> <br /> The problem with romantic visions is that they always refer to a made-up past that never existed, being actually bits and pieces of several places and moments, both exaggerated and mashed together without real coherence.<br /> <br /> So that's their guideline, and the worse is that it is based on Vampire, not Werewolf. They never wanted to do Werewolf itself and they said that before, they want to do VtM with shapechifters and a nod to Legacy WtA. But since their vision is of a romantic past version, it doesn't really has a guiding goal or basic coherence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-16T18:21:03-08:00","id":1555509,"title":"","content":"How I would fix W:TA:<br /> <br /> &quot;Wolfbloods&quot; - Reintroduce Kinfolk <br /> <br /> &quot;Claws of Fenris&quot; - An outlaw Nazi hunting group of Get who believe the Cult of Fenris is a bunch of Garou who came from the Umbra like alien invaders, maybe a pocket dimension, to slaughter as well as replace most of their kind.<br /> <br /> &quot;Beastkin&quot; - Rules for playing out shifter types<br /> <br /> And just ignore the contradictions.<br /> <br /> Maybe even an adventure where the Garou discover the Umbral silver record as a concept was stolen and recovering it restores the Garou's memories of the past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-16T19:27:41-08:00","id":1555510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555509#post1555509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How I would fix W:TA:</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't fix it because I think doing so is fundamentally playing by the same book, bulldozing the work of others and the game of other gamers just to have it may way.<br /> <br /> My take is to just run Legacy, and if economically feasible continue this new setting for whomever likes it, but with an actual plan and professional designers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-16T19:52:46-08:00","id":1555511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555510#post1555510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't fix it because I think doing so is fundamentally playing by the same book, bulldozing the work of others and the game of other gamers just to have it may way.<br /> <br /> My take is to just run Legacy, and if economically feasible continue this new setting for whomever likes it, but with an actual plan and professional designers.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's from the fan perspective but I mean from the Paradox perspective, if fixing is possible.<br /> <br /> Fans have created SABBAT: THE SCHISM and WEREWOLF: THE ESSENTIAL.<br /> <br /> Hell, I made the Murder of Modius for Gary, Indiana.<br /> <br /> Fan content fills a void but it can't substitute for things fans actually want to watch. If they really wanted to make things better, they'd get another official stream going.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-17T00:25:29-08:00","id":1555520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555511#post1555511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's from the fan perspective but I mean from the Paradox perspective, if fixing is possible.<br /> <br /> Fans have created SABBAT: THE SCHISM and WEREWOLF: THE ESSENTIAL.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also fun fact about WTE is that It does actually support W5 in addition to W20 (through the W20 is a smoother exprance on the ST end) so you could use the book to bring in some legacy elements to a W5 game.<br /> <br /> Line one concept I had for a W5 game is basically the matrix adventure where the players actuality exploit &quot;glitches&quot; to allow them to access legacy abilities to help them bust out of the illusion they found them selves in. Or Just some Legacy/WtE elements popup in W5 adventures (like say a Eastern concordat algined pack showing up in Isle of Splintered Dreamsas an example) if the ST isn't welling to brave the mountain of paperwork to pull it off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-17T06:19:48-08:00","id":1555527,"title":"","content":"This isn't exactly about Bloodlines 2 but I heard that Colossal Order, devs of City Skylines, separated from Paradox and a new development studio is taking City Skylines 2.<br /> <br /> Man, Paradox is lucky that Europa Universalis 5 is a hit, otherwise this was a horrific year for them. It still is, but not as horrific as it could have been.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-17T07:46:16-08:00","id":1555529,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's still Paradox as the publisher but instead of the Colossal Order developer-studio, it's now Iceflake studio that's going to continue work on the game. Paradox really needs to do some self-reflection because it is weird that these sorts of issues between them, the publisher, and their chosen developers just keep happening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-17T09:18:24-08:00","id":1555534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555511#post1555511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's from the fan perspective but I mean from the Paradox perspective, if fixing is possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was actually talking from a business and/or artistic perspective.<br /> <br /> From a fan perspective I have other avenues than canon to solve any problems I have. It isn't the same, sure, but it does the job.<br /> <br /> And from the Paradox perspective there's no problem, <b>that's</b> the problem. It isn't really rocket science to solve this mess, but it would demand them to notice the problem, diagnose it and recognize the role of their current strategy on it. They're simply not in the required head-space to do any of it right now.<br /> <br /> So it only makes sense to think of what we'd do if given the reins of the IP as a publisher.<br /> <br /> Either way, as a fan I stand by what I said, I just ignore w5, it's simple enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-17T12:27:54-08:00","id":1555547,"title":"","content":"Here's an article on the change regarding Cities Skylines 2 - and the title says it all: <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/paradox-interactive-parts-ways-with-cities-skylines-studio-after-over-15-years-as-publishers-misfortunes-continue\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Paradox Interactive parts ways with Cities: Skylines studio after over 15 years, as publisher's misfortunes continue&quot;</a><br /> <br /> I think, it's hard to miss at this point that Paradox has issues it needs to work through. The article mentioned above has a quote from last year that the deputy CEO offered to the outlet last year about the company's future: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;What we have to do is start small, listen to the fans early, and most importantly, stay within our core,&quot; Lilja told Eurogamer last year, discussing the company's future. &quot;We do more extensive and earlier peer reviews to get honest feedback earlier. </div> </div> </div>But then I look at the announcement for Cities Skylines 2 and Paradox is <i>still </i>talking about a console-version of the game. That was another thing that was announced at the start and then later had been delayed indefinitely. Making the UI controller-friendly, adjusting the game to work on consoles... there are a lot of challenges connected to this, of course and Colossal Order had pretty much given up on it at some point. But for whatever reason, Paradox seems to be very interested in the idea of Cities Skylines 2 getting a console-release. <br /> <br /> But at the end of the day, Colossal Order was a small developer with 30 employees and this new Iceflake Studio seems to be pretty small, too. There are certainly a lot of job-offerings on their website. Who knows how this is going to go...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-17T16:17:10-08:00","id":1555561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555534#post1555534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Either way, as a fan I stand by what I said, I just ignore w5, it's simple enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>well that's a vald way to run WtE since again it's desgined to run with W20 so you could just ignore w5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555547#post1555547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's an article on the change regarding Cities Skylines 2 - and the title says it all: <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/paradox-interactive-parts-ways-with-cities-skylines-studio-after-over-15-years-as-publishers-misfortunes-continue\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Paradox Interactive parts ways with Cities: Skylines studio after over 15 years, as publisher's misfortunes continue&quot;</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that the same deputy CEO who said that they're scaling back Boodlines 2 post launch support and probably in house devloupment of WoD products? <br /> <br /> Like if nothing else she seems to be in favor of cutting back projecta. For better or worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-17T16:30:25-08:00","id":1555562,"title":"","content":"It confuses me what White Wolf being revived as a company means then.<br /> <br /> Will they produce anything (as not part of Paradox) or just as a licensing group?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-17T17:05:29-08:00","id":1555568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555561#post1555561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like if nothing else she seems to be in favor of cutting back projecta. For better or worse.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Bloodlines 2</i> cost 60 million USD already (<b><u>expensive</u></b> AA games usually cost less than 5 million), and only made about 13 from sales until now. It's a money sink.<br /> <br /> Paradox's problems for the last years have everything to do with too many ambitious projects they're unprepared to deal with for various reasons.<br /> <br /> Just to say it isn't the CEO, the company is really in need of cutting projects right now. Although not necessarily the ones they're cutting, or in the way they're doing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555562#post1555562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It confuses me what White Wolf being revived as a company means then.<br /> <br /> Will they produce anything (as not part of Paradox) or just as a licensing group?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they're moving <i>City Skylines</i> to an internal team, too. It seems that they don't want to contract developers anymore.<br /> <br /> My impression is that the company who messed things up royally by being overly controlling is trying to have even more control and micromanage development to try and make it work. It makes some sense, as they <i><b>believe</b></i> the problem is other people.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-17T17:15:27-08:00","id":1555570,"title":"","content":"Yes, it absolutely is a AAA game in expense and got AA results.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-17T21:04:53-08:00","id":1555591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555570#post1555570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it absolutely is a AAA game in expense and got AA results.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well compare that to a game released around the time A superhero themed workplace comady game by former talltale staff called Dispach. It sold over one million after 10 days after release.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.rpgfan.com/2025/11/09/dispatch-1-million-copies-sold-worldwide/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.rpgfan.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Dispatch-Screenshot-004-1280x720.webp\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.rpgfan.com/2025/11/09/dispatch-1-million-copies-sold-worldwide/\" target=\"_blank\"> Dispatch Soars With Over 1 Million Copies Sold Worldwide | RPGFan </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.rpgfan.com/2025/11/09/dispatch-1-million-copies-sold-worldwide/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.rpgfan.com/2025/11/09/dispatch-1-million-copies-sold-worldwide/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> AdHoc Studios has announced that their superhero adventure game Dispatch has sold over 1 million copies since its initial release for console and PC on </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-17T23:25:51-08:00","id":1555592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555568#post1555568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Bloodlines 2</i> cost 60 million USD already (<b><u>expensive</u></b> AA games usually cost less than 5 million), and only made about 13 from sales until now. It's a money sink.<br /> <br /> Paradox's problems for the last years have everything to do with too many ambitious projects they're unprepared to deal with for various reasons.<br /> <br /> Just to say it isn't the CEO, the company is really in need of cutting projects right now. Although not necessarily the ones they're cutting, or in the way they're doing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Well, they're moving <i>City Skylines</i> to an internal team, too. It seems that they don't want to contract developers anymore.<br /> <br /> My impression is that the company who messed things up royally by being overly controlling is trying to have even more control and micromanage development to try and make it work. It makes some sense, as they <i><b>believe</b></i> the problem is other people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell, even on the book side of things... Renegade's work has got the WOD-RPG-books the fourth place in sales for years now. I may have my issues with these books but, as a company, Renegade has proven to be quite reliable in terms of releases and distribution. So, for example, when it comes to Mage the Ascension Fifth Edition, if you had told Renegade to release that, we would already have it in our hands by now, I imagine. It's not that Renegade can't release a book like that, it's that Paradox hasn't allowed them to do so. With other companies like Onyx Path, it would be the same thing (although the release would happen on a smaller scale via a Kickstarter model). The only way you're not gonna get this timely release was to rely on the nebulous inner workings of this in-house WOD-team. And then first Justin Achilli left with his big job being left unoccupied for a long time and then you got the whole kerfuffle with the switch to the newly resurrected White Wolf. With no timetable for a release of an M5 corebook. <br /> <br /> And it really does seem like Paradox has drawn the strange conclusion that the reason they've gone through so many misadventures with their publishing is... that they didn't have enough control. That and some belief that only grand strategy games are something they can do - as if they're cursed to fail at everything else. <br /> <br /> Hopefully, Cities Skylines 2 won't suffer the same fate as Prison Architect 2 where the switch to a new developer just led to an indefinite delay in the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-18T16:42:07-08:00","id":1555613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555591#post1555591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well compare that to a game released around the time A superhero themed workplace comady game by former talltale staff called Dispach. It sold over one million after 10 days after release.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but the point isn't that. Paradox has successful games, too, that's why they are the size they are.<br /> <br /> <i>Dispatch</i> is a small game with a small production cost and a small price. If it ended up being a flop, it would be a relatively small loss. It was also done by experienced devs working within their know-how. For this thread what's important isn't that it was an astounding success (and I have it and here in my house we've been expecting it since it was announced for the first time), but that it was a project well managed (it seems, at least). By the way, it wouldn't sell nearly as much if they wanted to price it 60 USD.<br /> <br /> <i>Bloodlines 2</i> is a money sink because it cost too much. Even if it had sold over 1 million copies it wouldn't break even, and the decision to price it as an AAA probably backfired. It needed the kind of numbers Nintendo gets from <i>Pokemon</i> and <i>Zelda</i> games to be deemed profitable. This kind of investment by a mid-level publisher is just bad manager, failure was a given even if the game were actually a success.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555592#post1555592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it really does seem like Paradox has drawn the strange conclusion that the reason they've gone through so many misadventures with their publishing is... that they didn't have enough control. That and some belief that only grand strategy games are something they can do - as if they're cursed to fail at everything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>This belief is actually accurate, if only because they're incompetent at doing anything else.<br /> <br /> But the problem is that actually this isn't their conclusion, either. They believe, and directly said more than once, that only Grand Strategy games <i>are profitable</i>. The problem isn't them, it is an inherent aspect of everything else.<br /> <br /> On the book side of things they could, from the get-go, just had allowed Onyx Path to continue and focus on marketing (the one thing they did well). Seriously, they didn't need anything else, OP was already releasing at a good enough pace, and even if they wanted to stop the Kickstarts, OP's costs are pennies/\u00f6ren to Paradox. Same with Renegade, as much as we could critic the results as art, we certainly couldn't argue their results as a company.<br /> <br /> Yet... Paradox wants more control. And by now I don't think it would be easy for them to get a good partner even if they wanted, because it really seems they're not great to work with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-22T06:26:59-08:00","id":1555754,"title":"","content":"It doesn't seem like Paradox these days is able to catch a break. Besides Europa Universalis 5 (which was a success) and Bloodlines 2, Paradox as a publisher also released Surviving Mars Relaunched a couple days ago. Mind you, this game's a remaster of an older game. So, how's this going, you might wonder...<br /> <br /> From the article (source: PCGamesN): <a href=\"https://www.pcgamesn.com/surviving-mars/remastered-reception\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Surviving Mars Relaunched crashes on Steam as the strategy game's paid remaster doesn't even fix the original's flaws&quot;</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The point is that the release of Surviving Mars Relaunched has rubbed players of the original strategy sim the wrong way, and they're making sure any new or returning colonists know it via the Steam reviews. Now sat at a 'mixed' 42% positive from close to a thousand responses, players are primarily complaining about &quot;core bugs and issues&quot; being left in from the original. One also jokes that maybe they'll see improvements if they &quot;buy the game for a third time\u2026&quot; It begs the question, if bugs return intact, does it officially make them a feature?<br /> <br /> Another reads, &quot;This should've been early access&quot;, which is a bewildering idea for a game released seven years ago, stating that &quot;not only is charging twice for the same game a shady tactic, but the 'reworks' aren't really good&quot; and that, echoing the sentiment of the top review, &quot;the game is riddled with bugs.&quot; Again.<br /> <br /> Outside of one positive review, which basically says it's a good deal if you're upgrading from the base game given that the remaster includes the previously paid-for DLC, multiple people point out that many of its major bugs only kick in long after the typical Steam refund period has passed. </div> </div> </div>So, it isn't even the entire strategy game genre, it's just this one specific type of grand strategy games they can pull off...<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, taking a look at <a href=\"https://steamcharts.com/app/532790#1m\" target=\"_blank\">Steam-charts</a>, Bloodlines 2 has pretty much fallen off the radar. It isn't that surprising because I wouldn't say that the game has good replay-value and with the general mixed reaction not giving it a good word-of-mouth boost... The next interesting moment will come when the first story DLC gets released. I'm curious what the player numbers will look like then.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-22T07:18:14-08:00","id":1555757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555754#post1555754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile, taking a look at <a href=\"https://steamcharts.com/app/532790#1m\" target=\"_blank\">Steam-charts</a>, Bloodlines 2 has pretty much fallen off the radar. It isn't that surprising because I wouldn't say that the game has good replay-value and with the general mixed reaction not giving it a good word-of-mouth boost... The next interesting moment will come when the first story DLC gets released. I'm curious what the player numbers will look like then.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really have any enthusiasm for the DLC because I have no interest in playing a serial killing anti-Thin Blood bigot. I really would have enjoyed more Phyre content.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-23T07:45:05-08:00","id":1555799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555757#post1555757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't really have any enthusiasm for the DLC because I have no interest in playing a serial killing anti-Thin Blood bigot. I really would have enjoyed more Phyre content.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I get the Toreador-one but Benny... That was a weird choice. After having finished it, I thought a more interesting choice would've been characters like Tolly or Safia (like a deep dive on their character by giving them parallel adventures or something like an origin story).<br /> <br /> But Phyre would've also been interesting. Like a hunter who used to go after her way back in the past but now he's back because he was willing to become a ghoul or a vampire (depending on the time) in order to hunt down Phyre. And it's just this setup for a combat-arena (with stealth-options), a nice-looking fight against an adversary and then you have some &quot;Do you want to spare him or not?&quot;-option at the end. Something modest like that would've been a good addition, I think. <br /> <br /> To be optimistic for a second, I hope that this elongated development-process (via DLC) allows them to overhaul stuff like combat and the Resonance-system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-23T19:27:56-08:00","id":1555818,"title":"","content":"Lets see what they can pull out. I still think all things considered, TCR did a miracle by releasing a game so not-horrible, so I'm not completely without hope for how the DLCs will improve it for this single year of support.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-23T19:47:09-08:00","id":1555819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/jH3zvmNcxIs\" data-code=\"jH3zvmNcxIs\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/jH3zvmNcxIs/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> A discussion by Matt about the creation of the game. The actual review starts at 3:00.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-24T02:14:06-08:00","id":1555821,"title":"","content":"The most bizarre thing about looking back at what happened with Bloodlines 2 is to realise that Paradox hasn't truly learnt its lesson. Switching to new developers, buying into overhyped pitches from developers to the point of overconfidently buying them... They're still doing it! This is exactly the same mess that happened with Cities Skylines 2 recently. They split ways with Colossal Order, then buy up Iceflake studios and let them continue. Except... Iceflake studios is a small studio that made a mediocre low-budget strategy game and other than that, the studio has only worked on small mobile games. And yet at the same time, they were also apparently very sure that continuing to work with Colossal Order would be a bad idea. So, realistically, it's hard to see what gave Paradox the confidence to handle the situation like this. Prison Architect 2 also follows that pattern. At least in the case of Chinese Room, they did end up delivering a game, though.<br /> <br /> The only way I could see Paradox thinking that none of their decisions were to blame for these mistakes and failures is if they actually believe that whenever a bad thing happens with a videogame, it's the developers' fault.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-24T22:23:11-08:00","id":1555840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555821#post1555821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only way I could see Paradox thinking that none of their decisions were to blame for these mistakes and failures is if they actually believe that whenever a bad thing happens with a videogame, it's the developers' fault.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems to be exactly what they think.<br /> <br /> Maybe sometimes they can blame the market, or a given entire genre, but overall they blame the developers.<br /> <br /> What I think is that they got overconfident with their success at their own subgenre and didn't notice it was mostly an accident.<br /> <br /> And that's the problem because to learn other things they have to accept that they don't know the secret of their own success. And in the end that's the problem: they fail at things because they assume they know far more than they actually know.<br /> <br /> Dunning-Kruger as commonly understood isn't a real thing, but Paradox is a real life example of the legendary take on it. They're too stupid to realize just how stupid they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-25T03:25:14-08:00","id":1555841,"title":"","content":"Dan Pinchbeck, one of the cofounders of The Chinese Room (who has left The Chinese Room in 2023), was on a podcast talking about the development of Bloodlines 2.<br /> <br /> From <a href=\"https://www.pcgamer.com/games/rpg/the-chinese-rooms-cofounder-told-paradox-we-cant-make-bloodlines-2-but-then-they-did-make-bloodlines-2-and-it-was-like-untangling-an-anaconda-f-ball-of-competing-priorities/\" target=\"_blank\">Rick Lane's article on PCGamer</a>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As is so often the case, it appears Bloodlines 2's adoptive developers were highly aware of this potential problem. Speaking to Cat Burton of the Goth Boss Podcast (via PCGamesN) TCR cofounder Dan Pinchbeck explained how he urged Paradox Interactive not to call Bloodlines 2, well, <b>that</b>.<br /> <br /> Pinchbeck says that, from the start, The Chinese Room intended to build its own version of the game, rather than try to finish the work done by Hardsuit Labs up to that point. &quot;When we first started talking to Paradox, I said\u2014we'd even seen the Hardsuit build\u2014I was like 'We're a studio that [has] built our reputation on storytelling.'<br /> <br /> &quot;And I guess you want to do it justice. You want to take care of it. But taking over a project that had already been in development as well, that's such a tricky thing to take on. We are an original IP studio. The only way we're going to want to do this is if we are able to, basically, we'll take everything that's there and use as much as we can. But we don't just want to finish someone else's game.&quot;<br /> <br /> Paradox, apparently, agreed to this. But Pinchbeck says the &quot;tricky question&quot; was whether The Chinese Room's should herald its status as a sequel to Bloodlines 1, something he repeatedly discussed with one of Paradox's former producers. &quot;We used to sit there and have these planning sessions of 'how do we get them to not call it Bloodlines 2?' You can't make Bloodlines 2. There's not enough time. There's not enough money.&quot;<br /> <br /> Pinchbeck points out that the original Bloodlines came out at a &quot;really interesting period&quot; when games like Stalker and Shenmue were shooting for the moon in terms of roleplaying simulation. &quot;You could ship a really ambitious game that was full of bugs and holes, was totally flawed, but the ambition was really exciting.&quot;<br /> <br /> Pinchbeck says that &quot;you couldn't get away with&quot; that style of design now. &quot;Trying to recreate that magic in a different environment felt wrongheaded. No one would be happy. You wouldn't make people who love Bloodlines 1 happy and you wouldn't make people who didn't know about Bloodlines 1 happy, because they'd never get Bloodlines 2 and they'd always get a flawed game that was built too fast and with not enough money.&quot;<br /> <br /> To briefly interject, I'd point out that making an ambitious but broken RPG wasn't acceptable in 2004 either\u2014Bloodlines was a commercial failure that resulted in the death of Troika. Its reputation has been salvaged mainly through time and the absurd dedication of one German chemist.<br /> <br /> Nonetheless, Pinchbeck is correct that it's even less acceptable now than it was then. Hence, in a pitch that he says would make Bloodlines 1 fans elicit a &quot;psychic scream&quot;, Pinchbeck said to Paradox: &quot;We can't make Bloodlines 2, we can't make Skyrim, but we can make Dishonored. And if we look at something which is not an RPG and is not fully open world, but is really tightly focused and true to the mythos, and it's a good ride, we get a Bloodlines title out in the world.<br /> <br /> &quot;And then we started talking about saying, then 'what would the next big Bloodlines game look like after that, if that happened'?&quot; In other words, The Chinese Room tried to rework Bloodlines 2 as vampire Dishonored as a stepping stone to another Bloodlines game, perhaps Bloodlines 3 or, if The Chinese Room had its way, the true Bloodlines 2.<br /> <br /> Personally, I don't think The Chinese Room pulled off this plan of making vampire Dishonored either\u2014though you can see that DNA more clearly than you can Bloodlines 1. And I think Pinchbeck recognises this too, as he says that &quot;like every other game&quot; Bloodlines 2's development became a process of &quot;untangling an anaconda fuckball of competing priorities and what everybody wants and things like that&quot;.\u200b </div> </div> </div>The part I want to highlight here is that on one hand, Paradox desperately wanted to release something called Bloodlines 2 - but they had no realistic plan whatsoever to make that happen. Bloodlines 2 was supposed to be a bigger game and I can understand that any studio might be reluctant to agree to &quot;simply finish the work&quot; under those circumstances. There are all sorts of issues and challenges with making that happen. <br /> <br /> But then another baffling thing is that if Dan Pinchek is to be believed both TCR and well, I guess, some part of Paradox were aware that the way they were handling this would lead to issues if they were going to call the game Bloodlines 2... and nothing came of that. At least, I understand why Paradox leadership was so pessimistic in 2024. They had already been talking for over a year how calling the TCR-game &quot;Bloodlines 2&quot; is a bad idea.<br /> <br /> The way I think it makes sense is that ultimately the choices were between calling the TCR-game &quot;Bloodlines 2&quot; (obviously a bad idea) or telling your shareholders that Bloodlines 2 would be yet another canceled boondoggle of a game that Paradox had spent tens of millions of dollars on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-25T10:53:21-08:00","id":1555858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555841#post1555841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dan Pinchbeck, one of the cofounders of The Chinese Room (who has left The Chinese Room in 2023), was on a podcast talking about the development of Bloodlines 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Paradox has a history of finishing projects. Take from this what you will, but you can count on the fingers of one hand how many games they started to make and didn't finish. They may abandon franchises, but they'll bury a lot of money before they give up on an ongoing development.<br /> <br /> And that isn't a good thing. TCR was possibly unaware of just how stubborn Paradox is with names, or just couldn't pass on such a chance, but the fact remains that Paradox was willing to burn 60 million USD (actually 600 million Krona) instead of abandoning this project.<br /> <br /> What I know is that if he's saying they had not enough money for <i>Bloodlines 2</i>, then it's already probable that most of this money went to HL's try. Not necessarily to HL, but to their period at the helm of this project.<br /> <br /> More than once before Paradox launched a title they were unhappy with, just for the sake of seeing whatever they promised happen, and then turn their backs. We also have cases were said project was actually a commercial success, yet this didn't change Paradox's indifference to the results as it wasn't what they wanted.<br /> <br /> Everything in their regular behavior spells bad business.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-25T11:51:14-08:00","id":1555862,"title":"","content":"With Pinchbeck's comments in mind, I started to think about these bizarre, harsh comments from 2024 again. &quot;Bloodlines 2 is a dead end&quot;, &quot;If Bloodlines 3 will ever get made, it will be by someone else&quot; etc. With the context Dan provides, this now makes a lot more sense. The whole point of that was to loudly reject the idea of this released TCR-Bloodlines-2 being a &quot;stepping stone&quot; for a Bloodlines 3 which would be a true sequel to Bloodlines 1.<br /> <br /> I'm sure from TCR's perspective at the time that made sense. And I'm sure there were even people at Paradox that were happy to go along with that. Given the limitations for the TCR-version of Bloodlines 2 (both in terms of money and time), Bloodlines 2 can't be a true sequel. And if the goal is to make a true sequel to Bloodlines 1, why not make a Bloodlines 3? And maybe even rename this &quot;Bloodlines 2&quot; to make it clear that it's just a stepping stone. <br /> <br /> That's the developers point-of-view, though... I'm sure, other people at Paradox were probably having a heart-attack at the notion of a Bloodlines 3. Because I also think the majority of the 60 million dollars went to Hardsuit Labs side of the project. And this proposal essentially meant investing in three games - at least, in terms of money. Of course, all the work and money poured into the Hardsuit Labs was wasted. But this proposal was calling to finance the unfinished Hardsuit Labs version (which was essentially wasted), the TCR-Dishonored pseudo-&quot;Bloodlines 2&quot; and the much bigger true sequel &quot;Bloodlines 3&quot;.<br /> <br /> (I also could envision that &quot;If Bloodlines 3 will ever get made, it will be made by somebody else&quot; meant Paradox might hope to find somebody in the future who takes the Hardsuit Labs stuff and simply &quot;finishes the game&quot; as a cheap way to make another Bloodlines... well, good luck to them if that's what they're dreaming about...)<br /> <br /> But giving TCR neither enough money nor enough time to make a true sequel (which are both hallmarks of a bad publisher) while also being aware all along how much of a disappointment it would be to release this supposed &quot;stepping stone&quot; as just &quot;Bloodlines 2&quot; and while also being under a lot of pressure to release something called &quot;Bloodlines 2&quot;... I mean, this is like a perfect case-study of a publisher mismanaging a project. Paradox had managed to maneuver itself into a position where there were only bad options. Releasing this underfunded TCR-version called &quot;Bloodlines 2&quot; was simply the least bad option available to them. <br /> <br /> And it goes back to them not having learnt a thing from this. I highly doubt Iceflake studios will produce a console edition for Cities Skylines 2 or will magically redeem the project in the eyes of older fans in a speedy fashion. More likely, at some point Iceflake studios will tell Paradox that they can't fulfill their expectations because of the lack of time and money they're given by Paradox. And then once again, just as TCR was telling Paradox they won't be able to make a true sequel to Bloodlines 1, Paradox will have to face the fact that Iceflake studios can't magically improve Cities Skylines 2. Then once again Paradox will have to confront how much they've already spent on Cities Skylines 2, and as a result, they'll end up settling for mediocrity or worse. Because they're now too far along on this path to change course. And what consumers will end up experiencing is just more disappointment and frustration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-25T14:53:47-08:00","id":1555865,"title":"","content":"I think the most depressing part of Bloodlines 2 and its handling is that it very much is a game that has strong bones and could be, in its present state, the perfect sort of game for expansion. It has its issues but I would gladly play a University Commons Expansion, a amusement park, and other levels that would take advantage of the assets from Hardsuit Labs. The same for adding sidequests from the original game that were written by Mitsoda and Avellone. I would certainly pay money for these expansions.<br /> <br /> There's other areas they could be improving this game for with combat, saving, adding more ability to sneak past enemies to skip the arena fights, and more tweaks. There's plenty of places this game could be expanded.<br /> <br /> However, that's not what's going to happen.<br /> <br /> We have the planned expansions and they seem to be more Fabien-esque DLC where we jump in the shoes of Benny and Ysabella, two characters who are (let's understate matters) less than sympathetic. Phyre's story is done and they were really just getting started. The game feels very strongly like its been released as is as a form of damage control for all the previous struggles and it's just trying to get back as much investment as possible.<br /> <br /> I don't blame Paradox for this, unpopular opinion as that may be, because it's sixty million dollars for a AA game when they really could have had a AAA game for that amount of money. Pouring more resources into it at this point must feel like a sunk cost fallacy writ large. However, I feel this is a game that feels like its never going to be able to reach its full potential. I like it for what it is but its the vanilla shake in its current form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-25T21:52:08-08:00","id":1555873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555862#post1555862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because they're now too far along on this path to change course.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of the problem is that usually they're <i>not</i> too far along to change course except in their own minds.<br /> <br /> <i>Bloodlines 2</i> should have been scrapped as soon as the dev cost reached 50 million Krona without seemingly nearing completion. They spent 12 times this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555865#post1555865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the most depressing part of Bloodlines 2 and its handling is that it very much is a game that has strong bones and could be, in its present state, the perfect sort of game for expansion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it does seems to be the case.<br /> <br /> By the way, if they had simply accepted it isn't <i>Bloodlines 2</i> and had run TCR's project as its own thing, we could have a more accurate picture of the current game's production cost.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't call it just vanilla, it's plain unfinished, but it is a game someone can work with. It was definitely released as damage control, and a badly planned one at that, hence the AAA pricing.<br /> <br /> Sixty million USD isn't an actual AAA, though, and that's part of the problem. While AA games don't cost more than 5 m in the higher end, AAA begin at 100 m. They're serious business by serious companies, they get a lot of money and sell in the tens of million copies even at their price. Paradox wasn't ready for an AAA game and didn't really put an AAA investment here. This would be a rather weird case if the result could somehow make back its total cost.<br /> <br /> Do I blame Paradox? To a certain point, yes, even if we only focus on giving up on this game. Sunk-Cost fallacies are a complex thing that don't really apply to this case once the game is released (although I do agree it looks a lot like one). They fell for the S-C fallacy when they showered HL with maybe more than 500 million Krona, they did with a gusto. But now that the game is out, it's a new investment altogether. The DLCs don't have to recover the cost of the whole development, they have to recover only their own cost. Everything else is already said and done, the game is already a financial failure, the DLCs are not.<br /> <br /> That said, I think it's the most understandable bad decision they made through this whole ordeal. They want to retreat to the position of waiting for licensees, and as bad as they are at this strategy, it is certainly far safer, and they're not in a position to take risks anymore. So... yeah, that's that. The game will get whatever TCR can make for a year and then be done and buried. Anyone wanting to produce a <i>Bloodlines 3</i> will have to do so out of their own pockets even after convincing Paradox they deserve to use the name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-26T02:12:52-08:00","id":1555883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555873#post1555873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Part of the problem is that usually they're <i>not</i> too far along to change course except in their own minds.<br /> <br /> <i>Bloodlines 2</i> should have been scrapped as soon as the dev cost reached 50 million Krona without seemingly nearing completion. They spent 12 times this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, the original sin certainly was whatever had happened with Hardsuit Labs. But they decided to sever ties and look for a new developer. And I suspect they did that under the auspice of whoever would be going to pick up development would simply take the work of Hardsuit Labs and &quot;finish it&quot;. So, The Chinese Room come in - and here's the first point which should've caused a moment of self-reflection for Paradox. TCR tells them that they're not going to simply &quot;finish the job&quot; but rather, they want to do their own thing. This then leads to another weird decision from Paradox. They agree to let TCR do that - but they're not adjusting their expectations in terms of time and money. So then TCR comes back and tells them &quot;We neither have the time nor the money to produce a true sequel to Bloodlines 2. How about we do this little one as a stepping stone and Bloodlines 3 is the true sequel?&quot;. Another moment that demanded self-reflection. Instead, they just let things go ahead. And then only as this TCR version of Bloodlines 2 is nearly finished, that's when they became active and decided not to go with the plan from TCR and instead now the plan is &quot;We release this version of Bloodlines 2 and that's it for now.&quot;<br /> <br /> But looking back on that, I would say the make-or-break moment for Paradox should've been when TCR told them that they want to do their own thing and they wouldn't just &quot;finish what Hardsuit Labs did&quot;. Because obviously, the implication is clear that we're talking about a sort-of new project at that point. Or at least that's how one should've looked at that. But then Paradox was all caught up in making up for the deep black hole that Hardsuit Labs created and then all this back and forth about how to produce a &quot;true sequel&quot;... After everything, you could just go back and wonder about scrapping it sooner. Since Paradox ended up with the notion of &quot;Making a Bloodlines 3 seems like a bad idea.&quot;, why was it worth spending even more money on the TCR Bloodlines 2? Making a Bloodlines 3 isn't more or less unpalatable than making a Bloodlines 2, after all. Getting wet feet that late in the process certainly led to a less-than-ideal outcome. For example, if you had decided early on that making another Bloodlines wasn't what you wanted and knowing TCR wanted to do their own thing, you could've simply financed TCR to do just that but rename the project. And in regards to Bloodlines 2, well, I guess, scrapping it and eating shit was bound to happen at some point anyway, considering what happened with Hardsuit Labs.<br /> <br /> Instead, you got this half-hearted attempt at a Bloodlines 2 that lacked both time and money. And I think it's important how time was an impediment here as well. Originally, the release-date was supposed to be October 2024. The game-footage at the time made clear, though, that this wasn't realistic. And that's another bad thing a publisher can do: push for unrealistic release-dates. I doubt development on the game was aided by this pushiness. And then of course abandoning the idea of &quot;Bloodlines 2 as a stepping stone and Bloodlines 3 as the true sequel&quot; meant that Paradox now would release the TCR Bloodlines 2 while knowing that it was nowhere close to a &quot;true sequel&quot; (despite the name). I don't think this was exactly the most graceful way to handle this situation.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-26T10:27:06-08:00","id":1555887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555883#post1555883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think this was exactly the most graceful way to handle this situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Overall from a business perspective their greatest sin was to not scrap <i>Bloodlines 2</i> as a project sooner. It's not that the signs of problems came too late and they had no choice, the signs actually came pretty early and they fell hook, line and sinker for the Sink-Cost Fallacy. Which is, again, <i>something they did before</i>. Somehow they think backing down from a project is worse than wasting millions upon millions on it, despite that being something other companies in the entertainment industries do all the time.<br /> <br /> On top of that they have this problem with never truly revising their (already unrealistic from the get go) expectations.<br /> <br /> As I said before, they decided a long ago that this would be <i>Bloodlines 2</i>. And their problem is that they wouldn't settle for anything else no matter the cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-27T03:23:04-08:00","id":1555904,"title":"","content":"It's now official (via gamesindustry.biz): <a href=\"https://www.gamesindustry.biz/paradox-takes-37-million-write-down-after-vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2-misses-targets\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Paradox takes $37 million write-down after Vampire: The Masquerade - Bloodlines 2 misses targets&quot;</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Data from GameDiscoverCo suggests the game sold 121,500 copies on Steam, which would amount to net revenue of around $4 million. The game currently has &quot;mixed&quot; reviews on the platform and on Metacritic.<br /> <br /> CEO Frederik Wester took it on the chin. &quot;Vampire: The Masquerade - Bloodlines 2 is a strong vampire fantasy and we are pleased with the developers\u2019 work on the game,&quot; he said in a statement. &quot;We\u2019ve had high expectations for a long time, since we saw that it was a good game with a strong IP in a genre with a broad appeal. A month after release we can sadly see that sales do not match our projections, which necessitates the write-down.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The responsibility lies fully with us as the publisher. The game is outside of our core areas, in hindsight it is clear that this has made it difficult for us to gauge sales. Going forward, we focus our capital to our core segments and, at the same time, we\u2019ll evaluate how we best develop World of Darkness\u2019 strong brand catalogue in the future.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Well, I guess, it could've been worse... But then again, astonishing that they had higher expectations considering that they already knew what a challenge this game was up against by calling it Bloodlines 2. I also wouldn't say the issue Paradox has with working outside their core-genre is that they simply can't properly &quot;gauge sales&quot;. I think the issue is a bit bigger than that.<br /> <br /> And they've been talking about &quot;refocusing on our core-segment&quot; for over a year now. Sure, Europa Universalis V proves they can still produce grand strategy games that sell well and their whole &quot;deliver a nigh-infinite number of DLC&quot;-scheme is also still going well. But they still haven't been very clear in what they want to do with the WOD-IP now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-27T03:57:54-08:00","id":1555905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555904#post1555904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But they still haven't been very clear in what they want to do with the WOD-IP now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well if I was a betting man than it involve them selling off the IP sooner or later.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-27T11:01:57-08:00","id":1555913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.pcgamesn.com/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2/development-cost-write-down?fbclid=IwdGRjcAOVf1xjbGNrA5V_T2V4dG4DYWVtAjExAHNydGMGYXBwX2lkDDM1MDY4NTUzMTcyOAABHnCp7INLq0uSv-XyzPOO1U-v4Az3YlAMNT_KJ569Z9x5eOghmpZmN81Tl-vB_aem_yg0cf6_SkipKBvyBp1QriA\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.pcgamesn.com/wp-content/sites/pcgamesn/2025/11/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2-paradox-write-down-37-million-ceo-apology.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.pcgamesn.com/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2/development-cost-write-down?fbclid=IwdGRjcAOVf1xjbGNrA5V_T2V4dG4DYWVtAjExAHNydGMGYXBwX2lkDDM1MDY4NTUzMTcyOAABHnCp7INLq0uSv-XyzPOO1U-v4Az3YlAMNT_KJ569Z9x5eOghmpZmN81Tl-vB_aem_yg0cf6_SkipKBvyBp1QriA\" target=\"_blank\"> Bloodlines 2's disastrous $37 million write-down \"lies fully\" with Paradox, says its CEO, as the controversial VTM game flops </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.pcgamesn.com/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2/development-cost-write-down?fbclid=IwdGRjcAOVf1xjbGNrA5V_T2V4dG4DYWVtAjExAHNydGMGYXBwX2lkDDM1MDY4NTUzMTcyOAABHnCp7INLq0uSv-XyzPOO1U-v4Az3YlAMNT_KJ569Z9x5eOghmpZmN81Tl-vB_aem_yg0cf6_SkipKBvyBp1QriA\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.pcgamesn.com/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2/development-cost-write-down?fbclid=IwdGRjcAOVf1xjbGNrA5V_T2V4dG4DYWVtAjExAHNydGMGYXBwX2lkDDM1MDY4NTUzMTcyOAABHnCp7INLq0uSv-XyzPOO1U-v4Az3YlAMNT_KJ569Z9x5eOghmpZmN81Tl-vB_aem_yg0cf6_SkipKBvyBp1QriA </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> As Paradox writes down $37 million in development costs for Vampire The Masquerade Bloodlines 2, its CEO explains what went wrong. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Interesting article on this subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-27T13:02:58-08:00","id":1555917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555913#post1555913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://www.pcgamesn.com/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2/development-cost-write-down?fbclid=IwdGRjcAOVf1xjbGNrA5V_T2V4dG4DYWVtAjExAHNydGMGYXBwX2lkDDM1MDY4NTUzMTcyOAABHnCp7INLq0uSv-XyzPOO1U-v4Az3YlAMNT_KJ569Z9x5eOghmpZmN81Tl-vB_aem_yg0cf6_SkipKBvyBp1QriA\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.pcgamesn.com/vampire-the...kipKBvyBp1QriA</a><br /> <br /> Interesting article on this subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's incredibly depressing.<br /> <br /> I loved Bloodlines 2 and tried to get as much enthusiasm going for the game as possible. I even bought all of my friends copies of it for Christmas.<br /> <br /> It's sad this will be the end of vampire as an IP.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-27T14:18:03-08:00","id":1555924,"title":"","content":"The game had come out, so we had some estimates regarding sales. And the critical reception had been &quot;mixed&quot;. Bank analysts had been estimating how much money Paradox had spent on development. Everybody knew that Bloodlines 2's development had been a tumultuous mess. Then of course there was the podcast-interview with the Chinese Room founder who talked about the development in not very flattering terms...<br /> <br /> I mean, Paradox coming out and saying Bloodlines 2 didn't meet their expectations was one of the least-surprising events in this whole saga.<br /> <br /> Hopefully, it will lead to a sale because clearly, Paradox is neither capable nor (at this point) willing to utilize the WOD-IP for videogames. And really, it's just mostly about capability. Because there's nothing inherently wrong with the WOD-IP, of course. I still think this whole notion of &quot;Paradox are only good at a particular niche of videogames&quot; is ridiculous. They have the money. I get it that they started out with a particular niche but they were successful. So they have the money. And so why not hire people who <i>can </i>do the job?! Like making an RPG-videogame, for example. And the only reason you're not able to do that (<i>despite </i>having the money to do it) - is because there's something deeply wrong with your company. <br /> <br /> The worst thing that could happen is that Paradox is just gonna sit on it. And who knows where the whole &quot;revived White Wolf thing&quot; is gonna go from here. In the announcements, &quot;reviving White Wolf&quot; and releasing Bloodlines 2 were always uttered in the same breath. Never liked that. But then again, I had also been on the more skeptical side regarding Bloodlines 2 long before the &quot;revived White Wolf&quot; had been attached to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-27T14:56:53-08:00","id":1555926,"title":"","content":"What's sad is that we know for a fact that a great WoD game can be made. Forget Baldur's Gate. Wrath of the Righteous, Kingmaker, Divinity, all of them are great games.<br /> <br /> Why can't we have a top down adventures of a vampire coterie? A werewolf pack? If you want, make it set in Dark Ages, during War of Omens. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555917#post1555917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's incredibly depressing.<br /> <br /> I loved Bloodlines 2 and tried to get as much enthusiasm going for the game as possible. I even bought all of my friends copies of it for Christmas.<br /> <br /> It's sad this will be the end of vampire as an IP.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> Hey, could be worse. Game is at least functional, can be fun at times and story is decent enough. <br /> <br /> I will give it another decade or two before we get another attempt at AAA WoD game.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-27T15:23:09-08:00","id":1555927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Technoma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555926#post1555926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's sad is that we know for a fact that a great WoD game can be made. Forget Baldur's Gate. Wrath of the Righteous, Kingmaker, Divinity, all of them are great games.<br /> <br /> Why can't we have a top down adventures of a vampire coterie? A werewolf pack? If you want, make it set in Dark Ages, during War of Omens.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a shame they let the modded version of Crusader Kings go on when they should have offered to buy it and sell it.<br /> <br /> But they had an easy template to follow and couldn't make it work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hey, could be worse. Game is at least functional, can be fun at times and story is decent enough.<br /> <br /> I will give it another decade or two before we get another attempt at AAA WoD game.<br /> </div> </div> </div>I'm more pessimistic. Bloodlines was the most successful thing and it took decades to get fixed--and this won't ever have the same fanbase.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-27T15:36:31-08:00","id":1555928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555927#post1555927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was a shame they let the modded version of Crusader Kings go on when they should have offered to buy it and sell it.<br /> <br /> But they had an easy template to follow and couldn't make it work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aside from turning a really popular Crusader Kings mod into a full-fledged game (and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> is right in mentioning that as a natural idea for a WOD-game), I never understood why Paradox abandoned Star Trek: Infinite. Sure, the game got middling reviews and I'm sure both sales and critical reception didn't live up to expectations and I assume the Star Trek license-fees are pretty hefty... but c'mon, it's Star Trek! Grand Strategy is supposedly the one thing Paradox is good at and they got themselves the opportunity to produce &quot;Star Trek: The Grand Strategy Game&quot;. But then when it didn't become a huge success in the first year... Paradox simply gave up. It's the goddamn Star Trek IP! Why would you let that slip through your fingers?! And because they did give up, all they had in the end was a mediocre grand strategy game with lackluster sales...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-27T22:38:16-08:00","id":1555933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Technoma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555926#post1555926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I will give it another decade or two before we get another attempt at AAA WoD game.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Part of the issue is the AAA culture is currently imploding and bloodlines 1 wasnt a AAA game full stop.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-28T01:28:06-08:00","id":1555936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555917#post1555917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's incredibly depressing.<br /> <br /> I loved Bloodlines 2 and tried to get as much enthusiasm going for the game as possible. I even bought all of my friends copies of it for Christmas.<br /> <br /> It's sad this will be the end of vampire as an IP.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hold your horses. This isn't a small setback, but it isn't the end of the world, either, and WoD already literally survived the time of judgement before.<br /> <br /> A lot can happen from now on, but it simply shutting down for long isn't the most likely outcome.<br /> <br /> The game isn't half-bad, either. Far from what it should be, and I think your enthusiasm is incomprehensible, but it certainly has its merits, and while they won't reverse their loss, they'll most surely keep the IP in people's minds more than normal.<br /> <br /> Look at the common thread among the articles: people disliked this game, <i>but they really like the IP</i>. They <b><u>want</u></b> a well done VtM game. They don't blame the game's failures on setting or premises. They remember fondly the first game, they remember the TTRPG, they like the setting and want it to thrive.<br /> <br /> IP value is a weird thing. While the game certainly devalued it in Paradox's hands because they've shown they can't do much with it, it also gave the IP momentum and a presence in recent memory, and this is important.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555924#post1555924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still think this whole notion of &quot;Paradox are only good at a particular niche of videogames&quot; is ridiculous. They have the money. I get it that they started out with a particular niche but they were successful. So they have the money. And so why not hire people who <i>can </i>do the job?!</div> </div> </div> </div>So. While I think you're mostly correct, this is an important misconception.<br /> <br /> Making a game, or any other kind of business, isn't just a matter of having money and hiring people who know how to do it.<br /> <br /> It isn't obvious, but companies do a lot of work to get any project done. There are many parts to manage, goods and services to source, a lot of planning and projections to make, there's a lot of resources to allocate, there's marketing, other companies to deal with, like retailers or platforms, there's a lot of things, really.<br /> <br /> And those things <b>are</b> sensitive to what you're doing. Making an RPG or making a Strategy Game, that changes key details on all those moving parts, even if they remain mostly similar, details that can make or break a project. Even your accountant can have a hard time dealing with unfamiliar waters. So &quot;hiring the people who know&quot; means pretty much re-hiring your whole company, not just the devs, but up to your CEO.<br /> <br /> None of this excuses Paradox, as they <b>should know this</b>. A lot of their mistakes come precisely from working every project as if it was the projects they know how to handle. In a sense, they're not off the mark when the CEO says they couldn't gauge sales, this is literally one of many things they have to do and didn't really knew how to, even if this remark was actually just a veiled way to say it was the RPG market that doesn't make money, which is blatantly false. Paradox should have gauged first their know-how and tackled smaller projects to get the handle of things, they should have gotten consultants about each new niche and heard the advice from people who work on them, they should have accepted, in short, that there are things about games they don't know.<br /> <br /> They have a lot of problems, it goes far deeper than &quot;just&quot; not knowing how to make other games. But companies being good at some things and not others is definitely a thing, and in fact well known in the investment world.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Technoma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555926#post1555926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will give it another decade or two before we get another attempt at AAA WoD game.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was not an attempt at an AAA game, Paradox doesn't have this kind of cash. This was an overpriced AA that sucked at being AA.<br /> <br /> More important, though, going AAA isn't the point. Even going AA isn't necessary, although it's certainly good.<br /> <br /> What we need is competent people doing good games that aren't just glorified fanfics (even if eventually good fanfics). It may be <i>Vampire </i><i>Stardew Valley</i> for all I care. And a reliable flow of such people, not necessarily huge, but enough for us to expect a game every couple years or so.<br /> <br /> Despite Paradox's bet on it, <i>Bloodlines</i> as a franchise isn't by far the most important thing here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-28T07:27:45-08:00","id":1555938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555917#post1555917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's incredibly depressing.<br /> <br /> I loved Bloodlines 2 and tried to get as much enthusiasm going for the game as possible. I even bought all of my friends copies of it for Christmas.<br /> <br /> It's sad this will be the end of vampire as an IP.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>This doom and gloom talk is ridiculous.<br /> We\u2019re not fans of Paradox. We\u2019re not even fans of Onyx Path (mea culpa). We are fans of the World of fucking Darkness. Yes, WoD5 and Bloodlines 2 should have ignited a new renaissance for the IP. It diddnt, so what? Simple as.<br /> <br /> Still, things will continue. No valuable IP ever truly dies. Look up the tale about the town musicians of Bremen collected by Grimm. The message is optimistic and fits here. It suggests the possibility of sustainable solutions even for precarious situations or listen to the greats like Olliver Kahn, when he roughly translated says &quot;continue, always continue!&quot;.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is me, just forgot my PW and changed my email<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25163-crytash2","name":"Crytash2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25163_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-28T20:56:43-08:00","id":1555947,"title":"","content":"I think nostalgia has led people to forget that the original Bloodlines was also a commercial failure and a major factor in Troika going out of business. Nevertheless, the World of Darkness persisted. That perfect storm of zeitgeist and innovation that made the line as big (and maybe bigger in some areas) as Dungeons and Dragons isn't something that will likely ever be recaptured. This is doubly the case now that the World of Darkness is owned by a company beholden to stockholders, and the need for constant growth overcomes artistic decisions. It really is a shame that franchises like <i>Underworld</i> or <i>True Blood</i> reached audiences that the World of Darkness couldn't. The game is still alive and well. These forums, like almost all spaces on the internet, are a small, non-representative sample of the total population of World of Darkness enthusiasts, so it's easy for us to get caught up in an echo chamber of doom. The more I see other people playing in the same World of Darkness with interpretations and styles that are completely foreign to the game I started playing in 1992 (which is also very different than the game I am playing today), I know the franchise isn't going anywhere. Paradox can continue to fuck it up, but it will continue to exist in some form or another, I'm sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6423-higgipedia","name":"higgipedia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6423_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-29T11:00:50-08:00","id":1555954,"title":"","content":"So, to keep people abreast of what's going on with Paradox. So, after the announcement from Paradox about Bloodlines 2, plenty of videogame-outlets have written about it. Lots of talks of failure and Bloodlines 2 being called a &quot;flop&quot;. Well, but if you were to look at how the Paradox stock is doing and what people in the financial world are saying, it's quite the opposite. They're practically celebrating. The first weird sign was last Thursday when the news broke, one board member massively increased his shares in Paradox (it's not like I'm saying he potentially got tipped off about what was about to happen... insider-trading is a crime after all...). And now, <a href=\"https://www.marketscreener.com/news/danske-bank-upgrades-paradox-to-buy-citing-best-position-in-years-ce7d51dadc88f621\" target=\"_blank\">Danske Bank's recommendation shifted from hold to buy</a> when it comes to the Paradox stock. So why do they think that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Danske Bank has upgraded its recommendation for gaming company Paradox Interactive to &quot;buy&quot; (from &quot;hold&quot;) and raised its target price to 210 kronor (previously 180), according to a recent analysis.<br /> <br /> The upgrade comes on the heels of a successful launch for the highly anticipated Europa Universalis 5, with the game trending in line with the bank's quarterly estimates.<br /> <br /> &quot;Even more important is that the success of this title has likely paved the way for many more years of continued growth for the franchise and its games-as-a-service model,&quot; Danske Bank writes.<br /> <br /> The bank further notes that downloadable content (DLC) has been released for nearly all of Paradox's core games, and that these expansions appear to be performing well.<br /> <br /> At the same time, the expected write-down of Bloodlines 2 means that the company has finally moved past its &quot;junk period.&quot;<br /> <br /> This allows Paradox to look to the future, which, according to the bank, &quot;consists almost entirely of the genres where Paradox is the market leader: grand strategy and simulation games.&quot;<br /> <br /> In summary, Danske Bank concludes that the company, taking into account all recent successes, &quot;is now in the best position it has been in for a long time.&quot; </div> </div> </div>That doesn't mean Paradox can't chart their own course despite what these bank analysts are saying. But I think it will have an impact on Paradox that the money people call all their &quot;experiments&quot; with exploring different genres (other than grand strategy) over the last couple of years a &quot;junk period&quot;. And Paradox acquiring the WOD-IP, of course, and trying to publish games with it, would be part of this so-called &quot;junk period&quot;. So, the hope from the bank analysts appears to be that Paradox actually let Bloodlines 2 be the last WOD-game they're gonna publish. <br /> <br /> And of course, they're not entirely wrong. That whole scheme Paradox got going with their grand strategy games and the nigh-endless number of constant DLC-releases certainly rakes in a lot of money. I would have called it the greediest DLC-scheme in videogaming but Bethesda's new thing with &quot;paid mods&quot; is even worse, I think. But still, you can't get around the fact that Paradox has a &quot;games as a service&quot;-model that works.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, though, this feels like short-term-thinking \u00e0 la &quot;It works now, so let's just keep doing it and don't try anything else.&quot;. They're essentially pigeonholing themselves to be committed to just one thing if they go with the bank-analysts' advice. And I hear you, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> that it's about more than who you hire but Paradox has been at this for years. Clearly, though, whatever they're doing over and whoever's in charge over there - it's not working. So, either hire more people or fire/replace people who are there. And it's a challenge to get into multiple genres but the reward is that Paradox isn't just &quot;the company that does grand strategy games&quot; anymore. So that was an ambitious project but in the end, they simply haven't pulled it off.<br /> <br /> But they were right to be ambitious. Not just in the sense thatt hey'd be moving up in the world as a videogame company. But they'd be in a safer position, too. You never know when somebody might come along and simply do the same thing as Paradox with their grand-strategy-games - but better. <br /> <br /> But Paradox aren't entirely out of the woods yet. That 37 million dollar write-down is only part of the story and we're gonna get the whole story at the end of January when Paradox is obliged to release its Q4 2025 earnings report.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-29T20:40:04-08:00","id":1555967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555954#post1555954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But they were right to be ambitious. Not just in the sense thatt hey'd be moving up in the world as a videogame company. But they'd be in a safer position, too. You never know when somebody might come along and simply do the same thing as Paradox with their grand-strategy-games - but better.</div> </div> </div> </div>They were, and market analysts know this. Only making one type of game exposes them to serious market risks.<br /> <br /> Look at Nintendo. While its biggest share, Video Games answer for less than 60% of their profits. The other 40-something% is mainly toys and their original core business of regular playing cards.<br /> <br /> Diversifying is important and you're right on your analysis, and those people know that.<br /> <br /> But first, their analysis is indeed focused on the next year at most, this is the market standard, so for the near future things look more promising for Paradox as they stopped throwing money away in projects that see little return at the best of times.<br /> <br /> Second and more important, though, is that it can't be helped because Paradox is incompetent. This is a thing. This wasn't their &quot;junk period&quot; just because they were doing other stuff, but because they were doing it incompetently and burning a lot of money in the process. <i>Bloodlines 2</i> shouldn't have cost more than 5 million no matter what, or should have been a full fledged AAA game. Their forays in other genres was shock-full with costly failures. They kept a lot of side projects they devoted too much attention and money for how small they were, yet not enough to make something for real out of them.<br /> <br /> You keep saying what a healthy company should do, but the market simply accepted that Paradox isn't a healthy company for now. They're a good investment for the near future, while completely unprepared to deal with dangerous market changes (that happen sooner or later), but they already demonstrated that they simply can't change this and their attempt was a complete mess that cost too much without any return. It was a junk period because all they released as side projects was junk.<br /> <br /> How do you correct course when you don't know what's wrong with the current course? How do you expect Paradox to make the changes it needs when it has no clue what those changes are? How can them even hire the right people if they don't know who the right people are? They have demonstrated time and again that they didn't learn with their mistakes and simply repeated them <i>ad nauseam</i>. They need intervention, and if they get lucky they'll hire someone that can do it for them with the money they'll make in the next couple years doing their main stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T13:17:19-08:00","id":1555990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555967#post1555967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They were, and market analysts know this. Only making one type of game exposes them to serious market risks.<br /> <br /> Look at Nintendo. While its biggest share, Video Games answer for less than 60% of their profits. The other 40-something% is mainly toys and their original core business of regular playing cards.<br /> <br /> Diversifying is important and you're right on your analysis, and those people know that.<br /> <br /> But first, their analysis is indeed focused on the next year at most, this is the market standard, so for the near future things look more promising for Paradox as they stopped throwing money away in projects that see little return at the best of times.<br /> <br /> Second and more important, though, is that it can't be helped because Paradox is incompetent. This is a thing. This wasn't their &quot;junk period&quot; just because they were doing other stuff, but because they were doing it incompetently and burning a lot of money in the process. <i>Bloodlines 2</i> shouldn't have cost more than 5 million no matter what, or should have been a full fledged AAA game. Their forays in other genres was shock-full with costly failures. They kept a lot of side projects they devoted too much attention and money for how small they were, yet not enough to make something for real out of them.<br /> <br /> You keep saying what a healthy company should do, but the market simply accepted that Paradox isn't a healthy company for now. They're a good investment for the near future, while completely unprepared to deal with dangerous market changes (that happen sooner or later), but they already demonstrated that they simply can't change this and their attempt was a complete mess that cost too much without any return. It was a junk period because all they released as side projects was junk.<br /> <br /> How do you correct course when you don't know what's wrong with the current course? How do you expect Paradox to make the changes it needs when it has no clue what those changes are? How can them even hire the right people if they don't know who the right people are? They have demonstrated time and again that they didn't learn with their mistakes and simply repeated them <i>ad nauseam</i>. They need intervention, and if they get lucky they'll hire someone that can do it for them with the money they'll make in the next couple years doing their main stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I look at it is that you have the idea of what Paradox should've done in the past and what they should do now. So that's about hopes, mistakes in the past and idealistic visions of what they could achieve if everything goes right. Then there's the realistic perspective. What are the patterns of their behavior in the past and how much worse can this get if they stick to these patterns? And then there's the pessimistic take. This bad thing happened and not only are Paradox NOT learning from it, they're drawing a completely wrong conclusion from it. So we're about to go from bad to worse here. <br /> <br /> You're gonna move between these three but recent times have only shown that past patterns of behavior have stayed around. The optimistic scenario of Paradox requires change. And the worst thing about Paradox is that over the course of the last couple of years, they've never changed, they've never learned a goddamn thing from their missteps and failures. <br /> <br /> Of course, the finance people are only thinking short-term. They're probably just calling it the junk-period because they're butthurt about the Life By You write-off. The earnings for that quarter were like 90% less (!) than expected because of that. And I would defend Paradox for this experimentation in an effort to grow if they actually had learned anything from it. Well, anything aside from &quot;Just don't do it.&quot;, of course. That's not just banal but it would also mean Paradox had been throwing tens of millions of dollars into a black hole for no reason. Besides, do they really think these same losers who fucked it all up on the publishing-side won't eventually get their grubby little hands on these precious grand-strategy-games and (somehow) fuck that up, too? <br /> <br /> And the WOD-IP is caught up in all of this, of course. Selling it now is a bad idea and forgoing developments on WOD-related RPG-videogames seems like a wasted opportunity. So what now, then? Just publishing RPG-books for some chump change also seems like a waste. <br /> <br /> Just a terrible situation all around...<br /> <br /> __________________________________________________ _____________________<br /> <br /> I thought this video was also a good summary of Paradox's current troubles:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ccz05jIE0AA\" data-code=\"Ccz05jIE0AA\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Ccz05jIE0AA/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T14:05:41-08:00","id":1555999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555990#post1555990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I look at it is that you have the idea of what Paradox should've done in the past and what they should do now. So that's about hopes, mistakes in the past and idealistic visions of what they could achieve if everything goes right. Then there's the realistic perspective. What are the patterns of their behavior in the past and how much worse can this get if they stick to these patterns? And then there's the pessimistic take. This bad thing happened and not only are Paradox NOT learning from it, they're drawing a completely wrong conclusion from it. So we're about to go from bad to worse here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I won't say financial analysts aren't usually self-serving ideological capitalist pricks, they definitely are, but as far as market analysis goes they have to be realistic, because the other two takes, while fine for us, mean they lose money. Not only their money, but the money of their clients, as their analysis are a service.<br /> <br /> And here we have, as you pointed, Paradox's pattern. And I wouldn't say it's for the last 2 years, it has been for 10 years already. Their redeeming feature is that their star games make enough of a profit to cover for their astounding sequence of bad decisions on their many, many side projects.<br /> <br /> They didn't learn anything until now, and do seem to have taken the wrong conclusion here and there. So yeah, as an analyst I wouldn't say anything too different from what they did, Paradox should definitely change a lot of things, but I can't trust <i>your</i> money on them doing it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555990#post1555990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I would defend Paradox for this experimentation in an effort to grow if they actually had learned anything from it. Well, anything aside from &quot;Just don't do it.&quot;, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>Me too, and many other people in the finance sector would. In fact, if Paradox hires and actual business analyst to examine things <i>for them</i>, they'll probably defend such experiments. Their current narrow profile is a serious risk in the long run.<br /> <br /> But at this point &quot;Just don't do it.&quot; is pretty much the best we can reliably expect. It's terrible, but less terrible than to keep throwing all this money away for nothing at all because they're neither competent at doing other things nor capable at learning in the process.<br /> <br /> Well, I mean, there's at least one good thing: this money is actually going somewhere, so that's a social bonus, I guess? Each project means a couple years of employment for someone...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555990#post1555990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the WOD-IP is caught up in all of this, of course. Selling it now is a bad idea and forgoing developments on WOD-related RPG-videogames seems like a wasted opportunity. So what now, then? Just publishing RPG-books for some chump change also seems like a waste.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the last option is the most likely for the time being. As I said many times before, I'd focus on making a game with the IP that's actually within their niche, but keeping making books seems the next best option (far worse, but still less worse than the others). It beats making games they can't get right by their current pattern or just sitting upon it doing nothing.<br /> <br /> Selling now would be a terrible mistake as it would sell for a huge loss, although it would at least recover some of the investment for them to put to other uses, but I think they don't need the money so desperately and this IP can at the very least be sold at a more opportune time in the not-so-near future.<br /> <br /> Then again, Paradox has a history of terrible mistakes, so...\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-04T07:39:52-08:00","id":1556144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.pcgamesn.com/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2/interview-chinese-room-paradox\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.pcgamesn.com/wp-content/sites/pcgamesn/2025/11/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2-ex-chinese-room-co-founder-paradox-change-name.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.pcgamesn.com/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2/interview-chinese-room-paradox\" target=\"_blank\"> Chinese Room co-founder wanted Paradox to drop the 'Bloodlines 2' name, because \"no one would be happy\" with the final game </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.pcgamesn.com/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2/interview-chinese-room-paradox\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.pcgamesn.com/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2/interview-chinese-room-paradox </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Speaking on The Goth Boss Podcast, co-founder of The Chinese Room Dan Pinchbeck says Paradox should've ditched the 'Bloodlines 2' name. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> A deeper discussion of what happened from The Chinese Room's perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-21T16:29:17-08:00","id":1556882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>higgipedia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555947#post1555947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think nostalgia has led people to forget that the original Bloodlines was also a commercial failure and a major factor in Troika going out of business. Nevertheless, the World of Darkness persisted. That perfect storm of zeitgeist and innovation that made the line as big (and maybe bigger in some areas) as Dungeons and Dragons isn't something that will likely ever be recaptured. This is doubly the case now that the World of Darkness is owned by a company beholden to stockholders, and the need for constant growth overcomes artistic decisions. It really is a shame that franchises like <i>Underworld</i> or <i>True Blood</i> reached audiences that the World of Darkness couldn't. The game is still alive and well. These forums, like almost all spaces on the internet, are a small, non-representative sample of the total population of World of Darkness enthusiasts, so it's easy for us to get caught up in an echo chamber of doom. The more I see other people playing in the same World of Darkness with interpretations and styles that are completely foreign to the game I started playing in 1992 (which is also very different than the game I am playing today), I know the franchise isn't going anywhere. Paradox can continue to fuck it up, but it will continue to exist in some form or another, I'm sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see a lot of that mindset, but the reality is less hopeful.<br /> <br /> For a start, BL 1 and 2 are two different beasts, from two different birthplaces, appearing in two different gaming cultures.<br /> <br /> When BL 1 came into being, it was an adaptation of a niche IP (as in it was unknown to the video game audience, it was only preceded by redemption, a game with little clout back then). It also appeared in the 2000, when games were mostly bought physically, online spread of Fandom was a distant dream.<br /> <br /> Looking at BL2, the story is entirely different. BL 1 had massed over more than a decade a cult following, in fact I think a lot of people discovered the WOD thanks to it (I\u2019m amongs them).<br /> <br /> And let\u2019s be honest, it\u2019s mostly for that factor that paradox bought the wod IP. They were not going to gain money from new editions of the TTRPG. It was always about video games, and BL2 was always resented as the beach head of that attempt.<br /> <br /> Add to that the massive change in video game culture. For a start, it has become nearly entirely online, hype and reactions are constantly shared. And the hype for BL2 started as soon s it\u2019s original announcement. So it\u2019s release cannot be compared to a BL1 that release without much fanfare. BL2 was awaited.<br /> <br /> So the crash down is doubly damning, especially since, while Troika tried to make a game for some relatively obscure IP, paradox was trying to make the sequel to a classic for an audience that was waiting for a long time.<br /> <br /> And not only did they botched it, but they have no excuses. Troika had terrible executive issues, technical problems with the game engine, and ambitions too great for the ressources they had.<br /> <br /> Paradox had literally one job. Remake a BL with modernized graphics. And they failed at that.<br /> <br /> So honestly, it seems that the doom and gloom of the forum is on point. Paradox brought back the wod for a reason, and that reason failed. And it cost them massively.<br /> <br /> <br /> And it will have an impact on the IP. In fact, we already suffered it.<br /> <br /> Remember how OPP, following the success of the V20 lines decided to make their own V4? It was cut from us because paradox bought the IP for that sweet adaptation potential, and imposed the mess that was the V5.<br /> <br /> And when you look at the fact that the only correct V5 books are those done by OPP, we can see what was essentially stolen from us wod fans.<br /> <br /> That and the fact that Cofd was essentially killed to avoid competition with V5.<br /> <br /> And yet, all that bitter taste could have been compensated if paradox succeeded in it\u2019s promise to bring back the wod to the video game sphere. Now even that is over.<br /> <br /> <br /> So we end up with a dead Cofd line, a V5 constantly alternating between the tolerable and insultingly mediocre, a lost of failed or at best passable video games, and a spearhead games that is neither a good sequel to a classic of the 2000s, nor even a good game on is own.<br /> <br /> So yeah, the IP is essentially dead. At least during the interegnum between CCP and paradox, OPP brought the flame back to life. Now what can we expect? Following their massive loss these last few years, paradox announced they\u2019ll concentrate on their grand strategy genre, the only thing they haven\u2019t entirely screwed, so unless someone there has the genius Id of making a strategic wod games, the IP video game future is dead in the water. Add to that the catastrophe that was W5 and h5, and the future of the ttrpg seems bleak indeed.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-21T17:56:06-08:00","id":1556886,"title":"","content":"You're overlooking, for the ttrpg side of things, that to a video game company the size of Paradox, it costs basically a rounding error worth of budget to keep a ttrpg going, and even when successful, makes an amount of money that is a rounding error worth of budget (it's not like this game is D&amp;D big or has been even close for years and years and years, let's be real here). The ttrpg side of the WoD has always been a vanity project for them by those standards. They can keep it going as long as it satisfies whatever fannish urge some of the members of the company have to keep it going as far as whatever satisfaction they get out of being able to say &quot;I win&quot; as far as getting to set the direction of the WoD, resolve decades of fan arguments to their liking, and decide how vampire works (and if you think that hasn't been a part of things, I am going to point you to.. a loooot of the early dev and staff interviews being near verbatim that shit, and even Achilli's dev statements diving into shit like that. Only Jason Carl even made an effort towards not sounding like that, and he's gonezo). It's not worth underestimating how much personal satisfaction they get out of holding onto this stuff.<br /> <br /> I mean, I personally find V5 pretty godawful with a tiny handful of exceptions, but it's been <i>relatively</i> successful enough as a ttrpg to crank out books for the past 7ish years at this point. Sure, the back half of those books demonstrates being completely out of ideas for their core premise as far as doing all the things they mocked in the early days of V5 and said they would never do. And sure, their latest book is a slightly desperate and somewhat incompetent looking attempt to blatantly tie into ItV's resurgence in popularity that fits terribly into the current structure of their setting. But the books do still keep rolling along.<br /> <br /> Is it dead as a larger videogamey &quot;transmedia&quot; IP? Yeah. Can they just cling to it and keep churning out the ttrpg side of it at basically no real cost on a corporate level as long as it pleases their inner fanboy though? Absolutely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-21T18:17:28-08:00","id":1556887,"title":"","content":"Ha ha, you almost got me again, desire to add a detail that would have turned my post into spam due to editing it! Basically I mean, the current ttrpg gameline has its fanbase and all. I'm not one of them, but they certainly exist enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-21T22:03:55-08:00","id":1556894,"title":"","content":"Oh trust me, I was there back when the whole thing was announced with their &quot;one world of darkness&quot; pr\u00e9sentation. It was always clear they saw V5 as the ttrpg equivalent of &quot;I can fix her&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> In retrospective, all the signs of the disaster, at least for the ttrpg side of the story, were there already. I notably remember, I'm not sure if it was directly in the Q&amp;A following the presentation or in a follow-up interview, from Mark Rein Hagen, that Vtm drifted away from the origin al idea they had of the game, and that V5 was supposed to bring it back. Most probably speaking of the street level personnal horror focus. <br /> <br /> <br /> And even then I couldn't help but think, yeah, maybe mark, the success of the game also came from that drift. And that the game you originally envisioned wasn't what attracted most people to vtm. <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-22T02:07:49-08:00","id":1556896,"title":"","content":"the question is what DLC's are alredy in the pipe and may actually ready to drop, all developed on the Initial Budget?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28255-dropbear","name":"DropBear","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-22T22:30:00-08:00","id":1556931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1556886#post1556886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're overlooking, for the ttrpg side of things, that to a video game company the size of Paradox, it costs basically a rounding error worth of budget to keep a ttrpg going, and even when successful, makes an amount of money that is a rounding error worth of budget (it's not like this game is D&amp;D big or has been even close for years and years and years, let's be real here). The ttrpg side of the WoD has always been a vanity project for them by those standards.</div> </div> </div> </div>In practice, yes, it has come across as a vanity project. The reality, though, is that it is a missed opportunity in relation to IP development. RPG books are very unlikely to make a large profit in themselves, and certainly nowhere near as much as a successful series of videogames, but they function to engage your potential audiences (cheaply), build and test ideas (cheaply), and keep the IP ticking over (cheaply) whilst you consider ways of exploiting it. I don't think Paradox ever considered the World of Darkness from this viewpoint, unfortunately, which is something of a pity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-23T00:05:02-08:00","id":1556933,"title":"","content":"I think that treats Paradox a bit too much as a monolith. The CEO is a VtM fan, bought the IPs, and hired a team to revive White Wolf as a subsidiary as both a vanity project and to rebuild the public image of the IP's brand so core Paradox would have the building blocks in terms of tone, setting elements, themes, and so on to slot into more lucrative media expressions. The first group under Martin was very clearly in the position of getting to make their vanity project under the larger corporate goal the rest of the board wanted of a new IP to exploit.<br /> <br /> The board (at least based on what I could gleam from their English language shareholder statements in the past) never sounded passionate about the WoD as a group, and I doubt the next few reports are going to look good for the WoD IP if they even say something about it directly on record. With how BL2 landed, anyone on the board that was only tolerating Wester's little TTRPG vanity projects on the grounds of minimal cost regardless of outcome because they wanted some serious video game money out of it now has a lot less reasons to think they're going to see any return on that investment and that's going to influence how things go in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-23T23:13:18-08:00","id":1556950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1556882#post1556882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see a lot of that mindset, but the reality is less hopeful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that misses what the mindset in question means.<br /> <br /> Back in 2004 we had the decision to close the WoD completely, and 2 years later White Wolf was essentially dead. You can't get more hopeless than we were at the time, for all intents and purposes the WoD was dead. Yet years later we got V20, and then more.<br /> <br /> The IP is a thing that exists independently from Paradox. I won't deny that things will be bad for the time being, but the time being will pass. And unless a lot of things change drastically to a point where we can't access the old books never again (which will probably mean we have more pressing matters to attend than WoD), the game isn't really going anywhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1556894#post1556894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And even then I couldn't help but think, yeah, maybe mark, the success of the game also came from that drift. And that the game you originally envisioned wasn't what attracted most people to vtm.<br /> \u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I can tell, Mark is a smart guy, but he always had this tendency to think he's much smarter and more cultured than he actually is, and overall not being a very pleasant person to be around when you're not praising the very same things he likes.<br /> <br /> But even then I'd partially disagree, here. His original game was definitely what brought a lot of people, even with the later developments.<br /> <br /> The problem is more his notion of thematic purity and one right way of having fun. The setting grew to be what he envisioned and much more, but he can't accept it being more than he envisioned, as most of the additions are things he despises (the guy despises a lot of things, really). And in the end V5 was not his vision coming true, either, nor was his vision as pure as he thinks (which is normal).\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1556933#post1556933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that treats Paradox a bit too much as a monolith.</div> </div> </div> </div>A monolith and a static thing.<br /> <br /> I don't think they'll sell the IP soon because it isn't a great idea to do now, but vanity projects only go so far.<br /> <br /> BL2 is above all a testament to how much those things can cost money if left unsupervised, and that's when pragmatism takes hold.<br /> <br /> Maybe they'll keep releasing books for the pocket change, simply because it's a smart move. For personal satisfaction? I highly doubt anyone there is now in a position to insist on this, anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-23T23:34:06-08:00","id":1556951,"title":"","content":"Given they managed to bring in a former WotC VP who was very directly involved with the TTRPG side of D&amp;D this summer, I'm pretty sure there's at least one more shot and brad recovery the board has acceded too. I'm not sure what she can actually do to right the ship, but at the same time, there isn't exactly someone out there you can point to that could get the IP to where the board wants it to be. It sucks to be setup to fail, but I'm pretty sure they're compensate her well enough to finally prove that Paradox shouldn't be in the TTRPG business. I do doubt they're sell the IPs, but being more like CCP and leaving the IP in the hands of one solid third party studio to recover is the best they can do if they want to try another video game stab in a few years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-25T04:16:00-08:00","id":1556983,"title":"","content":"Didnt their last financial report say that they had like 100+ licenecies, the majority not announced. <br /> <br /> I have no idea why there is all this doom and gloom in this thread. I dont find it reflected in any outwards communication from Paradox themselves. <br /> <br /> I think people confuse Paradox plans for their computergames and how they view the license itself. <br /> <br /> They say have had a bitter leason on going outside their comfort zone in developing computer games. The key word is developing. I see nothing hinting at them not being happy letting others take the risk (development costs).<br /> <br /> My prediction is that we can safely expect the ebb of low budget games will not stop with Bloodlines 2. And it will not effect Renegades publishing of RPG books. <br /> <br /> If anything I think Fallouts outrageous success on Amazon makes alot of Paradox higher ups imagine dollar rain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27829-mallgoth","name":"Mallgoth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-25T14:17:55-08:00","id":1556996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mallgoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1556983#post1556983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didnt their last financial report say that they had like 100+ licenecies, the majority not announced.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a fairly meaningless figure. When you're looking at these sorts of documents, you have to remember that it's Paradox painting themselves in the best possible light to keep their shareholders happy, entice new investments, and not spook existing investors.<br /> <br /> Onyx Path is still a licensee in that group... which is just what Paradox gets for the Exalted books being made. I'm pretty sure that's a rounding error in Paradox's budget.<br /> <br /> Paradox is also been engaged with multiple rounds of divestment. They went on a buying spree (of which the WoD/CofD/Exalted were only a small piece of) of both IPs and smaller video game studios. A decade ago they were feeling very bullish about expanding their company; and that was before the was a video game bubble that happened during COVID (though fortunately that seems to be deflating rather than bursting). Well beyond Bloodlines 2, Paradox had already been scaling back everything that wasn't part of their core profit makers from ten years ago. They had a lot of really rough lessons in the fact that expanding the company takes more than having a lot of cash on hand and just hiring developers/studios with more experience but no experience working within Paradox's corporate culture.<br /> <br /> However, they still have a bunch of games they made, or haven't cancelled but are struggling with, but are promising to get out. And with the trimming, they've licensed out that work to other companies to take over what they can't do in-house. That's why the number by itself isn't really a positive thing that it could be; it's inflated by factors that have nothing to do with, &quot;people want to pay us to make products with our IP.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have no idea why there is all this doom and gloom in this thread. I dont find it reflected in any outwards communication from Paradox themselves. </div> </div> </div>Because some of us have decent experience reading between the lines when it comes to corporate statements, and it's not looking good. Paradox is in damage control because BL2 is a financial bomb.<br /> <br /> And as I've mentioned earlier in the thread, the leadership at Paradox has a fiduciary responsibility to their shareholders as a publicly traded company. Paradox's leadership has to be able to present sound investment based logic to their decision making, or the company could get mired in shareholder votes going against the current board. They can't just say, &quot;the WoD totally has value that will get all your money back and then get you the investment profits we said it would, trust us bros,&quot; even they kinda have to project that confidence anyway as they're trying to fix the problems going on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think people confuse Paradox plans for their computergames and how they view the license itself. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you mean. We all seem pretty clear that Paradox bought the IPs largely to generate revenues by licensing them out to other media companies; but making a TTRPG edition and making BL2 were always part of the plan to demonstrate that the brand still has value in 2025 to major license partners that could bring in more money than a hundred Onyx Paths could hope to do. Other companies aren't going to pay Paradox for the right to use the WoD brand if that's not going to increase their sales.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If anything I think Fallouts outrageous success on Amazon makes alot of Paradox higher ups imagine dollar rain. </div> </div> </div>No, it doesn't. They've been &quot;looking&quot; for a streaming deal pretty much from the start and don't have anything to show for it. The highers ups wish they could be salivating over that kind of partnership, but nobody seemed interested in making a VtM show before BL2 had a bad release. The industry factors haven't gotten better for such a deal now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-25T20:49:52-08:00","id":1557001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mallgoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1556983#post1556983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They say have had a bitter leason on going outside their comfort zone in developing computer games. The key word is developing. I see nothing hinting at them not being happy letting others take the risk (development costs).<br /> <br /> My prediction is that we can safely expect the ebb of low budget games will not stop with Bloodlines 2. And it will not effect Renegades publishing of RPG books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heavy Arms already said most of it, what I'd sort of add is that this is already what they've been doing for the last 10 years and it has consistently not worked.<br /> <br /> Sure, there's a good chance that we'll keep getting low budget light novels and mediocre books, but that's the optimistic scenario and I don't think many people here are thrilled with this prospect. While BL 2's failure wasn't unexpected, it was still the best shot at attracting interest from others to the IP, and to licensing from Paradox.<br /> <br /> It's less that we're gloomy because things are taking a turn to the worse (which may still be the case), and more that they'll stay at a low.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-26T12:47:07-08:00","id":1557010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1556950#post1556950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> As far as I can tell, Mark is a smart guy, but he always had this tendency to think he's much smarter and more cultured than he actually is, and overall not being a very pleasant person to be around when you're not praising the very same things he likes.<br /> <br /> But even then I'd partially disagree, here. His original game was definitely what brought a lot of people, even with the later developments.<br /> <br /> The problem is more his notion of thematic purity and one right way of having fun. The setting grew to be what he envisioned and much more, but he can't accept it being more than he envisioned, as most of the additions are things he despises (the guy despises a lot of things, really). And in the end V5 was not his vision coming true, either, nor was his vision as pure as he thinks (which is normal)..</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is interesting, my assumption historically is the puritan mindset arrived at 3rd with justin and mage. Mark throwing that....well....bollocks around is instructive. I know phils unpleasent about baddie play but is their anything im missing since im in error?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-26T13:38:24-08:00","id":1557011,"title":"","content":"I think the big thing to keep in mind around that context is that Mark RH's attitudes extended into the business practices of the company as he was the head of it; Justin was never the head of WW or of Paradox's WoD structure. The Wieck brothers basically had to stage an internal coup (I'm oversimplifying a lot here) to keep Mark from bankrupting the company, after that pushed to limit his power a bit the first time he almost bankrupted the company and they had to fix things.<br /> <br /> In my own personal, and thus anecdotal, experience Justin is actually a nice guy in person, and is fairly self aware of his social limitations and even how much of a One True Way-ist he was when he was handed VtM Revised. He has his personal justifications and doesn't necessarily think he was wrong on the fundamentals of a lot of what he said, but he at least knows in hindsight that he didn't communicate certain things well in the books.<br /> <br /> The various Revised era devs that have spoken about their time at WW back in the day always stress how much each game was it's own island. While it was never openly acrimonious, there were some strong opinions about what Revised should be, and each game line was largely free to go in its own direction until the ToJ decision was made. Putting Justin in charge of W5 was kinda odd because he never really worked on WtA as he and Ethan Skemp were the most vocally opposites on design philosophy; so it's not surprising W5 was so different from what preexisting WtA fans wanted (and who knows how much pressure Justin was under from above as Paradox seems to have exercised more control than WW did). This also goes into a much quieter thing where Mage Revised's team - even if a bit closer in ideas to Justin - felt like Justin poisoned the well a bit because the end point of the Mage metaplot shake-ups were quiet different from VtM's Revised metaplot, but the fans largely reacted as if both teams had the same intentions; the Mage revises stuff was not necessarily what Brucato would have done, but it was done with a lot more input from him than Justin bothered getting from his predecessors.<br /> <br /> All of which is to get to part of how V5 became so disjointed. Mark didn't like what Justin did even if the two of them would abstractly agree on far more than not, and both of their contributions to 5th edition has their very strong authorial tone present.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-26T17:45:27-08:00","id":1557016,"title":"","content":"I always find it somewhat hilarious that revised was absolutely the most judge you for playing it edition of vampire, to the point that Achilli's noted favourite Gehenna ending is the one that uses page space to explicitly say it would have been objectively better and more meaningful if you had never been playing vampire in the first place, and had been playing a game about mortals. <br /> <br /> I'm not kidding. Look it up in Wormwood.<br /> <br /> It was also hilarious because Revised was also the edition that ranged perhaps the most widely out of all of them, everything from repeated deep dives into international sect warfare to city books full o elders (Cairo), to whopping swaths of high end metaplot stuff. The end of the Transylvania Chronicles was a revised ed book with the players and their elder pcs stopping Saulot from starting WWIII. Yes, it was also the edition that did New York by Night, and had several city scale politics books, various street level things, a book just on havens, and what all have you, but again, it had range.<br /> <br /> It just haaaaated that it had range. Hated it so hard. Every time a book could find page space to tell you what a worthless shitty piece of trash you were for enjoying the game wrong and how the average vampire player was a gormless buffoon the developers had to protect the game from (this last bit is I kid you fucking not almost actual text in one of the books), it would absolutely use page space for it. &quot;Ha ha we were joking though&quot;. No, you weren't, and we knew you weren't. You just for whatever reason didn't have the power to completely change the game to your liking, only some parts of it.<br /> <br /> I think the apex for me was part 4 of the Giovanni adventure cycle where you suddenly had to play completely different, basically neonates, and the book lectured you on what an idiot you are to think you'd keep playing the same characters you were for the first three parts because playing characters who had over time earned becoming that powerful was for dumb dumbs who can't understand good gaming. I exaggerate, but not that much.<br /> <br /> Achilli may be a nice guy in person, but he has always had an adversarial attitude to his own audience, defends that attitude, hits a given game with a hammer from mechanics to setting until the end result reflects that attitude, and screams a vibe of failed novelist who is offended that you are getting your grubby nerd mits on his artistic masterpiece. Self awareness of that doesn't matter when he thinks he's justified anyway. And that level of puritanism (which again, he comes off as thinking is absolutely correct, and fuck, has said so online when talking about how um actually games should be narrow like Pendragon in what they let you do, in reference to Vampire 5th) helped V5 reach it's current &quot;shit, we're out of ideas, time to do everything we were previously calling stupid and impossible&quot; era.<br /> <br /> If he feels he didn't communicate certain things well in the books, it's hard for me to think he means that in any way other than the problem was more people should have agreed with what he was saying because of how right he is, not that there has ever been a problem with his ideas, his writing, or his developing, or his desire to have as restricted an audience as possible as long as they all agree with him.<br /> <br /> I say this by the way as someone that really heavily/seriously started playing VtM with Revised (and then went back to look at earlier books for being big into VtM at this point), and will always look back at revised with fondness for it being my gateway edition, as it were. I love that era. I love them books, warts and jank rules and all. But man, and lots of Revised fans will tell you this, there were a lot of times I loved it in spite of what the game was trying to do, not because of it, as it screamed into my ear like a petulant, snot nosed, crying, spoiled child &quot;NOOOO, YOU'RE DOING VAMPIRE WRONG! STOOOOOOP!&quot;<br /> <br /> V5 being so mechanically and narratively punitive to enforce how narrow and small it demands that it be, and a few moves in some of VtR definitely reflect a sometimes presence of some of the revised era writers and devs that seemed to have hated the game they were working on in that era, or at least that people had wide supportable options to play and experience it &quot;incorrectly&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\u2615","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-26T19:48:48-08:00","id":1557026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557010#post1557010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is interesting, my assumption historically is the puritan mindset arrived at 3rd with justin and mage. Mark throwing that....well....bollocks around is instructive. I know phils unpleasent about baddie play but is their anything im missing since im in error?</div> </div> </div> </div>While I can't state from personal experience, Mark is infamous for being a pretentious asshole of higher order. When he doesn't seem something as a superior art form, he derides it big time, and the people who like it. Monte Cook, for example, is said to have meet Mark in the early days of Vampire, and the reason he didn't work for White Wolf through the 90's was basically the terrible sin of liking D&amp;D. Cook got ridiculed and humiliated for liking D&amp;D by the guy who later officially added a weird dot in his own name as a &quot;statement to the meaningless of things&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, yeah. This puritan mindset about WoD was his to begin with. And while he was one of the main designers behind four or five of the gamelines, he mostly stayed within the first, defining books, as he despised the gonzo of the sourcebooks and supplements (because of course there was no gonzo on the first edition core books, the hypocrisy), and eventually left WW to go to Holywood, where he got a lot of trouble for still openly hating when people &quot;ruined his vision&quot;, and had a number of forays in making all sorts of games that all failed because apparently the world isn't prepared for his vision.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557016#post1557016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always find it somewhat hilarious that revised was absolutely the most judge you for playing it edition of vampire, to the point that Achilli's noted favourite Gehenna ending is the one that uses page space to explicitly say it would have been objectively better and more meaningful if you had never been playing vampire in the first place, and had been playing a game about mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet, as you said yourself, <i>Revised</i> covered a lot of ground, and it also had far more robust and coherent rules. Mark Rein\u2022Hagen (yes, until a few years ago his name had this weird dot in the middle, not a hyphen, because artistic reasons) instead defended that rules don't matter because anyone trying to use them to build a good character is playing wrong, and true players choose objectively worse options.<br /> <br /> <i>Revised</i> had more of a vitriol against badwrongfun because it had, in fact, a lot of ways to play it, a lot of elements to use, and a lot of legacy content to implement. So a lot of <i>canonical</i> badwrongfun for the purists. Mark didn't look as judging simply because his books usually precede the stuff he despises.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-28T10:20:45-08:00","id":1557060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_