ays to play it, a lot of elements to use, and a lot of legacy content to implement. So a lot of <i>canonical</i> badwrongfun for the purists. Mark didn't look as judging simply because his books usually precede the stuff he despises. </div> </div> </div>I still remember that the rather ruthlessly optimized sample characters in Shadow Lords Revised caused a little bit of a shit storm on the forums. When the author defended the stat allocations, it got a bit a stronger. But hey, if there are any characters that are probably going to be ruthlessly optimized, the Shadow Lords would probably be at the top of the list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-28T20:35:02-08:00","id":1557072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557016#post1557016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always find it somewhat hilarious that revised was absolutely the most judge you for playing it edition of vampire, to the point that Achilli's noted favourite Gehenna ending is the one that uses page space to explicitly say it would have been obje