ds that attitude, hits a given game with a hammer from mechanics to setting until the end result reflects that attitude, and screams a vibe of failed novelist who is offended that you are getting your grubby nerd mits on his artistic masterpiece. Self awareness of that doesn't matter when he thinks he's justified anyway. And that level of puritanism (which again, he comes off as thinking is absolutely correct, and fuck, has said so online when talking about how um actually games should be narrow like Pendragon in what they let you do, in reference to Vampire 5th) helped V5 reach it's current &quot;shit, we're out of ideas, time to do everything we were previously calling stupid and impossible&quot; era.<br /> <br /> If he feels he didn't communicate certain things well in the books, it's hard for me to think he means that in any way other than the problem was more people should have agreed with what he was saying because of how right he is, not that there has ever been a problem with his ideas, his writing, or his developing, or his desire to have as restricted an audience as possible as long as they all agree with him.<br /> <br /> I say this by the way as someone that really heavily/seriously started playing VtM with Revised (and then went back to look at earlier books for being big into VtM at this point), and will always look back at revised with fondness for it being my gateway edition, as it were. I love that era. I love them books, warts and jank rules and all. But man, and lots of Revised fans will tell you this, there were a lot of times I loved it in spite of what the game was trying to do, not because of it, as it screamed into my ear like a petulant, snot nosed, crying, spoiled child &quot;NOOOO, YOU'RE DOING VAMPIRE WRONG! STOOOOOOP!&quot;<br /> <br /> V5 being so mechanically and narratively punitive to enforce how narrow and small it demands that it be, and a few moves in some of VtR definitely reflect a sometimes presence of some of the revised era writers and devs that seemed to have hated the game they were working on in that era, or at least that people had wide supportable options to play and experience it &quot;incorrectly&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12141\" data-vbnamecard=\"12141\">MarkK</a>... I fully agree with your posted analysis about the so-called &quot;puritans,&quot; with it being so poignant that it has actually awakened me from &quot;torpor&quot; so to speak. It was just so strikingly beautiful, brilliantly summarized, and just rapaciously inspiring of a post.. that I had to just wake up and give my own quarter to this piece!<br /> <br /> The problem with the puritans (in my opinion of course), is that they're almost all horrible at creative endeavors, and daring to be further bold, just terrible at understanding what made Classic World of Darkness so interesting. I have more of an admittedly neophyte perspective to preface, as I'm only &quot;older&quot; GEN Z and wasn't around and kicking when the classic era was still in full motion.<br /> <br /> The ability of choice of how to run and interact with the world, is a staple of what an RPG should be. Though that's not to imply that mitigation of that aspect, when trying to incur a certain atmosphere or game logic in concert with metaplot - i.e. generations with Masquerade, in contrast with the fluctuating potency of Requiem; where Masquerade is about power lying in the eldest, wherein the young most plot to subsume (diablerize) such elders if they wish to truly ascend to the highest point of Kindred society, Requiem is simply about just waiting long enough for you to get that power and nothing else - said mitigation is only really good when it's done carefully and emplaced at near-perfect places of design (&quot;near,&quot; because chasing perfection shouldn't be the point).<br /> <br /> The puritanical branch of White Wolf Writers in vivid contrast, whether old or new, think they've actually achieved orchestrated pure artistry by emphasizing the &quot;human&quot; or &quot;street level&quot; (the latter playstyle I've come to abhor because how it was used to break Masquerade, then the other games) and, in the same breadth, by mitigating global scale, outsized epic plots, and supernatural grand strategy; that they have kept and/or &quot;saved&quot; World of Darkness.. when all they have done is completely, and inequivalently, destroyed it.<br /> <br /> In an effort to be &quot;grounded&quot; (when ironically most of their implementations have been completely nonsensical in the greater scheme of oWoD itself) they have essentially become an extreme reverse of the so-called &quot;trenchcoat munchkin katana&quot; style that they have so despised; YA-tier yuppie posers, who only bare to have the most limited perception of media outside of YA, and think every other genre is &quot;silly,&quot; when in actuality most of YA is undetailed and surface level trash (which WoD has unfortunately aped due to the horrible writing and lack of care with this edition).<br /> <br /> This is very evident with how the non-VTM X5 titles were dealt with. Whilst V5 had a lot of lorebreaking retcons, they could remain retcons as such because the writers at least somewhat played VTM or some iterations based on it (Requiem) somewhat knew what they were doing; but it's very apparent that they did not understand Reckoning or Apocalypse, at all. From the Imbued being removed from their literal main game to Werewolf being a complete erasure-baring reboot (with the absolute worst cardinal abolishment in Werewolf being the de-emphasized connection with the Umbra.. in a game outside of the Werewolves, is primarily about spirits), you can tell what they remove and what they keep follow a pattern (in overall relation to what they perceived as &quot;grounded&quot; and how they excise specific aspects too &quot;high-octane gonzo&quot; or &quot;too grognard&quot; (term-of-phase many along the puritanical prescribe to fans of Classic World of Darkness))<br /> <br /> For example, to circle back to Masquerade, the Tremere and the Lasombra:<br /> <br /> The Tremere were targeted for removal by the puritanicals due to many factors;<br /> <br /> 1) they kept the Camarilla too strong. It has become obvious these revised-era puritanicals favored the Anarchs over the former, so they fabricated that contrived SI aerial missile assault on the canonically teleporting blood magically cloaked Vienna Chantry, wherein subsequently the major Clan flaw of Tremere of loyalty to the Seven became non-existent and now Anarch Tremere are (un)surprisingly now possible! Not only Anarch Tremere. How convenient and completely grounded, and of no way of an artificial contrivance of logic!<br /> <br /> 2) while I never really found the Tremere interesting, it's well apparent that many of the non-puritanicals of VTM (I'll henceforth prescribe them as the &quot;gonzo-radicalists&quot;) liked the Tremere because of their extended granular powerset in the form of Thaumaturgy. So many Paths and Rituals to them, it was honestly a beautiful sight; a problem for the puritcanicals, however, because such a thing was of course &quot;badwrongfun.&quot; But on another route of circulation, the puritanicals liked the IDEA of Thaumaturgy and/or (now generically parlanced as) &quot;Blood Sorcery.&quot; The solution? What I mentioned they already did in the first point. Two birds with one stone (in the overall tangent scheme of &quot;streamline&quot; game design philosophy); remove a &quot;problematic&quot; &quot;overcomplexitied&quot; perceived &quot;munchkin-like&quot; Discipline and co-opt / mutate a power to be &quot;defanged&quot; so to speak, to be more palpable to the arbitrariness of the puritans (and their small unimaginative audience).<br /> <br /> Such as thing was not exclusive to the Tremere, with Tzimisce being burdened by this with the removal of Vicissitude and Serpentis with the Followers of Set (now Abrahamicized to the so-called &quot;Ministry&quot;: which on another brocade, being that of a means to de-emphasize their connection with Egypt / North Africa from the game. You can tell that these writers adhered VERY heavily to the particular piece of advice of only &quot;writing what you know&quot; instead of having the bravery to research and implement respectfully. But no, just metaphorically Christianize than put in effort to what the former actual good writers, with limited research abilities of the 90's, at least tried to do). Also not to forget about Necromancy and the erasure of its Paths, along with its absolute hamfistery of so-called &quot;amalgamation&quot; with Obtenebration...<br /> <br /> And speaking of Obtenebration, now the Lasombra:<br /> <br /> The major thing wrong with, and an overall insight to how the X5 writers write, can be seen with the Lasombra defection to the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> It's no secret, from what I've read in the past, is that many of the puritanicals LOVED the Lasombra, but detested the fact that they were a part of the Sabbat; a faction many loved and played by gonzo-radicalists, who loved the vampiric action-oriented pack mentality of the Sabbat, further interposed by the semblances of highly inverted Catholicism that was horizontally transported into the Sabbat primarily by said Lasombra. Along with the Tzimisce, the Sabbat was the creation of these two clans. So many losses and gains, honor, pride, and power were vested into the Sabbat by the Lasombra. It was a common informal view that, with the Lasombra and the Venture rivalry of who were the true rulers of the night were; that in course these two organizations heavily vanguarded by them, being that the Camarilla and the Sabbat; it's against all penultimate logic for how their defection came to be. Against the Vaulderie, against the Sabbat Inquistion, and just to tear down everything they've built.. and to then join the Camarilla, to be under the suzerainty of Clan Venture..<br /> <br /> ...it's just pure ham-fistery of the highest order.<br /> <br /> And like I touched on before, their care for the Lasombra is equivalent to what I broached on before; just pure surface level understanding, especially in regards to how they excised and retconned Obteneberation (though it is possible that the puritanicals DID understand it, but it veered too close to &quot;badwrongfun&quot; which is why it is the state that it's in with V5).<br /> <br /> The puritanicals talk about groundness, but paradoxically don't care about internal world logic or good writing to get to where they &quot;want&quot; the World of Darkness. They either want it to be more inline with CofD (which decidedly has not worked at all, wherein many fans of the latter have not switched over at all, just lamenting at the fact of no more CofD content and just turning off the former who really don't like the direction of the franchise) or casted into a way of mundanity that even becomes illogical<br /> <br /> They talk about &quot;street level&quot; and how such things preclude to mean &quot;weakness&quot; when I'm very sure most of them don't know about the actual streets, and how complex in halls the of power such places can be (in at least into regards of how many criminal organizations and gangs have historically (and at the present) gained power from such areas, and subsequently and almost always have gone onto exert global-sized influence across the stage). The most logical focal rise from a continued &quot;street level&quot; paradigm, in the context of vampires, will always eventually evolve to the epicness of Classic World of Darkness. They are immortal vampires, ones with (before V5) specialized powers determinant to their lineage, that allowed them to dominate and indirectly rule the vast majority of mankind from the shadows. This even extends to the lowest of Kindred in the hierarchy: high-gen Vampires, largely due in part from said features.<br /> <br /> If even mortal organizations from the streets can eventually grow to global, and if not that, interstate organizations, you can bet Vampires would do so such as well. And with that at a crescendo, the view of the gonzo-radicalists is the one that makes sense; that the epic high supernatural shadowplays of Classic Masquerade is one that actually is the one more &quot;grounded&quot; than whatever the puritanicals are trying to achieve with X5.<br /> <br /> And like you said before, to put it simply, they just hate the material of WoD. If not Vampire (which I focused on the most, as not to derail from the fact that this is the VtM subforum). Look at how they've treated HtR and WtA. Apocalypse is the worst offense, but I haven't spoken about it the most, because the clarity for how badly it was done is way more apparent. If they cared, they would have only MINIMALLY improved on spotty material (not even retcons in the sense of &quot;true&quot; retcons; merely slight adjustments for actual spotty material or general incongruities) and try to devise ways to continue the overall oWoD metaplot, post a scenario where &quot;Time of Judgment&quot; was merely a spinoff. But no, Imbued were removed and the Garou finally &quot;lost&quot; the war (but they're decided not Garou at all). Kinfolk were removed and now Garou can breed together with no consequences, breaking a MAJOR plot component of Apocalypse and the Umbra of all things was made to be more obscured... to a society that's supposed to be steeped and aware of many aspects of it, inherently nebulous as such a dimension is.<br /> <br /> I honestly think they made the Umbra more obscure in W5, is because it was too complicated and fell under the &quot;streamline&quot; modus operandi of the puritanicals. Such a thing was done in Revised Mage with the Avatar Storm, so to see it aped in WtA when the &quot;Fianna-is-just-a-word&quot; man got his hands on it, makes it clear on why such a case came to be.. EDIT: (VtM isn't even my favorite gameline, with such an honor being preceded toward Wraith and Apocalypse.. hench my avatar, I just love ghost, spirits, mindform entities, extradimensional creatures, etc. Such entities are inherently highly complex, which is something the puritanicals don't like; which I found interesting, considering the more &quot;groundness&quot; you try to seek, the more complex you have to be to capture such an atmosphere and resonance. Streamlining is an anathema to that.)<br /> <br /> Anyways its late now and I've spent hours on this essay. Most of it was spitballed tangets that I wanted to get down, but it's distracting me from my actual personal writing.. damn, another day wasted.. I hate procrastination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 12-28-2025, 11:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-29T00:55:25-08:00","id":1557073,"title":"","content":"OK, I think this has gotten pretty far from helping to clarify the impact of hiring specific old school WW creatives to work on WoD5. We might be &quot;on topic&quot; for the broad forum, but this isn't a thread for all of this. It's also getting from beyond some minor snide jabs (though to be clear, largely at things done over 25 years ago), into a whole essay about design mentalities in TTRPG creators/developers/etc.<br /> <br /> First, a bit of a pet peeve: lets not call them puritans. In English at least, a puritan is a member of one of the Puritan movements of Protestant Christianity. While the adjective puritanical does come from deriding people for acting like the Puritans, the noun didn't acquire the same dual use. If people are really desperate for a label why don't we use one that actually communicates the problem. The attitude that got Justin so unpopular back in 1999 was that he's a prescriptivist. That he, he thinks there are &quot;correct&quot; and &quot;incorrect&quot; ways to play a TTRPG internal to the game (as opposed to violations of social norms like cheating your dice rolls, mistreating other players, etc. which are incorrect ways to play any game). It's also a term that doesn't run afoul of what happens when the creator of a game feels that way about it. None of us here might give a shit about how Mark RH feels is the proper way to play VtM, but it's hard to consider him puritanical for having a very narrow idea of what that is since he created it in it's &quot;pure&quot; original form before other people tampered with it into something else (that was, after all kinda the whole point of Puritanism: to reform Christianity to its &quot;proper&quot; &quot;pure&quot; form, not to just recreate the &quot;mistakes&quot; of the Catholics but with the King in charge instead of the Pope). Prescriptive thinking is still a perfectly appropriate label for his comments on the matter since we get to play the game however we want and no prescriptivist can do more than fume about it while we go have fun.<br /> <br /> And lets face it, prescriptivism is way more common in TTRPG creatives than most of us as fans would like to admit. It's an inevitable side effect of having a creative vision, and the drive to actualize it into a game. People make games to be played a specific way, because that's what they're designing and what we're paying them to do. I've listened to and read enough Steve Jackson to know that &quot;universal&quot; RPG makers are just as subject to this as people that make highly bespoke indie games. What pisses us of isn't the idea that the people that made the games designed them with specific game play loops in mind (we actually love that, and I'd argue that W5 and H5 suffer heavily from Justin not really caring as much about that and just making Paradox happy with core books before he moved on to the next job he had lined up, rather than too much prescriptivist mentality), but the badwrongfun push back when people are having fun playing the game differently. A designer without a solid concept of an &quot;ideal&quot; version of their game and how it should be played is on that's going to make an incoherent mess because that ideal is what you need to judge the rest of the product on.<br /> <br /> So, to get back to Paradox: this is basically Paradox's problem with the TTRPG books. They hire loudly vocal prescriptivists because they assume that confidence and history with the product means vision, drive, and so on that consumers will follow (and they really don't care if those are old gamers coming back or new ones, a sale is a sale, and whether we're talking Bloodlines 2 or Hunter the Reckoning, the labels are always less important than having a qualify product that people actually want). They're not thinking &quot;hey, when was the last time Mark made... anything... for a TTRPG that really spoke to younger and newer players?&quot; or &quot;Why didn't the CofD start really get a strong identity as its own game with its own dedicated fans instead feeling like the late Revised WW authors rebooting the WoD until after guys like Justin left?&quot; and probably most importantly I'm unconvinced anyone at the company ever really asked, &quot;Is Martin making VtM for Martin, or for the widest audience so VtM can reclaim a spot within the cultural discussion?&quot; The point isn't ad hominem put downs of people because of a specific design mentality, but thinking about what the right design mentality is for what the company wants out of all this; a popular enough IP to license for lots of profit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-29T00:56:30-08:00","id":1557074,"title":"","content":"Well on W5 there has been some push back in the form of WtE whose goal is to address the problems with elements of the past editions while trying to bring them forward (well not conically since the default time fame is the late 80's but you get the gist).<br /> <br /> Like the team behind it has compiled at least 300 gifts for the first (of five) WtE Books and even promise some integration with W5 just so St's could bring some elements to the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-29T02:38:19-08:00","id":1557079,"title":"","content":"To come back to Paradox as a business. The whole point of buying the WOD-IP was that it was part of a growth-strategy, to expand beyond their core-games (all the grand strategy stuff). And at this point, it's clear that Paradox's management has failed. <br /> <br /> Life by You is probably the epitome of that failure. Paradox controlled everything. They chose the project: A Sims-like life-simulator. They chose the devs. They even created a new studio just for this game. They gave the project time. This thing had been years in development. They even gave it a huge budget (for an AA-game) with 20 million dollars. But then it all came crushing down. Game cancelled and 20 million flushed down the drain. Just like that. <br /> <br /> And the 37 million dollar write-down for Bloodlines 2 is less about a game worth 37 million dollars failing but rather it's the bill Paradox handed itself with all the chaos and mismanagement of the game's development. It would've taken a miracle for the game to overcome that in the end. <br /> <br /> The next big event for Paradox as a company will be late January when they'll release their earnings-report for Q4 2025 (that future report and all the past ones can be found <a href=\"https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/investors/financial-reports\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>). Their current strategy of just doing their core-games (strategy games) for the foreseeable future might keep costs down but it also will show that Paradox won't have the growth-potential investors might want. And so when it comes to Paradox owning the WOD-IP, I think there's the possibility of Paradox selling it because they just want to focus on their core-games. But depending on how bad this Q4-report might turn out to be combined with this retreat to a very conservative focus on their strategy games, I think another possible future scenario for Paradox might be for someone bigger to buy the company. Someone like Tencent (that have already invested a bit in the company) or Microsoft. And who knows what will happen with the WOD-IP once huge companies like that get a hold of it... <br /> <br /> In my opinion, the whole book-side of the WOD-IP, this whole drive to do WOD5E, has just ended up being another endeavor that lines up perfectly with Paradox's wider performance over the last couple of years. Overconfident, ambitious beginnings, huge expectations and promises... And it all just devolved into a mismanaged, chaotic mess that hasn't gone anywhere. Things didn't live up to expectations, promises weren't fulfilled and in the end, it all feels like more trouble than it's worth. Because what's even the point of WOD5E books at the moment? You can have Renegade churn out supplements for V5, W5 and H5 for the rest of time, I guess but since that's all they're allowed to do, the whole thing feels like a road to nowhere at this point. They revived White Wolf - only to immediately link it to Bloodlines 2 which turned into a financial failure. Just yet another bad decision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-29T03:00:50-08:00","id":1557082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557073#post1557073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prescriptive thinking is still a perfectly appropriate label for his comments on the matter since we get to play the game however we want and no prescriptivist can do more than fume about it while we go have fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the thing. As it turns out, they can. &quot;No one is coming to take away your books&quot; and &quot;no one is kicking down the door to tell you how to play&quot; are the usual statements put forth in response to what, sure, let's call it prescriptivism then, gets called out for in its impact. But they elide over the actual problems, and also why this kind of thing can generate such ill will when inserted in places it previously didn't really exist.<br /> <br /> When we pay for ttrpg books, we are in part paying for a support service because we don't have the time/inclination/juice to just create our own game, rules, what have you, and especially in an increasing age of gaming groups forming via online grab bags of strangers structure, an actual published game is the easiest medium to organize them towards doing ttrpg stuffs, as it were. It's the most viably direct route to the fun/catharsis/Aristotle's theories about how to safely experience emotions you can't otherwise, or whatever all else someone gets out of doing the ttrpg thing.<br /> <br /> If the game ceases to support playing a certain way or indeed goes so far as to make playing a certain way such a punitive hill to climb that you might as well not even bother, then the simple result is that the game gets less use out of any way besides what it encourages. For example, if Giovanni Chronicles 4 gives you dead zero nothing to help you play or run in accordance with the first three parts of the series but you still wanted to do that, you either now have to, as a GM, pull an entire adventure out of your ass, or, as a player, try to convince your GM and gaming group to pull an entire adventure out of their ass. Past a certain point of devs narrowing the crap out of a gameline from how you were using it, you're throwing away time and money on a game that not only doesn't want you to be playing it, it's taking, for instance in V5 especially, dedicated measures to ensure that vibe. Past a certain point, you have to wonder what the hell are you doing here, you don't belong here, you don't belong here (and the devs have definitely been vigorously suggesting you are totally a creep, you are indeed a weirdo). Past a certain point of lack of support, a game will mostly be a means to form groups for the way it is supported.<br /> <br /> And the thing of it is, being real, VtM successfully sustained 4 entire editions with no really deep prescriptivism beyond &quot;this is a game about playing Vampires in a darkly themed lore rich setting based off the modern world, in which there are a variety of ways to engage with the experience of that setting&quot;. Yeah, revised hated your guts for that being the case if that was what you were into, that range of play, but as myself and others noted, it could only sometimes try to actively get in your way about that. And yet lots of people enjoyed having tangible support for lots of ways to play make believe about vampires, or 4 entire editions of VtM would not have existed to have let them do that.<br /> <br /> To be topical about Paradox and the state of vampire the masquerade, V5 went all in on prescriptivism by contrast, completely indulging its devs to go hog wild with prescriptivism. And while you can search my posts for me repeatedly noting that V5 has certainly found a fanbase for doing so for the past 7ish years, we have in the end come to the flaw of Justin Achilli style prescriptivism, or MRH's, or whoever. The game ran out of ideas. The game used up all the runway its narrow little approach gave it, and is now doing something that I can certainly note anecdotally is giving a number of V5 fans fits, and more objectively point to various staff and dev statements in the past for sheer sharp contrast with the now.<br /> <br /> As I've said, it's lately putting out books that fly wildly in the face of its years of repeated mission statements, open derisions, promotional campaigns that made.. choices... and even in book material. The game is becoming disjointed and contradictory on itself as we get books about high scale plot, about romance and fucking, about playing older vampires, books that are nothing but grab bags of powers, books working in bloodlines that are now getting significant enough treatment to show up with dedicated named sections in promoted previews as if to say &quot;no no, this book is still usable for you, Salubri players!&quot; (which is ironic and hilarious for this being some of the most attention in modern era games the Salubri have received outside of Lore of the Clans in V20), books that make nonsense out of the Second Inquisition because ItV is popular again. It doesn't come off as the game having range this time so much as the game getting desperate and almost random in the face of the identity it tried to ground itself in, successfully or not. And that's because of, even in comparison to revised, how hard it tried for so long to do the opposite. Again, 7ish year old gameline. The people who came in new in 2018? Y'all getting older, soon you will be as decrepit as the rest of us! *makes eeerie aged finger waggling gestures, then has to go take tylenol arthritis for my fingers hurting from connective tissue disorder*<br /> <br /> By contrast, 1st edition VtM almost immediately branched out in all kinds of ways, right after the corebook really, and 3 more editions kept that more open approach going, even when they so clearly and desperately didn't want to.<br /> <br /> Some prescriptivism is a good idea, sure. Some measure of identity, setting, vibe, what have you. But taken too far? (And if you feel that Achilli hasn't been part of doing so, don't know what to tell you there) It's just the serpent that eats its own tail, and it's difficult to look at V5 and not see it running the hell out of tail. Maybe the new devs will figure out some way to refresh it (though any other edition of vampire after this many years would have definitely gotten the ol 'new edition time!' button pushed), maybe they won't, but they definitely have their work cut out for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-29T03:58:25-08:00","id":1557084,"title":"","content":"Also, and I don't mean this at all seriously, watching a fan of Mage talk up, again, I'm fine to call it prescriptivism, is interesting stuff ;p<br /> <br /> I mean say what you will, but until around the late middle-end there with whatever the Rogue Council was for example, Mage Revised had prescriptivism in buckets.<br /> <br /> *desperately flees ahead of pitchfork and torch wielding mob while waving a banner that is the 'why are you booing me' gif printed onto a flag*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-29T06:12:09-08:00","id":1557091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557072#post1557072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Such as thing was not exclusive to the Tremere, with Tzimisce being burdened by this with the removal of Vicissitude and Serpentis with the Followers of Set (now Abrahamicized to the so-called &quot;Ministry&quot;: which on another brocade, being that of a means to de-emphasize their connection with Egypt / North Africa from the game. You can tell that these writers adhered VERY heavily to the particular piece of advice of only &quot;writing what you know&quot; instead of having the bravery to research and implement respectfully. But no, just metaphorically Christianize than put in effort to what the former actual good writers, with limited research abilities of the 90's, at least tried to do). Also not to forget about Necromancy and the erasure of its Paths, along with its absolute hamfistery of so-called &quot;amalgamation&quot; with Obtenebration....</div> </div> </div> </div>Completely agree on this.<br /> <br /> I remember CA Suleiman being essential to all things arabic when Veil of Night came out and his Cairo by Night was amazing! This is the thing that got dropped off by current V5, shame because it was really good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557072#post1557072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And like I touched on before, their care for the Lasombra is equivalent to what I broached on before; just pure surface level understanding, especially in regards to how they excised and retconned Obteneberation (though it is possible that the puritanicals DID understand it, but it veered too close to &quot;badwrongfun&quot; which is why it is the state that it's in with V5).</div> </div> </div> </div>Lasombra ARE amazing and nobody wrote them better than Bruce Baugh, the end. V5 took the Lasombra to the Camarilla using justifiable causes that can be considered acceptable, but the obvious intention was what you just said in you post. It just doesn't make sense on the long run.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557072#post1557072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The puritanical branch of White Wolf Writers in vivid contrast, whether old or new, think they've actually achieved orchestrated pure artistry by emphasizing the &quot;human&quot; or &quot;street level&quot; (the latter playstyle I've come to abhor because how it was used to break Masquerade, then the other games) and, in the same breadth, by mitigating global scale, outsized epic plots, and supernatural grand strategy; that they have kept and/or &quot;saved&quot; World of Darkness.. when all they have done is completely, and inequivalently, destroyed it.<br /> <br /> In an effort to be &quot;grounded&quot; (when ironically most of their implementations have been completely nonsensical in the greater scheme of oWoD itself) they have essentially become an extreme reverse of the so-called &quot;trenchcoat munchkin katana&quot; style that they have so despised; YA-tier yuppie posers, who only bare to have the most limited perception of media outside of YA, and think every other genre is &quot;silly,&quot; when in actuality most of YA is undetailed and surface level trash (which WoD has unfortunately aped due to the horrible writing and lack of care with this edition).<br /> <br /> This is very evident with how the non-VTM X5 titles were dealt with. Whilst V5 had a lot of lorebreaking retcons, they could remain retcons as such because the writers at least somewhat played VTM or some iterations based on it (Requiem) somewhat knew what they were doing; but it's very apparent that they did not understand Reckoning or Apocalypse, at all. From the Imbued being removed from their literal main game to Werewolf being a complete erasure-baring reboot (with the absolute worst cardinal abolishment in Werewolf being the de-emphasized connection with the Umbra.. in a game outside of the Werewolves, is primarily about spirits), you can tell what they remove and what they keep follow a pattern (in overall relation to what they perceived as &quot;grounded&quot; and how they excise specific aspects too &quot;high-octane gonzo&quot; or &quot;too grognard&quot; (term-of-phase many along the puritanical prescribe to fans of Classic World of Darkness))</div> </div> </div> </div>Here is where I give credit to Revised era. Back in 2nd ed the line culminated with The Masquerade of the Red Death novels. It explained who Lazarus was, how Anis conrolled almost all the Sabbat through her ghoul and how St. Germain/Seker was the big bad behind the diablerie of Saulot. This event wasn't liked by the fans and yeah it needed to be gone. This adjustment made the Final Nights infintely more interesting and expanded the world so much more. The introduction iof the Kindred of the East and their ties to Saulot expanded the VtM line to major plots that I personally enjoyed a lot to ST and roleplay.<br /> <br /> When it comes to the simplification of V5, it simply doesn't make sense. Imagine the old times when Lasombra had access to Necromancy since the beginning and same for the Assamites with their &quot;Blood Sorcery&quot; equal to the Tremere. This very fact breaks the VtM canon storyline. Writers should acknowledge this before releasing the game.<br /> <br /> I like the term &quot;puritanical&quot; to describe this trend of VtM writing.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-29T13:14:57-08:00","id":1557102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557084#post1557084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*desperately flees ahead of pitchfork and torch wielding mob while waving a banner that is the 'why are you booing me' gif printed onto a flag*</div> </div> </div> </div>Or you could, you know, start a new thread about this. And if you actually put as much work into trying to come up with a non-flame-war inducing framing to talk about this... it might actually do something useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-29T14:37:51-08:00","id":1557104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557102#post1557102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or you could, you know, start a new thread about this. And if you actually put as much work into trying to come up with a non-flame-war inducing framing to talk about this... it might actually do something useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, it's nothing I'm noting all that seriously as far as Mage. I have no particular desire to experience the Mage revised discussions again.<br /> <br /> At most I would say in some more serious fashion, I think that the reactions at the time to Mage revised, and the reactions I read posted fresh to this day certainly suggest that people have different tolerances for what you're calling prescriptivism that they're willing to put up with, defend as viable choices or otherwise find favourable with in a given gameline.<br /> <br /> If I was otherwise going to further explore something about understanding Vampire 5th and the mentality that the people who took 5th to where it went and where it is now, well, we may as well instead talk about Pendragon.<br /> <br /> Because, okay, Pendragon. This is a commonality between Justin Achilli, Mark Rein Hagen, and several other devs and writers who could be termed puritanical or prescriptivist or what have you that have worked on the WoD at some point.<br /> <br /> They love Pendragon. It is not that hard to find commentary on them referring to it as the closest thing to a perfect rpg and their major inspiration. This is a years long love affair. Any number of older white wolf writers and devs idolize this rpg.<br /> <br /> There are some people at this point probably going &quot;what is even Pendragon?&quot;<br /> <br /> And. Okay. Pendragon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UqDuUCRrles\" data-code=\"UqDuUCRrles\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/UqDuUCRrles/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> I have OPINIONS (tm) about Pendragon, but they're almost completely irrelevant to talking about its impact on Vampire and WoD devs . They mostly stem from being really into the Matter of Britain and not being happy with Pendragon's take on it. And ultimately they're my opinions. People like it fine. It's fine.<br /> <br /> What can instead be said with concrete relevance about Pendragon is this: Pendragon is an rpg from the 80s about playing knights in Arthurian Britain. It is either famously narrow in its take on this, or infamously narrow, depending on if you like this game or not. It certainly does exactly what it tells you it is going to do, and rigorously mechanically reinforces that (as long as you ignore some of the source material it claims to us- *stops self* That's a different discussion). You want to use prescriptive instead of puritan? This is the ultimate prescriptive game. (Which I would actually prefer in this case as word choice, the idea that there's any &quot;pure&quot; Arthurian narrative or ever has been is bonkers. The Matter of Britain makes a really strong case for having invented &quot;this is my fanfic about my OC, do not steal&quot;. You like Launcelot? That is how he entered the narrative).<br /> <br /> The thing about Pendragon is that it is fundamentally allergic to wider ideas, approaches, narratives. It is 6 editions deep now into basically recycling and mandating the same notions, over and over, with little variance. The bells and whistles change a bit, the system gets more refined-ish, but really, that's mostly it. There was one edition in there that was more experimental, but also thus very polarizing in the game's fanbase and in many corners viewed as a mistake, to put it gently. The art improves I personally think? Though even that is a controversial thing to say in some corners.<br /> <br /> Pendragon recycles its adventures across editions (the biggest adventure release it made for its newest edition is a moderately updated for 6th adventure from 1st edition, as an example), with not a lot of variance. Pendragon at this point is, outside of when it was in its heyday and they could put out more adventures, basically the corebook, the Great Pendragon Campaign, and some supplements and a few other adventures for flavour. Repeat across several editions. The biggest innovation of 6e is that they decided to split the corebook into multiple books, and are going to do the same with the GPC. And they did a starter set I suppose, because everyone is doing one of those these days.<br /> <br /> If someone wants to tell me that Pendragon innovates just fine I'm going to respond that Pendragon's biggest recent deal was a kickstarter for republishing their first edition core/boxed set thing and that part of their promotional campaign was to proclaim, directly &quot;you can't improve on perfection&quot;. I wondered if this meant they were going to refund all the people who bought the 6e corebooks they just released because everything after the 1e core was a lesser effort? But apparently not. It did fine for a kickstarter for let's say an at this point 5th tier rpg? Not an indie, but certainly nowhere near wider acclaim (200k or so)<br /> <br /> This is not a game that brings in a lot of new players as near as I can tell. It certainly has a very, very loyal fanbase that has supported it through multiple editions, mostly. But it is a niche ttrpg game, and ttrpgs are already themselves, niche. It lost its heyday much faster than the WoD did honestly, and is at this point, if we want to be honest, a few steps above an indie game. People in the ttrpg space as it currently stands will, even if they don't know much about it, probably have some idea what you're talking about if you mention Vampire the Masquerade, or Shadowrun, or what have you. The odds that they've heard of Pendragon are well lower.<br /> <br /> And I need to clarify that for various people, this is a feature, not a bug. The attitude from various WoD figures towards Pendragon is that it is *art*, that it has slipped the sundry bonds of what roleplaying games are capable of and is something more refined. If it's not all that popular comparatively speaking, that makes it even cooler to be into, like you're cool enough to really *get* what rpgs should be. They hold up Pendragon in a way that people will refer to an obscure musician as &quot;your favourite musician's favourite musician.&quot; It's better that Pendragon is a smaller game than to have compromised its artistic integrity or some such thing.<br /> <br /> But whatever seminal inspiration you want to call it, and I will acknowledge Pendragon had an incredible, semi unseen influence on rpg development outside of D&amp;D spaces, it is also at this point almost calcified, static and much smaller than what once it was, even from what it was 20 years ago, and in a way much smaller than the WoD shrank from 20 years ago (I know some people are getting their dander up now, I will refer those people to the promotional campaign for the Classic Pendragon Kickstarter, frankly. This game embraces being calcified).<br /> <br /> So, when I talk about &quot;these devs love Pendragon and wish the WoD was fundamentally Pendragon&quot; that is stuff they themselves have said, for years. Years!<br /> <br /> Whatever Paradox might have wanted or not wanted, or currently want, several of their major writers over the years have wanted something very particularly, and that is for Vampire to be Pendragon. For the WoD to be Pendragon. An extremely specific thing, that enforces the &quot;best&quot; way to be that thing, narrowing its focus entirely that way. Wanting to be Pendragon is unavoidably a statement that you would in fact be fine with a smaller audience as long as you got to reinforce the true best way of gaming. In fact that might even be preferable, almost moral. I mean the 6e corebook has been out for over a year and it hasn't moved past Gold on drivethru. And that's, y'know, not unsuccessful? But that's the core rules, of the newest edition. Regardless, when you bring in those writers and give them even something resembling free reign, that is what you are going to get, and that's what we got. I mean Ericsson was more about winning fan arguments on the internet, but Achilli and Rein Hagen have for some time lamented that Vampire isn't the personal horror equivalent of Pendragon.<br /> <br /> <br /> I mean this is the thing. The WoD is not Pendragon. It's never going to be Pendragon, and the efforts to treat it that way have taken us to the point we are at now as far as any issues in the ttrpg side of things. They are definitely the origin point of why Revised would have these eruptions of judgemental, hateful vitriol here and there. And it's a pointless thing because the structure of the WoD as a published gameline doesn't really allow for recycling batch editions that don't really go anywhere. Which is part of why we are in the out of ideas space.<br /> <br /> Pendragon's influence, to actually just briefly touch Mage revised with a feather, is certainly an influence on why there is an entire sequence in one of its books that uses one of the signature npcs to thinly veiled lecture the players that they have been doing Ascension wrong, as the sig character is lectured on having failed her own avatar journey with her life choices and adventures to this point.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-29T14:39:29-08:00","id":1557105,"title":"","content":"To avoid the spam edit thing, that should say &quot;that Pendragon still innovates just fine&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-29T15:18:11-08:00","id":1557108,"title":"","content":"That feels like an incredibly long winded way of saying that you agree with my previous assessment that Paradox seems to have confused prescriptivist confidence with the actual right mentality for the job when making significant hiring decisions for their TTRPG division. Also I could care less about Pendragon (yes, I said it the way I meant to say it). I don't find your claim of relevance particularly moving. It's at best trivial truth, repeating many things others (including me) have already said without taking time to rant about a game that's not actually important to clarifying anything. We already all agree that Martin, Mark, and Justin are overly narrow in their ideas of what the WoD should be. Their views on Pendragon doesn't add anything new.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm going to note that it's always really amusing that people can say Justin and Mark just fine, but then it's always &quot;Mage.&quot; It makes me wonder who of the Mage Revised team you've actually read from, talked to, or whatever. I've heard from both Jess and Malcolm that a lot of the impressions about Mage Revised are a combination of Justin poisoning the well and people not listening to them pointing out how much of the stuff people still claim was some sort of reversal/saving throw was actually preplanned from the get go of Revised even when they can point directly at the foreshadowing present in Revised core. Or some claim that Bill Bridges coming in later was some sort of shift in the edition (it wasn't).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-29T15:20:56-08:00","id":1557109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557079#post1557079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And so when it comes to Paradox owning the WOD-IP, I think there's the possibility of Paradox selling it because they just want to focus on their core-games. But depending on how bad this Q4-report might turn out to be combined with this retreat to a very conservative focus on their strategy games, I think another possible future scenario for Paradox might be for someone bigger to buy the company. Someone like Tencent (that have already invested a bit in the company) or Microsoft. And who knows what will happen with the WOD-IP once huge companies like that get a hold of it...</div> </div> </div> </div>licensed<br /> <br /> Well I would hope that some inde company would buy the WOD IP if paradox decides to sell it. More likely a large company would be welling to buy the IP. With Games Workshop as my personal pick as the best out of the worse options for reason I already expressed earlier in this thread (mainly they are actually component with handling they licensed games), though it's more likely Warner bros, Netflix or even Hasbo would actually be interested to buy it.<br /> <br /> Now the prospect of Tencent buying WoD IP and/or Pradox would lead to some... Interesting times to say the least. Like there's always the possibility that Tencent would rent out the IP to a third party developer to ride the recent wave of &quot;inde AAA&quot; games started by Black Myth Wukong. Though More likely than not they would just use the IP to make live service game with hyper predatory monetary system (MMO, Mobile Gacha Game, Battle Royle or Cain forbid a overwatch-like ).<br /> <br /> And well if we're really lucky we would could even get a Kindred of the East reboot that's written by an actual asian /S","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 12-29-2025, 06:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-29T16:06:01-08:00","id":1557114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557108#post1557108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That feels like an incredibly long winded way of saying that you agree with my previous assessment that Paradox seems to have confused prescriptivist confidence with the actual right mentality for the job when making significant hiring decisions for their TTRPG division. Also I could care less about Pendragon (yes, I said it the way I meant to say it). I don't find your claim of relevance particularly moving. It's at best trivial truth, repeating many things others (including me) have already said without taking time to rant about a game that's not actually important to clarifying anything. We already all agree that Martin, Mark, and Justin are overly narrow in their ideas of what the WoD should be. Their views on Pendragon doesn't add anything new.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm going to note that it's always really amusing that people can say Justin and Mark just fine, but then it's always &quot;Mage.&quot; It makes me wonder who of the Mage Revised team you've actually read from, talked to, or whatever. I've heard from both Jess and Malcolm that a lot of the impressions about Mage Revised are a combination of Justin poisoning the well and people not listening to them pointing out how much of the stuff people still claim was some sort of reversal/saving throw was actually preplanned from the get go of Revised even when they can point directly at the foreshadowing present in Revised core. Or some claim that Bill Bridges coming in later was some sort of shift in the edition (it wasn't).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is Mark Rein Hagen and his at the time fellow writers talking about Pendragon:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>There\u2019s a story behind this story. In the early 1990\u2019s, the staff of Chaosium were celebrating with a feast at Mader\u2019s Restaurant in Milwaukee after a successful Gen Con. At the table next to them, the White Wolf staff also feasted on haunches of meat and steins of beer. My brother Stewart and Mark Rein Hagen, founders of White Wolf, stood and toasted Greg Stafford and the Chaosium crew, \u201cHail to Chaosium, the pioneers, the seers, the shamans, who ignited the flame of storytelling in our roleplaying hobby\u201d, and the White Wolf table cheered their respect.</i> </div> </div> </div>You can say &quot;Pendragon has no relevance to this&quot;, the writers we are talking about don't agree with you. It's not hard to find several WoD writers talking glowingly about Pendragon and the huge influence they consider it to have on them. They've done it a lot. If you don't think people saying repeatedly over the years what a huge inspiration a game is on them to their approach to game design, is relevant to talking about their approach to game design, I have no idea what to tell you. If you feel that when Justin Achilli says that V5 having a similar specificity to Pendragon is a good thing is an irrelevant statement, okay for you? I think it's relevant to explore what influences people to take the approaches they do and what that can cause as far as flaws in doing so, for why a given game is taking the shape that it is. You, for whatever reason, don't.<br /> <br /> Their views on Pendragon inform and explain their approach to game design. If someone is interested in the notion of &quot;why did the writers do that when its results have been in several ways unfortunate&quot;, which I am, then, to me, dissecting what they think is good gaming and where those ideas came from feels relevant. There's a pretty solid venn diagram between fans of the Pendragon rpg, and people in positions to do so feeling the WoD should work a certain way. If that's uninteresting to you, I can only tell you that I didn't really care much about the etymology lecture on the use of the word puritan, but by comparison I still went with trying to accommodate my word choices.\u200b<br /> <br /> I don't know whether it's from mentioning Mage at all in a way you dislike, which seems to be a sore topic with you across these forums and inclines you from what I've read to assume the absolute worst, but from saying I'm trying to start flame wars off of what was just meant as a gag post to this, you're getting remarkably personal and insulting at this point, which is an interesting contrast to telling other people they're making ad hominem statements on devs as far as dismissing what they might be saying. You're telling people what terms they should be using because their word choices annoy you, so, okay, I accommodated. Not good enough I guess? You're calling my posts ranting while you go on like that by contrast. It's justified when you do it because you're right, I guess? I'm glad you find my posts amusing, I suppose. I'm happy I could bring a ray of light into a cloudy day.<br /> <br /> If this is how you want to keep talking about these things, I'm pretty cool to not with you. I'm not trying to have an argument on the internet with you as you talk completely past me and throw insults around and tell me why you shouldn't have to even bother with engaging with most of what I'm saying, but you sure seem keen on having one with me. <br /> <br /> Ranting, long winded, and how amusing my posts are. But hey, I said some things you didn't like, so.<br /> <br /> I do certainly find this topical to discussing things like the tone of Revised edition VtM, at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-29T16:23:48-08:00","id":1557115,"title":"","content":"Really all I'm getting from this is that using pendragon that well sutable for rpgs with narrow focause isn't condusive to free form play? <br /> <br /> Like sure the devs seems obsessed with the system but it seems be a symptom rather than the cause.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-29T16:45:18-08:00","id":1557116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557115#post1557115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really all I'm getting from this is that using pendragon that well sutable for rpgs with narrow focause isn't condusive to free form play?<br /> <br /> Like sure the devs seems obsessed with the system but it seems be a symptom rather than the cause.</div> </div> </div> </div>The virtue mechanics in original VtM were in part an attempt to channel the passion mechanics of Pendragon (ironically a much less intensive one than in that rpg honestly, even with the Beast). Rein Hagen cites Pendragon, as a direct influence on Vampire, in early Vampire books, by name. The desire to have been doing that style of game themselves is baked in pretty deep for some of the people who have worked on Vampire, and for quite some while.<br /> <br /> I mean there was going to originally be a companion game about knights to Ars Magica's wizards, but Rein Hagen decided Pendragon made that pointless.<br /> <br /> This isn't some secret arcane knowledge or something honestly. To bring it around to Paradox, when the people most responsible for the white wolf IP buy were big long term WoD fans, it seems unlikely they wouldn't know what they're getting when they have a particular guy do their thing. These are influences people wear proudly on their sleeves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-29T16:51:45-08:00","id":1557117,"title":"","content":"I would put it like this, to dip back to the music comparison. Someone can say if they want that the Beatles are only symptomatic of why Oasis sound like they do, not a cause, but, that doesn't really bear out when Noel Gallagher is saying he took lyrics for Don't Look Back in Anger from a John Lennon interview and otherwise using some of his musical arrangements. And also just.. everything else about Oasis really.<br /> <br /> (And also Liam claiming to channel his spirit or something, but uhh.. let's all try and forget that happened)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-29T16:58:55-08:00","id":1557118,"title":"","content":"Well again I still think it just the case of the devs projtecting they image of the Ideal Rpg onto Pendragon and has little to do with the game it's self.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-29T17:05:49-08:00","id":1557119,"title":"","content":"If a guy trying to write vampire into a narrower, turbo focused thing is saying they want vampire to be like Pendragon and have been saying adjacent stuff to that for years, I'm inclined not to think they're being facetious, is my note. I don't think you can really separate a designer saying the equivalent of that something is an influence on them as a designer, from what they then design. People are informed and influenced by things both conscious and un, but if they're loudly saying &quot;this is an influence on me&quot;, and doing several things to back that statement up, I don't feel you can dismiss that as a source point, as it were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-29T18:02:52-08:00","id":1557122,"title":"","content":"Again I just saying that the devs are protentus idiots is because they want to force Pendragon framework onto a totally unrelated game not purly because they are fans of pendragon in the first place.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 12-29-2025, 09:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-29T18:24:24-08:00","id":1557124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557114#post1557114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is Mark Rein Hagen and his at the time fellow writers talking about Pendragon:</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that's Steve Wieck recounting a story of a young White Wolf crew encountering the established Chaosium crew (who had been in the business for 25+ years by that point) offering respect to people that helped lay the ground work for a lot of future TTRPG companies. Chaosium's design methods might be outdated and unappealing to modern audiences, but that doesn't mean they didn't innovate a lot back in the late 70s and early 80s. Yeah, they then stagnated and have largely rested on those laurels... but they're also still in business so... that's that.<br /> <br /> Nothing about Pendragon in that quote.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can say &quot;Pendragon has no relevance to this&quot;, the writers we are talking about don't agree with you. </div> </div> </div>I could say that, but I didn't say that. As well, none of the people you're referencing have weighed in on this topic directly. You're inferring things from other discussions, which puts an onus on you to demonstrate why such comments matter to this discussion. I don't think you've done a sufficient job of that; largely based on the position that Mark or Justin's views on Pendragon doesn't tell us anything meaningful about what's going on at Paradox. What I've said is that Pendragon is trivial to all this. We already agree on what's wrong with how certain game designers operate for what we seem to agree would be better for the WoD's future. I have seen nothing in all the talk of Pendragon that says anything new or deeper about the topic of what Paradox should have done, or should be doing, to improve the state of the franchise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...I have no idea what to tell you. </div> </div> </div>You could actually read my posts and respond to what I'm saying instead of seeming to have the very shallow agenda of needling me for being a Mage fan and acting like I'm the one stirring the pot. I'm pretty sure you could come up with things worth saying to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you feel that when Justin Achilli says that V5 having a similar specificity to Pendragon is a good thing is an irrelevant statement, okay for you? I think it's relevant to explore what influences people to take the approaches they do and what that can cause as far as flaws in doing so, for why a given game is taking the shape that it is. You, for whatever reason, don't. </div> </div> </div>Justin didn't design V5. V5's fundamental flaws existed before he got to put a single official word of text into the edition. How Pendragon influenced him isn't why V5 went wrong. Do you not see why I might have trouble taking your analytic approach here seriously when you're ignoring things like the unidirectional flow of time? Justin is also not working on WoD5 anymore so... whatever happens next might have nothing to do with his views on Pendragon because Paradox has repeatedly demonstrated a lack of care of continuity between developer approaches.<br /> <br /> I made a much more significant claim about W5 and H5. But I think this proves the point that harping on Pendragon is not informative. W5 shows a distinct lack of trying to be the Pendragon of werewolf games. It's not a tightly packaged game where you're either going to love it for being very dedicated to being exactly the game it claims to be and no more or less. It's a disjointed mess. It's a slapdash of ideas from multiple development teams, from at least one person above Justin on the org chart at the time, and it fails to be very good at anything it's trying to be. As I said before, the case is far stronger that Justin just polished up what he was handed and passed in on, knowing he wants going to be working on it long term (as his departure from Paradox was stated as being planned and said plans were implied to be something of an imposed deadline for him).<br /> <br /> H5 is even more so an anti-Pendragon game. The only strong prescriptivist thing about it is the &quot;Orgs are inherently bad, Driven Hunters can't join them and stay Driven.&quot; It's not a game that demands you use a specific set of custom tools to work... it's a game that completely forgot to tell you that you need to bring your toolbox with you to do anything with it.<br /> <br /> I'll even go farther. Exalted is not what most people consider a highly prescriptivist game. It has a strong identity to it, but it's also a proud kitchen sink of fantasy that can handle almost anything players might want to do in the setting (if they can tolerate it's rules-tome approach to mechanics). Justin was a major designer on Exalted. He was probably a big reason for 1e going for its Virtue route. But the fact that Pendragon loving Justin worked a lot on the development of the game doesn't tell us much about what Exalted's flaws are, how they got there, or how they've morphed over time and the influence of everyone else that's worked on it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If that's uninteresting to you, I can only tell you that I didn't really care much about the etymology lecture on the use of the word puritan, but by comparison I still went with trying to accommodate my word choices. </div> </div> </div>If three sentences counts as a lecture... what does that make your posts on Pendragon given their length? If you want to discuss tone instead... I'm not sure that's going to help your case.<br /> <br /> There also isn't a clear comparison between my self-described peeve around word use, and my response to your talking about Pendragon. I made my case on why I think one word isn't a great choice, and then offered up an alternative word that I think is the better choice (also I didn't demand anyone speak how I want or else, I asked people to change their choice of terms). You didn't say, &quot;hey, I think people should consider the influence of Pendragon had on the people we're discussing because it's pretty clear how much it got them to this point,&quot; and then waited to see how people responded. You just launched into a whole essay about it, so I had no chance to &quot;accommodate&quot; by affirming that Pendragon was an influence on these specific authors so we could all move on with the actual topic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't know whether it's from mentioning Mage at all in a way you dislike,... </div> </div> </div>To be far more specific: I rankle when people treat other people as something not-human because acknowledging their personhood would be hard to do and keep hammering on whatever point you think they exist to embody. Humans are complicated. Trying to reduce people to some caricature so you can then justify saying whatever you want about them isn't something I appreciate. That's why I highlighted that the Mage Revised team is always &quot;Mage&quot; not specific people, while everyone loves to name Justin and don't even consider anyone else involved. The way you're talking about this doesn't communicate that you think of these game designers as people - people you might disagree with on countless topics are still people - but as rhetorical cudgels.<br /> <br /> And yeah, that number of times that means I'm about to have that same treated pointed right at me (oh look my posting history being used to justify how I'm the bad guy and you're the most perfect person to ever post on the Internets, yay!) is a part of why it ticks me off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...you're getting remarkably personal and insulting at this point... </div> </div> </div>Citation needed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...which is an interesting contrast to telling other people they're making ad hominem statements on devs as far as dismissing what they might be saying. You're telling people what terms they should be using because their word choices annoy you, so, okay, I accommodated. </div> </div> </div>Dude, what the fuck?<br /> <br /> 1) I said &quot;ad hominem&quot; as a clarification about <b>my own post</b> not being intended as one. I didn't respond to anyone's post in this thread accusing them of using ad hominem attacks.<br /> <br /> 2) I, again, asked people to change their language, I explained why, and I offered what I felt was not only a suitable alternative but a superior word choice for what we're talking about. I haven't belaboured the point, you're the one that seems to be unable to stop bringing it up (not really that accommodating at this point is it?). Yeah I called it a pet peeve. Should I have stated something different about how I feel it ranks in terms of my priorities, or is being honest OK? Everyone seems pretty OK with it so why is this such a bad thing exactly?<br /> <br /> I mean, seriously, who is the one that acting like they're here to read the absolute worst into someone else's posts? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If this is how you want to keep talking about these things, I'm pretty cool to not with you. I'm not trying to have an argument on the internet with you as you talk completely past me and throw insults around and tell me why you shouldn't have to even bother with engaging with most of what I'm saying, but you sure seem keen on having one with me. </div> </div> </div><b><u>You responded to my post and I've been dealing with your tanget</u></b>. So spare me the implication that I'm the one starting shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-29T18:28:48-08:00","id":1557125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557122#post1557122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again I just saying that the devs are protentus idiots is because they want to force Pendragon framework onto a totally unrelated game not purly because they are fans of pendragon in the first place.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm just noting that fan streak runs deep and isn't something to discount for the impact it has had. There was a few years there when white wolf was still its own company that they outright bought Pendragon for its 5th edition and published books for it out of the ArtHaus imprint.<br /> <br /> Bill Bridges was an actual contributor to the Pendragon 4th and 5th ed corebooks and wrote other material for the line.<br /> <br /> Though, Bill Bridges is comparatively interesting for being a kind of Uno reverse card in that sense, as 4th edition was the experimental one that some people harsh on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-29T19:28:07-08:00","id":1557128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, that's Steve Wieck recounting a story of a young White Wolf crew encountering the established Chaosium crew (who had been in the business for 25+ years by that point) offering respect to people that helped lay the ground work for a lot of future TTRPG companies. Chaosium's design methods might be outdated and unappealing to modern audiences, but that doesn't mean they didn't innovate a lot back in the late 70s and early 80s. Yeah, they then stagnated and have largely rested on those laurels... but they're also still in business so... that's that.<br /> <br /> Nothing about Pendragon in that quote. </div> </div> </div>It's a story being recounted in the context of Pendragon's publisher transitions, if you feel he's not talking about that in that context, okay, sure, whatever you say. Rein Hagen would go on to cite the game as a direct inspiration to vampire, but that's meaningless context to this as well I'm sure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I could say that, but I didn't say that. As well, none of the people you're referencing have weighed in on this topic directly. . </div> </div> </div>Justin Achilli, in an interview with Richard Dansky in 2022 giving examples of games that illustrate his design philosophy. He was working for Paradox on their WoD stuff at the time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I had been working on MMOs a while back and it used to bother me how a lot of MMO marketing was \u201cyou can be anything you can imagine in this enormous living world!\u201d but their gameplay was built around three or four very distinct classes or roles and combat quests. That always seemed really disingenuous to me. Better to have a very limited scope and help the player tell the best story they can within that scope than to try to tick every box and deliver adequately on only a few of them. <b>Pendragon</b> is an amazing TTRPG, and characters are comparatively very limited in what they are: Arthurian-era, mostly knights. And look at, say, <b>Stardew Valley</b> \u2014 it doesn\u2019t have one tenth of the feature list of, say, <b>Star Citizen</b>, but it\u2019s made millions of people very happy by letting them tell a very distinct kind of story, and it doesn\u2019t pretend to do anything else.\u200b </div> </div> </div>Aside from the story you've decided exists in a vacuum, Mark Rein Hagen listed Pendragon under games that inspired vampire, twice, once in the first edition core, and again in the second, in the first noting his attention to his influences thusly:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In order to honor those who gave so much to this work, I have included a list of works that have especially influenced this one \u2014 try to discern what of them exists in this book. </div> </div> </div>If you feel that has no bearing on his work and approaches all the same, hey, okay, sure.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Justin didn't design V5. V5's fundamental flaws existed before he got to put a single official word of text into the edition. How Pendragon influenced him isn't why V5 went wrong. Do you not see why I might have trouble taking your analytic approach here seriously when you're ignoring things like the unidirectional flow of time? Justin is also not working on WoD5 anymore so... whatever happens next might have nothing to do with his views on Pendragon because Paradox has repeatedly demonstrated a lack of care of continuity between developer approaches. </div> </div> </div>Justin furthered the brand along while he was there, and he was pretty clear on his philosophy in doing so. To say that he had no impact on the place he worked for several years and that whatever he might have done didn't reflect his game philosophies is a choice. Your alternative is apparently nothing he did while there moved things in any notable direction or otherwise furthered an existing one. His ideas contributed to moving vampire in the direction it was going. Published material reflected them. He didn't have to be there from the jump to be part of that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There also isn't a clear comparison between my self-described peeve around word use, and my response to your talking about Pendragon.\u200b </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> So the insults are fine because I merit them, got it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You just launched into a whole essay about it, so I had no chance to &quot;accommodate&quot; by affirming that Pendragon was an influence on these specific authors so we could all move on with the actual topic. </div> </div> </div>If you found my post to be trivial, irrelevant, long winded ranting (your words), what exactly forced you to respond to it? For a guy bolding and underlining a proclamation of &quot;you started it!&quot;, you certainly seem to feel obligated to keep posting to say how terrible my posts are. Again, it's fine because I have it coming, I guess?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Citation needed. </div> </div> </div>Talking about my posts:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I'm going to note that it's always really amusing that </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That feels like an incredibly long winded way of saying that </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> repeating many things others (including me) have already said without taking time to rant about a game that's not actually important to clarifying anything </div> </div> </div>If you feel that these are not insulting ways to describe someone else's posts you are responding to on a discussion forum, that no force on earth is requiring you to do, hey, sure buddy, whatever you say. I definitely tell people their ideas amuse me for their inaccuracy, while telling them their posts are long winded rants, when I'm just palling around and not meaning anything by it. That's how conversation works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, seriously, who is the one that acting like they're here to read the absolute worst into someone else's posts?\u200b </div> </div> </div>Do you honestly think the above commentary you've asked to be cited comes off not insultingly? If so, by all means continue to post whatever you feel you are forced to have to keep saying in response to my posts, I'm happy not to bother with replying further if that's how you believe you are coming off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To be far more specific: I rankle when people treat other people as something not-human because acknowledging their personhood would be hard to do and keep hammering on whatever point you think they exist to embody. Humans are complicated. Trying to reduce people to some caricature so you can then justify saying whatever you want about them isn't something I appreciate. That's why I highlighted that the Mage Revised team is always &quot;Mage&quot; not specific people, while everyone loves to name Justin and don't even consider anyone else involved. The way you're talking about this doesn't communicate that you think of these game designers as people - people you might disagree with on countless topics are still people - but as rhetorical cudgels. </div> </div> </div>Do you find even the slightest irony in saying things like this given the tenor of your replies to me? You've now decided to lecture me on that my posts represent a moral wrong, thus requiring you to keep replying like this out of some sense of wounded justice I suppose.,<br /> <br /> Do you have some understanding that when you say &quot;always&quot;, while with zero self awareness talking about reducing people to rhetorical cudgels, that such is what you are doing? I mentioned Mage in any kind of depth in this thread basically twice, and you are now calling me out as representing some constant dehumanizing trend you encounter in mage discussions. I definitely don't feel like I'm being reduced to a caricature so you can go on about people posting generally about Mage in ways you don't like. I &quot;always&quot; do that? Citation needed for my repeated pattern of posts talking about the Mage revised like that (I know the odds are you'll expand it to something beyond mage, but right now you're the one going on about the &quot;always&quot; wrongs done to its devs, a crime that stains me as surely as a scarlet letter. Or something). It's fine, you're not at all reframing me as an example to be be-cudgeled for whatever all discourse on Mage devs or Mage revised. Hey, maybe it just didn't occur to me off hand who wrote the segment I mentioned, but that would require ascribing to me a level of complexity inconvenient to my status as an example of discourse immorality. Also, the &quot;dehumanizing&quot; was to say a sequence like that comes off as a condescending lecture born of a particular sort of game influence. If you feel that statement robs someone of their humanity so thoroughly that you have to call out the moral outrage, okay, sure. You are at the point of saying that snarky critique is a crime against someone's sense of human identity that you are called up thus to defend. I'm aware in saying that you will probably just launch into why in fact that is exactly the case and why it matters to keep going on like this at me with some further reference to the depth of my crimes here, but again, okay, go for it.<br /> <br /> I've certainly said before I have huge problems with Mage as a conceptual gameline for a baked in ableism that feels frustratingly and relentlessly dehumanizing, and I've said that several times in fact, but that issue transcends editions. This thing you're going on about now? That's you, needing someone to wail on for Mage discourse you don't like and have decided I'm a convenient proxy for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Trying to reduce people to some caricature so you can then justify saying whatever you want about them isn't something I appreciate. </div> </div> </div>Is there any part of you capable of acknowledging that this comes off as &quot;I'm insulting you repeatedly because you deserve it for being bad&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And yeah, that number of times that means I'm about to have that same treated pointed right at me (oh look my posting history being used to justify how I'm the bad guy and you're the most perfect person to ever post on the Internets, yay!) is a part of why it ticks me off.<br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div>&quot;You made me mad, and you're a bad person, you deserve this. I have to keep saying how bad you are.&quot; No part of you, in any way, thinks you at all come off like that, I guess. You post things like this, while without blinking going on about reducing people to caricatures. I know, I know, I'm the one doing that, not you. Sure. Okay. <br /> <br /> I posted a thing about my views on how Pendragon plays a role in some writer habits. I said a couple of things about Mage. You decided that needs to be forum moral war. You decided you *had* to talk about how it was a pointless long winded rant, then say no, those aren't insults, and even if they are, I have them coming for ticking you off with my abominable conduct. That's you. That's your posts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-29T20:19:42-08:00","id":1557130,"title":"","content":"As I feel like this is going to go somewhere pedantic and perhaps the phrasing was ambiguous, when I note &quot;it's being brought up in the context of Pendragon's publisher transitions&quot;, I mean that the blatant context of the story about the toast is it being brought up in a discussion otherwise about Pendragon. Rein Hagen's first note about the game's influence on Vampire would likely predate it besides.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.chaosium.com/bloggreg-staffords-king-arthur-pendragon-rpg-returns-to-chaosium-ownership/#.XBDm32IlQo0.blogger\" target=\"_blank\">Greg Stafford's King Arthur Pendragon RPG returns to Chaosium ownership - Chaosium Inc.</a><br /> <br /> Wieck's explicitly talking about Pendragon when otherwise bringing up the white wolf toast story, the blog entry is titled for Pendragon, Wieck brings up the story as a &quot;story behind the story&quot; of Pendragon's ownership change and white wolf's regard. If someone wants to view that all the same as &quot;they didn't mean Pendragon when making the toast though, it's just that he brought it up while talking about Pendragon, and him telling that story was reposted in a blog post, about Pendragon, that specific part was not about Pendragon though&quot;, okay, sure. There's a marked point of obstinacy in that view, but sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 12-29-2025, 11:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-29T23:25:10-08:00","id":1557131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557128#post1557128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a story being recounted in the context of Pendragon's publisher transitions, if you feel he's not talking about that in that context, okay, sure, whatever you say.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I'll happily acknowledge that context. But... what does that additional context add or clarify? It's still not what you claimed it to be, &quot;This is Mark Rein Hagen and his at the time fellow writers talking about Pendragon,&quot; and Steve's full blog is talking about the transition of Pendragon back to Chaosium was a personal decision not just a business decision doesn't say anything about Steve's design philosophy, and since he hadn't worked on the WoD in years and hasn't since, or the future design philosophies that came after. He related in what any other context would be seen as a warm little anecdote about how the Wiecks and Greg Stafford became friends, and how that drove a change in IP ownership.... not some deep seated message about the &quot;secret&quot; Pendragon clique. You're absolutely trying to make that story into way more than it is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rein Hagen would go on to cite the game as a direct inspiration to vampire, but that's meaningless context to this as well I'm sure. </div> </div> </div>I'm open to the possibility that it could matter in some fashion, but I remain unconvinced due to a lack of any actual evidence. What in V5 can you draw a solid line between Mark's love of Pendragon and how the game was developed? Most of what V5 was turned out to be was well previewed by Martin and Ken Hite before Mark got brought in as well. The only thing that's every been explicitly state as &quot;this was Mark's baby&quot; was the whole Chechnya debacle. And that most certainly can't be connected to loving Pendragon in any concrete fashion.<br /> <br /> It's simpler with Justin and VtM Revised because he was the lead on VtM Revised and every book passed through him. He's acknowledged writing a number of things fans didn't like openly. We can actually point at Justin's explicit work and then see if it really fits into your position that it stems from being so enamored with Pendragon. Though the case for even that so far is rather mind-reading necessary as there are jumps in the flow of causation that only work if you assume you know what was going on in people's heads when they did things.<br /> <br /> And yes, to the larger issue of Paradox's brand mismanagement? The Pendragon thing is still <u>trivial</u>. I'm going to remain a bit pedantic here, but trivial does not mean &quot;meaningless,&quot; it means, &quot;unimportant,&quot; amongst other definitions. Or as I've already said in other words, the Pendragon stuff doesn't add to the understanding of what's going wrong with Paradox. Why Mark and Justin are such prescriptivist developers can't be the root cause of what's going on at Paradox with the facts we have, and being able to tease out a meaningful connection to Pendragon specifically seems a dubious effort at best.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Justin Achilli, in an interview with Richard Dansky in 2022 giving examples of games that illustrate his design philosophy. He was working for Paradox on their WoD stuff at the time. </div> </div> </div>This quote isn't as damning as you'd imagine. This is exceptionally common thinking in game design (and specifically video game design) as AAA games that try to do everything keep stumbling while indie darlings that just try to be the thing they are keep cropping up and being the hot game for a few months with last fandoms years after. Yeah, he name check Pendragon as an example, but it's a good example for what he's saying. So what? What does this actually illustrate? What does this map to in the WoD5 books that came out during his time there that clearly show this line from Pendragon to [various developers] to WoD5 flaws?<br /> <br /> &quot;Aha! Pendragon!&quot; Great. Despite you seeming to think you've been reading my posts, I've never said that people at WW didn't love Pendragon. I'm questioning the validity of saying that it was such a strong force in their work (to differing degrees, they're all different people with different bodies of work to look at).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Aside from the story you've decided exists in a vacuum, Mark Rein Hagen listed Pendragon under games that inspired vampire, twice, once in the first edition core, and again in the second, in the first noting his attention to his influences thusly: </div> </div> </div>And then the Wieck brothers, who were good friends with Pendragon's creator and also seem to have enjoyed the game, ousted Mark from the company... almost like loving Pendragon isn't something that turns developers into mindless robots out to assimilate everything into the image of Pendragon. And then Mark failed at every game related thing he dipped his toes into for over two decades and had to do other work. And then he got a job at Paradox because they seem to like hiring people that sound like they'd have name clout with the fans (they made a big deal of getting people from Bloodlines 1 to work on the first version of Bloodlines 2 as well), and know he's back at other things again.<br /> <br /> I really wonder where you're trying to go with these things. Mark had other influences. Mark wasn't very good at making something as tightly focused as Pendragon either. VtM 1e was scattershot and all over the place, that directly fed into the huge range of ideas 2e tried to run with, and Revised tried to bring back to a more cohesive whole. What is this supposed to show, explain, or elaborate for anyone? Nobody is disputing that Pendragon was popular with some of the WW folks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you feel that has no bearing on his work and approaches all the same, hey, okay, sure. </div> </div> </div>I feel the level of bearing is completely unestablished and you're unjustifiably assuming the maximum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Justin furthered the brand along while he was there, and he was pretty clear on his philosophy in doing so. </div> </div> </div>So... where does Pendragon factor into anything that made it into a book? That's your claim if you don't feel like remembering it. That it wasn't just Justin's existing bias towards prescriptive designs, but specifically Pendragon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So the insults are fine because I merit them, got it. </div> </div> </div>I said no such thing.<br /> <br /> I was criticizing your arguments, because they merit a lot of criticism, and you took it personally, so now I'm dealing with that too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...long winded ranting (your words)... </div> </div> </div>Splicing fragments from two different sentences together to imply a single statement is not how, &quot;your words&quot; works. If you've really paid attention to my positing history, the following should be completely unsurprising:<br /> <br /> Don't pull this shit with me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...what exactly forced you to respond to it? </div> </div> </div>Nothing, I take complete responsibility for the decision to respond as I do for all my posts. I'm the only one capable of compelling me to post. I abhor it when people that deny their own agency in such matters.<br /> <br /> I felt like it because I wanted to push back at your insipidly snide framing of all this, it's that simple.<br /> <br /> How about you? You could stop whenever you want as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For a guy bolding and underlining a proclamation of &quot;you started it!&quot;, you certainly seem to feel obligated to keep posting to say how terrible my posts are. Again, it's fine because I have it coming, I guess? </div> </div> </div>Yet again, just assuming what's in my head as if I'm not rather notorious for speaking my mind when I post. How about you stop assuming and just take the words I used as the words I wanted to use (with some consideration for the typos and the spam bot being an issue that makes it worse on my correcting them).<br /> <br /> Yeah, I highlighted &quot;you started it.&quot; Because that's fairly important to my feelings about all this. You're acting like someone that threw a punch, broke their knuckle in the process, and are now screaming at the guy you hit for your own injury; let alone if I actually punched back. If I threw the first punch and you only got that broken knuckle in self defense it would a much fairer complaint and a stronger moral imperative for me to attempt to do something about helping to fix the aftermath.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Talking about my posts: </div> </div> </div>See, that's the thing. &quot;Talking about [your] posts.&quot; Or as is commonly said,&quot;attack the argument, not the other person.&quot;<br /> <br /> You are taking, &quot;your post was long winded,&quot; as a personal insult on your character not a complaint about your writing choices; and playing the victim of my &quot;bullying&quot; attitude. That's bullshit. <br /> <br /> I do not believe for one second that is your honestly held bar for when a post becomes personal or insulting. I've seen you around too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I definitely tell people their ideas amuse me for their inaccuracy, while telling them their posts are long winded rants, when I'm just palling around and not meaning anything by it. That's how conversation works. </div> </div> </div>1) I did not state my amusement at inaccuracy. Rather the oddity of the direct comparison I made of how Justin is treated vs. how the Mage team are treated. It is not rare to be amused by juxtapositions such as that, even in a somewhat sarcastic fashion. Is it really that hard to reflect on the observation that you yourself fall into the habit of simultaneously trying to brush VtM and Mage Revised with the same brush, but also talking about the people behind things noticeably differently?<br /> <br /> 2) And I most certainly do mean things by what I say. I've just long, long, long been burnt out by lopsided appeals to civility. You want me to care about the implications of my manner of writing, but refuse any calls towards the same in regards to you. This isn't art class where all the students have to give critiques with positive and negative feedback. I'm not your manager with a corporate mandate to sandwich negative feedback between hollow positive affirmations. If I have negative criticism (though in this case I've said repeatedly we seem to be in agreement on a number of things and probably the far more important things and you seem to completely ignore that), and I think they're worth saying, you're going to do whatever you want with my posts. Just don't expect me to respect you inserting things I didn't say, twisting around my words to imply more than I said, or your own admitted preconceptions coloring your interpretations. Those are your responsibility in a conversation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you honestly think the above commentary you've asked to be cited comes off not insultingly? </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I do. I'm not surprised they weren't received well, but elevating them to insults instead of blunt negative criticism is a pretty big leap considering the context. It's not like I'm tucking in jabs like, &quot;what kind of idiot would say...&quot; in there. It's not like I haven't presented more to my posts that just those selective negative bits. <br /> <br /> Why should I continue to even entertain the idea that your Pendragon hypothesis is anything more than an excuse to rant about Pendragon (also see below with Mage)? You have not, at all, responded to the concerns that you haven't really connected the dots from &quot;these folks have a soft spot for Pendragon,&quot; to &quot;this is a specific thing in WoD5 that is directly because of Pendragon's influence.&quot; You've admitted you have strong feelings about Pendragon, made the deliberate decision to keep in bits of &quot;oh gotta stop myself before getting too much into why Pendragon is bad,&quot; instead of excising those, and aren't even entertaining any other possibilities. I mean, what if Justin's tenure at was really all about making Stardew Valley W5? And in saying that I wish that wasn't as plausible as it sounds when I give it a moment of serious thought beyond the joke. These are not people who only have one influence they talk about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you find even the slightest irony in saying things like this given the tenor of your replies to me? </div> </div> </div>No, because I don't see anything in my replies to you that I think can be in good faith be treat as reducing you to a caricature that only exists to be a rhetorical tool in my arsenal.<br /> <br /> I've engaged with your points, I've offered counterpoints. I've asked you questions that you could use to further make your case in answering if you decided to try to do so. I've gotten direct and personal negativity for my efforts. I'm not seeing a serious effort on your part to have a conversation here, and I'm not seeing any attempt to acknowledge what I have extended as points to focus on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You've now decided to lecture me on that my posts represent a moral wrong, thus requiring you to keep replying like this out of some sense of wounded justice I suppose., </div> </div> </div>More assumptions and mind-reading.<br /> <br /> How does, &quot;this thing rankles me,&quot; get you to this response exactly? When did I get on my soap box to decry your immorality exactly?<br /> <br /> And even if something I simply stated as a distaste should be elevated to a moral issue... am I wrong? Should I go back and quote your response to my anecdotal humanizing of Justin? Should I lay out in a much more direct way how you've consistently done what I've complained about in this thread? Do you really think you're not at least a little guilty of my criticize here? Because you're not denying it over deflecting back at me instead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you have some understanding that when you say &quot;always&quot;, while with zero self awareness talking about reducing people to rhetorical cudgels, that such is what you are doing? </div> </div> </div>That's a hell of a stretch. The &quot;always&quot; was attached to the observation that people name Justin and don't name the Mage authors when discussing Revised's flaws as an edition. I'll acknowledge it might be a hyperbolic statement since I can't actually prove it, and even a tad hypocritical since I'm usually not very well inclined to people that use unwarranted absolutes. I might fee it's warranted but I can acknowledge there's a case to be made it's not. That said the &quot;always&quot; is trivial to the rhetorical cudgel part. People can fall into the &quot;always&quot; camp without then also using the developers of the games as cudgels instead of talking about them like people.<br /> <br /> So deriding my self-awareness? Yeah, that's a no go. You're connecting two different statements - again - to make me look worse than what I actually said. Don't see why you'd expect that to make me thing differently about anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mentioned Mage in any kind of depth in this thread basically twice, and you are now calling me out as representing some constant dehumanizing trend you encounter in mage discussions. </div> </div> </div>No....<br /> <br /> I'm applying what you're doing to Mark and Justin too. To me the whole Pendragon (since the whole &quot;you need to do more to connect the dots here&quot; stuff isn't getting a response) thing is so you can use anyone that worked on a WW product you don't like as a cudgel; named or unnamed. The not-naming of the Mage team is a <u>highlight</u> of the phenomenon, not the entirety of it.<br /> <br /> I also never stated this as specific to Mage discussions. I've never even talked about Mage as a game in this thread. I've only talked about the developers and their reactions to the response to Revised in conjunction to the rest of the WoD teams.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I definitely don't feel like I'm being reduced to a caricature so you can go on about people posting generally about Mage in ways you don't like. </div> </div> </div>Yet you just accused me of doing what I was decrying in others, so which is it. Am I lacking in self awareness or did I tow the line successfully by not cross it since by your own statement you don't feel reduced in such a fashion?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I &quot;always&quot; do that? </div> </div> </div>Not the claim made, citations not necessary, ceding the warrant to make an absolute in the actual context being fair to question already made above.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've certainly said before I have huge problems with Mage as a conceptual gameline... </div> </div> </div>So here's the real simple point to me right now. You don't like Pendragon. You don't like Mage. You seem to be completely unaware of how much you're inventing reasons to attack people for not sharing those matters of taste. Your are desperately trying to shift the blame on me (not the one that brought up Pendragon, not the one that brought up Mage, not actually defending things you seem to think I am, not attacking many things you claim I am), rather than going and taking a break to consider if you just shouldn't talk about games you don't like with people that do. You entered into this with &quot;Heavy Arms is a Mage fan, so I must be as uncharitable as possible.&quot; You tossed my status as a Mage fan into this as soon as you had an excuse to, and took the gloves off, yet somehow consistently think you're in the right in all this.<br /> <br /> As they say, go touch some grass (well, maybe snow depending on where you live).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This thing you're going on about now? That's you, needing someone to wail on for Mage discourse you don't like and have decided I'm a convenient proxy for. </div> </div> </div>No, this is a complete invention of your mind. I don't need to wail on someone non-Mage person to get some Mage discourse going. I could got poke Dataweaver and probably be in page 20 on whatever disagreement we have never resolved in our approach to the game in years of debates before 2026 starts.<br /> <br /> You do realize that you're drawing out a huge amount from &quot;hey, maybe go start another thread for this tangent?&quot; Which is normally a fairly benign request? And I didn't call out Mage specifically, I meant the whole thing. But you, you're the one focusing in on Mage because you've got opinions. And you really do seem to want an excuse to vent them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is there any part of you capable of acknowledging that this comes off as &quot;I'm insulting you repeatedly because you deserve it for being bad&quot;? </div> </div> </div>I can broadly acknowledge that someone could feel that way, but the amount of mental gymnastics to get there from what I actually said is enough for me to dismiss it as a good faith criticism of what I posted. I've already covered how shallow I find your concept of an insulting response. I've made it clear that I think you're far more (if subconsciously) letting my being a Mage fan plus whatever else in my posting history you don't like color your interpretations of my words way out of line with what's in the posts. Yeah, the paragraph this is reacting to is a more serious and more harsh thing for me to have said, but the &quot;repeated insults&quot; are in your head, not my words. The implication that you deserve negative treatment beyond push back from me regarding your own dismissive attitude is also something in your head, not my words. I have not called you a bad person. I disagree with a lot of what you're saying. I don't like your rhetorical approach. But I don't know you. I don't know why you're posting like this and if it's a now thing or a a general thing because I don't recall any past interactions we've had going this way; as far as I recall we're usually in agreement and our differences in approach haven't lead to such animosity though I can't account for any side conversations about me you might have had with others I can't really be held into account for those either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;You made me mad, and you're a bad person, you deserve this. I have to keep saying how bad you are.&quot; No part of you, in any way, thinks you at all come off like that, I guess. </div> </div> </div>Nope. Because the vast majority of my time on the Internet has reinforced a simple lesson in my mind: if I let people know how I honestly feel, they're make up whatever they want. Since I want to honestly communicate how I feel, I have no ability to interact online with people under the presumption that saying, &quot;hey what you said was upsetting to me,&quot; will not result in someone resorting to bad faith, &quot;Oh, you said you're mad, that means you're also [insert whatever negative things someone what's to lay on me].&quot; I am left with the only recourse to not accept responsibility for the me others construct in their heads based on things I didn't say. You added &quot;and you're a bad person.&quot; You added, &quot;you deserve this.&quot; You added, &quot;I have to keep saying how bad you are.&quot; The Heavy Arms that said all that? That's a Heavy Arms in your head. That's not me. You control that fictional construct, not me. What you have him do? That's on you. I don't accept your narrative of my duplicate as my own actions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I posted a thing about my views on how Pendragon plays a role in some writer habits. I said a couple of things about Mage. You decided that needs to be forum moral war. You decided you *had* to talk about how it was a pointless long winded rant, then say no, those aren't insults, and even if they are, I have them coming for ticking you off with my abominable conduct. That's you. That's your posts. </div> </div> </div>And yet again, not the disparity here. You just posted some stuff. I decided. I imposed. I made moral declarations. I had to do it for truth, justice, and the Darkness way.<br /> <br /> Even if you're completely right about me? That doesn't absolve you. That's why I'm directly accusing you of deflecting. I answered your questions. Are you going to answer mine?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-30T02:17:19-08:00","id":1557132,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> Yeah I'm going to agree with @<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\">Heavy Arms</a> on this one.<br /> <br /> Pendragon isn't some part of a conspiracy to ruin RPGs.<br /> <br /> Like sure the V5's head writer might have an unhealthy obsession with\u200b the game but this only has a at best tangential relationship with his conduct. Like the pendragon team actually ousted him for gods sake.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557131#post1557131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And then the Wieck brothers, who were good friends with Pendragon's creator and also seem to have enjoyed the game, ousted Mark from the company... almost like loving Pendragon isn't something that turns developers into mindless robots out to assimilate everything into the image of Pendragon.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-30T02:40:57-08:00","id":1557133,"title":"","content":"Just to be clear about the timeline there, the Wieck brothers ousted Mark Rein Hagen from White Wolf (due to severe financial mismanagement) before White Wolf acquired the rights to Pendragon, which was then sold to Steve Wieck's personal TTRPG company by CCP as part of their divestment of the smaller WW IPs that CCP didn't predict would be valuable as licensed products as it was clear that the WoDMMO wasn't going to happen.<br /> <br /> It's a bit confusing because Pendragon traded hands three times if fairly rapid succession.<br /> <br /> So, as MarkK said, Mark RH put Pendragon in the inspiration section in WoD books first. Then The Wiecks ousted Mark RH. Then Chaosium had to sell Pendragon (to yet another company before WW got it), which eventually ended up in in the Wieck's hands in a convoluted fashion (WW bought it, CCP bought WW and Steve was kept as part of CCP's leadership, Steve Wieck bought Pendragon from CCP as CCP moved out of the TTRPG business). All of those sales happened in under 10 years.<br /> <br /> So there was never a chance for Mark RH to work on Pendragon while it was owned by WW. He was ousted by people that would become the Pendragon owners (and one of them a developer of one edition) later in the time line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-30T03:08:15-08:00","id":1557134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, I highlighted &quot;you started it.&quot; Because that's fairly important to my feelings about all this. You're acting like someone that threw a punch, broke their knuckle in the process, and are now screaming at the guy you hit for your own injury; let alone if I actually punched back. If I threw the first punch and you only got that broken knuckle in self defense it would a much fairer complaint and a stronger moral imperative for me to attempt to do something about helping to fix the aftermath. </div> </div> </div>Thank you for clarifying, that helps me understand what it is you think has been going on here. I will I guess just say that no, the post was just saying what it was saying. If you think it was an attack on you, that's on you. It wasn't. If you think it is anyway, feel free to go on about that. Your feelings seem to be that posts you don't like are a guy punching at you. If this is your headspace for even just something like posting a reply, okay then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I felt like it because I wanted to push back at your insipidly snide framing of all this, it's that simple. </div> </div> </div>Yyeap.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even if you're completely right about me? That doesn't absolve you. That's why I'm directly accusing you of deflecting. I answered your questions. Are you going to answer mine? </div> </div> </div>Don't see how I could clarify my views to you more than I already have at this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 12-30-2025, 06:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-30T03:19:34-08:00","id":1557136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557132#post1557132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah I'm going to agree with @<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\">Heavy Arms</a> on this one.<br /> <br /> Pendragon isn't some part of a conspiracy to ruin RPGs.<br /> <br /> Like sure the V5's head writer might have an unhealthy obsession with the game but this only has a at best tangential relationship with his conduct. Like the pendragon team actually ousted him for gods sake.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>An rpg people note as an influence on their work isn't a conspiracy, it's a thing someone openly notes as an influence on their work. That's just.. a thing they are noting as an influence on their work. That's it. If people are particularly struck by something, the idea that said thing doesn't then shape their own efforts feels pretty thin. There's no &quot;conspiracy&quot;, there's people reacting to a thing that shapes their viewpoints based on their reactions to that thing. That's not some ephemeral thing, that's the impact of a game decently serious efforts at putting together a history of rpgs have noted has had considerable influence on rpg design. None of this is some big secret and it's surprising that people think it is, though I suppose it speaks to my note about the obscurity the game has by this point fallen into.<br /> <br /> Ken Hite, who also worked on Vampire 5th, has been effusive in his praise of Pendragon as an rpg over the years, and the influence he feels it has on game design. He considers the Great Pendragon Campaign the best single campaign book ever written, in those words. He's bragged about playing in a Pendragon campaign run by the game's creator. It's a pretty known thing that a variety of writers consider this game an entirely notable influence. That's not some sinister, secret thing. That's an open, repeatedly referenced thing.<br /> <br /> Pendragon by its nature can't be.. whatever that is as &quot;conspiracies to ruin gaming&quot; go. It can certainly have played a role in shaping what some writers think good gaming is, and that can be seen in things from their approaches to stuff like how mechanics interact with a setting, to setting design itself.<br /> <br /> Justin Achilli's own term at Paradox as far as the ttrpg saw things like extending compulsions to messy criticals, which can be traced back to passions in Pendragon, where when you succeed, you're compelled by them as far as mechanisms that narrow and reinforce a particular style of play. His oeuvre included the big book of &quot;the sabbat are not playable in official V5&quot; as far as keeping the game as a constrained idea space, and the dubiously playable versions of the Ravnos and Salubri that were reinforced speak to an attitude of limiting character build and range of play. And H5 and W5 otherwise, similarly intended as narrower games of narrower experiences.<br /> <br /> At some point a guy saying a game is great game design, and doing things that reflect that game's attitudes in his own work is, y'know, that. That's not a conspiracy, or a secret, that's people saying a thing, things in the game they work on reflecting the thing they say, and my deciding you can in fact take that at face value.<br /> <br /> It's the opposite of mindlessness. People are influenced in their efforts by things they think are great and inspiring examples of effort. That's just how people work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 12-30-2025, 06:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-30T04:06:35-08:00","id":1557141,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557136#post1557136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> snip</div> </div> </div> </div>Why yes I get that V5 staff likes Pendragon but what that has to do with them being a total assholes to player. <br /> <br /> Like I said again the main writer possible obsession with a semi obscure roleplaying game about aurthrian knights his little to do with they writing desctions. And like why I actually thought there's conspiracy because you kinda do. Like you seem to think that Pendragon is the root of all bad decstion the writer of 5e did and not just them being control freaks who just so happen to like Pendragon?<br /> <br /> Like I kinda get you're argument against prescriptivist until I realize that WtE is arguably more prescriptivist than w5. Like the books default setting is isolated to the pacific northwest due to all but 13 of the cearns are blown up during the apocalypse and the emphasis and maniacs to reclaim the ruined cearns blatantly hints that the ST should take a Star Trek TOS syle adventure per week style approach to chronicles. And you know what it's still superior to W5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-30T04:08:28-08:00","id":1557142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557117#post1557117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would put it like this, to dip back to the music comparison. Someone can say if they want that the Beatles are only symptomatic of why Oasis sound like they do, not a cause, but, that doesn't really bear out when Noel Gallagher is saying he took lyrics for Don't Look Back in Anger from a John Lennon interview and otherwise using some of his musical arrangements. And also just.. everything else about Oasis really.<br /> <br /> (And also Liam claiming to channel his spirit or something, but uhh.. let's all try and forget that happened)</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly I don't care. <br /> <br /> Im not a music guy nor a Pendragon guy.<br /> <br /> You should probably get out before the mods see this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-30T05:41:14-08:00","id":1557145,"title":"","content":"The thing is that it isn't how people work, it's a tiny piece of how people work. Boiling people down to one single influence that you then confirmation bias yourself (another thing all humans do to some extent) into seeing in everything they do is just... narrowing your scope of their work down to mesh your preconceptions. It leads to things like blaming Justin for the state of the Sabbat in V5 when the Sabbat were written out of playabity in V5 core via metaplot. All Justin did was not change that... and to some extent tried to retcon a somewhat less hamfisted version of events. You are pointing to the influence of Pendragon when the much more plausible, &quot;his bosses said no playable Sabbat and so he didn't bother trying to make playable Sabbat,&quot; is also right there. Being influenced by Pendragon does not explain why he changed from being pro-playable Sabbat during Revised, to anti-playable Sabbat in V5. A change in who writes his paychecks certainly does.<br /> <br /> It should not be hard to see that making the argument that if something a game developer that likes Pendragon does could have possibly been influenced by Pendragon, than it must have been causally related to those positive feelings towards Pendragon is not a productive way of analyzing anything.<br /> <br /> It is utterly impossible for me at least to separate the claim that, &quot;At some point a guy saying a game is great game design, and doing things that reflect that game's attitudes in his own work is, y'know, that.&quot; from the claim of, &quot;At some point a guy saying a game is great game design, and doing things I say can only exist as reflections of that game's attitudes in his own work is, y'know, that.&quot;<br /> <br /> It also completely blurs the line between a reasonable set of things a game designer might take away from Pendragon as things they want to try out in their own designs, and &quot;designs I don't like.&quot; When you jump straight from &quot;possible&quot; to &quot;nearly certain,&quot; without establishing &quot;likely&quot; in the middle it causes people to reasonably question if Justin was under the influence of Pendragon for X decision, or under a dozen other likely options including the very likely hazy mix of inspirations and pressures from life beyond his personal design philosophy. If you keep circling around to the same answer, why shouldn't people start questioning if that's because you came into it with the presupposition already in place and are messaging the information to fit? If you're going to call H5 a Pendragon inspired game... I have no idea what being inspired by Pendragon is supposed to mean. There's no connection in writing style, in setting design, in approach to what characters can be (H5 is technically less narrow than HtR original since Driven can be powered by whatever the ST/players want and ditched the Average Joe sentiment, while the Imbued are a very specific type of empowered hunter), and the biggest mechanical addition was something lifted from the Alien TTRPG.<br /> <br /> I didn't say the &quot;secret&quot; Pendragon clique as some sort of way to slide in a real actual conspiracy. It was intended much more to indicate a conspiracy theory line of thinking where we insert the Charlie Day Pepe Silvia meme. It feels like any post now, you're going to try to convince people that we don't get a Werewolf CCG card with a Zmei eating a literal clown because of the story both Rich Thomas and Justin have told about Justin getting a lesson in how to communicate with artists, but because it was what a Pendragon fan would have done to show their disapproval of the Zmei vs a proper Arthurian style dragon.<br /> <br /> People are not that simple in how influence gets filtered into their personal creative efforts. Trying to convince people that it's really important to study Pendragon to understand a specific creative when nothing they're making is remotely like Pendragon in totality just does not fit with experienced reality where there's lots of things pushing us in lots of different directions and we've got to figure out a solution that we can work with. The influence of Pendragon isn't hard to notice because of Pendragon's obscurity, but rather that the influence is so atomized that most things are just &quot;traditional RPG design,&quot; that have been used and reused so many times who did it first doesn't really matter to how they get used now. There's very few games that actually look like someone tried to do Pendragon but with a twist (speaking of Bill Bridges... Fading Suns is the biggest example of that I can think of since it is very much Pendragon's mechanical framework to do Dune but with knights working for the space-king). It feels like we're doing a weird tangent to the Ship of Theseus problem but instead of questioning if the pile of scraps or the floating boat is the real ship of Theseus, or if they both are, or aren't... someone grabbed five nails from the pile to use to finish a patch on an unrelated boat and someone's going, &quot;No, that new boat with the nails is also a Ship of Theseus.&quot; And at that point the label &quot;Ship of Theseus&quot; clearly doesn't mean much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-30T07:45:19-08:00","id":1557148,"title":"","content":"When the terminology game developers like Ken Hite use about Pendragon and what he considers its impact on rpg design to be are things like, verbatim to his words, &quot;Greg Stafford was an amazing, godlike, shamanic figure who created the space in which a lot of things later, a golden age would bloom with Pendragon&quot;, I really have no idea what else to note here. At some point this is just looking at statements people make on how significant they find a game to be, on how they view gaming, and just wave it off. Those are the terms in use. There seems to be this idea that I am pulling this impression out of nowhere. That's how the game is discussed in these spaces. If you want to roll with that talk about a game like that doesn't mean it should then be viewed as having a fulsome significance on things, okay.<br /> <br /> Just to stick with Ken Hite for a minute, he notes just after his initial work on V5 when talking about what he considers Pendragon's influence on things like V5's development of its personality mechanics &quot;We've just about gotten in Vampire the Masquerade development to where Greg was in 1984.&quot; Those are just his actual words that he speaks. That's not &quot;the influence is so atomized&quot;, that's one of the people who worked on V5 directly referencing the game and its developer to measure V5's development by. If people want to dismiss stuff like that as &quot;you're going on crazy tangents&quot;, hey sure, but, that's not me saying these things, that's, a guy who worked directly on this game, saying these things. These are the statements and thoughts being put forward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-30T11:20:18-08:00","id":1557150,"title":"","content":"OK gang, since this is vacay for a bunch of our mods, you get me. Not great for you! Here's a bit of text from a Monday Meeting Notes blog from just two weeks ago:<br /> <br /> &quot;We encourage and allow plenty of commentary about our games so long as it doesn\u2019t break the rules for each of those venues. Please be aware that we have a long history with our game lines, and even though they may not have been books that <b>Onyx Path</b> published as they were before our founding in 2012, many of us were part of the original <b>White Wolf</b>, or at least have friends that were. \u201c<i>I was there Gandalf, 3000 years ago at the founding of White Wolf!</i>\u201c&quot;<br /> <br /> And you were not. So while I normally say &quot;please&quot; here, do bear in mind that I'm only saying that to be polite and failure to knock it off with the theorizing about the behind the scenes stuff and then using that to demonstrate why X sucks will be met with bans in the new year. So: please stop insulting analyses that take an entire creative person and try and dilute them into a single data point in a theory you made up. No more Pendragon messed up Vampire, no more spreading internet gossip about past creators' personalities or preferences as if those single creators could possibly dominate the creation of game lines with dozens of professional hands working on them - and that were created by companies with business and marketing objectives that they imposed on the games. Specifically:<br /> <br /> MarkK: Seriously, please read the above and take it to heart. <br /> Heavy Arms: You do not need to win the internet. Also, if you are going to pull data points to support your rebuttals, please learn the difference between Stew and Steve Wieck.<br /> MrornX: You've used up the right to bring up WtE in any space here but Off Topic. Please limit yourself to that for announcements or commentary until a mod tells you otherwise.<br /> <br /> And to you all, this isn't something you can argue with me about, or justify, or whatever. Please don't attempt anything like that.<br /> <br /> Thanks, and have a Happy New Year!<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-30T15:48:16-08:00","id":1557154,"title":"","content":"Yeah uh moving on from that whould happen to WoD if Tencent actually did buyout paradox?<br /> <br /> Like would acually use the IP to make games, even if not something we want (like say a overwatch clone) or would they just sit on it and occasionally release a WoD theamed League of Legends skin pack if they're felling nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-30T16:26:57-08:00","id":1557155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557154#post1557154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah uh moving on from that whould happen to WoD if Tencent actually did buyout paradox?<br /> <br /> Like would acually use the IP to make games, even if not something we want (like say a overwatch clone) or would they just sit on it and occasionally release a WoD theamed League of Legends skin pack if they're felling nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait what?!<br /> <br /> On the other side I did have a few ideas a while ago for a VtM gacha game.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-30T16:31:18-08:00","id":1557156,"title":"","content":"Another company buying Paradox is a big if, of course, at this point. But if there were a time to do it, right now would be a pretty good time. <br /> <br /> To emphasize why we are in this kind of moment right now is that this is pretty much the consequences of Paradox's decisions over the last couple of years. The WOD-IP, Life By You, City Skylines 2 (especially combined with the promise of a console version)... From around 2017 to 2023 all these big plans had been made to grow Paradox. The WOD-IP was part of that. But now in 2025 the result of all those efforts equals zero pretty much. That's not to say everything Paradox did was bad. It's just that the missteps (Bloodlines 2, Life By You, for example) were too big and whatever number of visual novels and indie games that were put out under the Paradox ARC label, for example, weren't enough to make a difference.<br /> <br /> And when all was said and done, the tragic end we've arrived at is that while the grand strategy games were going strong in 2017 and they're still going strong now... If Paradox had never even tried to expand and had just kept going with its grand strategy games - it would be in the same place it is right now. That's just how bad Paradox management has been. They screwed up on every front. If it had just been one big promising title that underperformed, you could say: &quot;Shit happens. Videogame-development is hard.&quot; But when it's pretty much every big project turning into a disaster to some degree (or really big degree like with Life By You), I'm not gonna look at the developers when it comes to responsibility but rather at the publishers who oversaw the whole thing. <br /> <br /> As for what would happen, if a bigger company were to buy Paradox... Let's just cross that bridge when we get to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-30T17:33:15-08:00","id":1557160,"title":"","content":"Outright buying Paradox doesn't really follow Tencent's MO if that's even a thing that might happen.<br /> <br /> Tencent's usual practice is to buy a minority share in a company, basically enough to guarantee they control at least one seat on the board, and sit back and gather information. They get some say in their investment but get to dance around anti-trust laws by keeping their position small enough, and they have a gigantic network of suits sitting in on every major negotiation going on in the broader tech sector around the globe while dancing around insider-trading laws.<br /> <br /> As such, I doubt it would change anything for the WoD stuff because they would leave Paradox's current people in charge of things.<br /> <br /> For all that Paradox is not having a great time with various products, Europa Universalis V is doing great by their figures, and that's a flagship product for Paradox compared to the not great news around the games Knightingale pointed to. So Paradox isn't in a place where they have to sell, but a significant cash infusion wouldn't be bad for them either... which is basically something Tencent would love to jump on if they're thinking about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-30T18:09:25-08:00","id":1557161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557156#post1557156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another company buying Paradox is a big if, of course, at this point. But if there were a time to do it, right now would be a pretty good time.<br /> <br /> To emphasize why we are in this kind of moment right now is that this is pretty much the consequences of Paradox's decisions over the last couple of years. The WOD-IP, Life By You, City Skylines 2 (especially combined with the promise of a console version)... From around 2017 to 2023 all these big plans had been made to grow Paradox. The WOD-IP was part of that. But now in 2025 the result of all those efforts equals zero pretty much. That's not to say everything Paradox did was bad. It's just that the missteps (Bloodlines 2, Life By You, for example) were too big and whatever number of visual novels and indie games that were put out under the Paradox ARC label, for example, weren't enough to make a difference.<br /> <br /> And when all was said and done, the tragic end we've arrived at is that while the grand strategy games were going strong in 2017 and they're still going strong now... If Paradox had never even tried to expand and had just kept going with its grand strategy games - it would be in the same place it is right now. That's just how bad Paradox management has been. They screwed up on every front. If it had just been one big promising title that underperformed, you could say: &quot;Shit happens. Videogame-development is hard.&quot; But when it's pretty much every big project turning into a disaster to some degree (or really big degree like with Life By You), I'm not gonna look at the developers when it comes to responsibility but rather at the publishers who oversaw the whole thing.<br /> <br /> As for what would happen, if a bigger company were to buy Paradox... Let's just cross that bridge when we get to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The disasters are disasters, but on the idea of some larger company buying Paradox, it doesn't <i>feel</i> impossible, just unlikely. I wouldn't call any of its brands global flagships or anything, but, they do have several still successful and notable ones, relative to the video gaming space they traditionally exist in. If there was a largerish company looking to give themselves a grand strategy bloc of things, they could do a lot worse than Paradox. No clue what would happen if one did, but it's not implausible for a company to be looked at when struggling and be offered some relative dumptrucks of money that only have to be relative due to that struggling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-03T21:01:50-08:00","id":1557251,"title":"","content":"I'm glad things are being kept civil on this thread this far, it gives me some hope for people in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-04T21:18:37-08:00","id":1557296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557160#post1557160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Outright buying Paradox doesn't really follow Tencent's MO if that's even a thing that might happen.<br /> <br /> Tencent's usual practice is to buy a minority share in a company, basically enough to guarantee they control at least one seat on the board, and sit back and gather information. They get some say in their investment but get to dance around anti-trust laws by keeping their position small enough, and they have a gigantic network of suits sitting in on every major negotiation going on in the broader tech sector around the globe while dancing around insider-trading laws.<br /> <br /> As such, I doubt it would change anything for the WoD stuff because they would leave Paradox's current people in charge of things.<br /> <br /> For all that Paradox is not having a great time with various products, Europa Universalis V is doing great by their figures, and that's a flagship product for Paradox compared to the not great news around the games Knightingale pointed to. So Paradox isn't in a place where they have to sell, but a significant cash infusion wouldn't be bad for them either... which is basically something Tencent would love to jump on if they're thinking about it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah A IP sell off is more likely and if that happens I hope that WoD would be brought by a complaint company. I personally prefer Games Work Shop as sort of the best of the worst choice. Like if nothing else they got the contact number of OwlBear Studios who while not BG3 era Larian is still a complaint RPG maker so I would really Like to see what they can do with the VTM IP. Unless by some miracle OwlBear decide to buy WoD IP them selves since they are getting into the publishing game themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-06T11:38:00-08:00","id":1557348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557251#post1557251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm glad things are being kept civil on this thread this far, it gives me some hope for people in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>if anything it's surprising it isn't more salty, consider the broad variety of issues atm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-08T22:02:18-08:00","id":1557399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1555228#post1555228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is whose to blame for this is themselves so any assesment will be flawed.<br /> <br /> With that in mind. They may shelve m5 depending on w5 sales but continue low effort stuff from v5 and farming out the brand.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think it's a pretty safe bet we won't be getting an M5, C5, or any other 5 going forward, regardless of how well sales do.<br /> <br /> 5th edition seems to want to keep the power scaling at street level, which is fine for Vampire and Werewolf. But completely ruins the premise of any other splat in the system.<br /> <br /> The entire goal of Mage is to ascend to the level of a cosmic power house, for whom reality is your plaything. While we have Changelings performing Arch Mage level feats straight out of character creation with their Arts and Cantrips.<br /> <br /> Demons are quite literally an apocalyptic level threat, depending on how much faith they're able to harvest.<br /> <br /> You can't reduce these splats down to street level without introducing a catastrophic nerf to their power systems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-12T07:24:13-08:00","id":1557506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557154#post1557154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah uh moving on from that whould happen to WoD if Tencent actually did buyout paradox?<br /> <br /> Like would acually use the IP to make games, even if not something we want (like say a overwatch clone) or would they just sit on it and occasionally release a WoD theamed League of Legends skin pack if they're felling nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Likelihood of it happening aside, buying either Paradox or the IP Tencent would be likely to keep at making WoD.<br /> <br /> Their MO with such things is to use the IPs they get, and on top of that they are (far more successfully than Paradox) investing heavily into branching their business into other areas and media. So a TTRPG franchise isn't out of their ambitions, and for now isn't something they have. And they'd certainly make mobile games, that's a given.<br /> <br /> Also they're heavily into transitioning things to the Digital Age. They already bought comics and manga to turn into web versions and other such things, and they have a growing market place. I would expect not just more PDFs, but subscriptions, online play services and aids, WoD-related social media stuff, overall a lot more digital support for the game. We may also get CoD back on the works.<br /> <br /> But the downside would be less development of new things, which we can't say how it will affect WoD specifically, and less support to the on-digital side of things. Tencent has a history of keeping things they buy going, but not invest on further development. Game companies they bought kept working with their flagship titles, for example, and even other titles, but the development of new titles practically came to a halt. They're also more likely to copy things that make success than make something truly new, being one of the few Chinese companies to already be mired in copyright lawsuits within China itself since the 90's.<br /> <br /> How does that affect WoD and CoD? Maybe they just get back to letting Onyx Path and others work to their heart's content on those lines and focus on making the digital side happen. Maybe they just focus on improving the Storyteller's Vault as a marketplace and keep selling old books for the rest of time. Maybe they focus development into turning WoD5 unto itself and use the rules to re-release updated versions of old books forever, with rules updates from time to time and that's it. All of those are on their ballpark.<br /> <br /> I think it's not the worse gamble for the IP from our perspective, but it's still a gamble.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557160#post1557160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Outright buying Paradox doesn't really follow Tencent's MO if that's even a thing that might happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, they do that sometimes, at least when they think they can get around antitrust laws. Paradox being Swedish and working with a rather particular market are things that may make it possible.<br /> <br /> But I agree that it is extremely unlikely. Good moments to buy out a company are when the company is facing serious financial hurdles, and that's not where Paradox is right now, but a sizable yet not major chunk of participation is certainly something that may happen. I do think they try to have some influence, though, and that may change things for the IPs. It's just a maybe, but it's there.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557399#post1557399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's a pretty safe bet we won't be getting an M5, C5, or any other 5 going forward, regardless of how well sales do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that assessment greatly ignores how they've been working.<br /> <br /> Scaling at street level is definitely <b>not</b> ok for Werewolf, it's about a society of superlative warriors that literally have a non-negligible chance at facing gods head on in combat and win, dedicated to literally fight the end of the world as an actual war without it looking like delusion.<br /> <br /> Yet that's exactly what they did: they scaled it down through a catastrophic nerf to its power system. The same thing they did to Hunter by ditching the Imbued and focusing on <i>Hunters Hunted</i> level protagonists. And in the process completely destroyed those settings, converting Werewolf in particular into something almost unrecognizable.<br /> <br /> While I definitely agree that you can't make the other games well enough by focusing on street level, nothing in this phrase is something they're either dedicated to do or competent at evaluating.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-12T09:02:33-08:00","id":1557510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557506#post1557506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I think that assessment greatly ignores how they've been working.<br /> <br /> Scaling at street level is definitely <b>not</b> ok for Werewolf, it's about a society of superlative warriors that literally have a non-negligible chance at facing gods head on in combat and win, dedicated to literally fight the end of the world as an actual war without it looking like delusion.<br /> <br /> Yet that's exactly what they did: they scaled it down through a catastrophic nerf to its power system. The same thing they did to Hunter by ditching the Imbued and focusing on <i>Hunters Hunted</i> level protagonists. And in the process completely destroyed those settings, converting Werewolf in particular into something almost unrecognizable.<br /> <br /> While I definitely agree that you can't make the other games well enough by focusing on street level, nothing in this phrase is something they're either dedicated to do or competent at evaluating.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, I forgot about shit like Nexus Crawlers and other cosmic horrors.<br /> <br /> But it also looks like they've scaled down the level of threats they have to face too.<br /> <br /> Take a look at Gorehounds from previous editions. Effectively a human shaped blender, that exists only to slaughter everything within reach.<br /> <br /> Now look at them in W5; it's a guy with a knife for a hand. Oooh, scary! How ever will my Crinos form deal with that!?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-13T00:27:54-08:00","id":1557537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557510#post1557510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now look at them in W5; it's a guy with a knife for a hand. Oooh, scary! How ever will my Crinos form deal with that!?</div> </div> </div> </div>You know I wonder what would happen if a W20 character was dropped into W5 and how fast and catastrophically they'll derail things. <br /> <br /> Also there's an upcoming W20 based fan book that offers a W20 to W5 conversion guide. I don't know How that would work nor how that balance would pan out with the published adventures since but it's a handy tool for an ST if nothing else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-13T01:22:08-08:00","id":1557538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557537#post1557537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know I wonder what would happen if a W20 character was dropped into W5 and how fast and catastrophically they'll derail things.<br /> <br /> Also there's an upcoming W20 based fan book that offers a W20 to W5 conversion guide. I don't know How that would work nor how that balance would pan out with the published adventures since but it's a handy tool for an ST if nothing else.</div> </div> </div> </div>The power level/competancy differance is absurd. Realistically anything which is a problem for a w20 is going to approachable for a w5. I imagine immediate derailment as well as a low key existential issue created by the uberwolf showing up.<br /> <br /> W5 werewolves are potentially a step down from human/wolf so it looks really bad against something which was actual made for what they're supposed to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 01-13-2026, 04:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-13T02:55:46-08:00","id":1557541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557538#post1557538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The power level/competancy differance is absurd. Realistically anything which is a problem for a w20 is going to approachable for a w5. I imagine immediate derailment as well as a low key existential issue created by the uberwolf showing up.<br /> <br /> W5 werewolves are potentially a step down from human/wolf so it looks really bad against something which was actual made for what they're supposed to do.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So how bad is the derailment on the scale of a luner showing up to paradoxproof mage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-13T06:14:24-08:00","id":1557544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557537#post1557537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know I wonder what would happen if a W20 character was dropped into W5 and how fast and catastrophically they'll derail things.<br /> <br /> Also there's an upcoming W20 based fan book that offers a W20 to W5 conversion guide. I don't know How that would work nor how that balance would pan out with the published adventures since but it's a handy tool for an ST if nothing else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering you'd need an elder vampire to have a realistic chance of bringing one down in single combat?<br /> <br /> Your deed name should be <i>&quot;Kills With One Punch.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Might of Thor doubles your Strength score, if I'm not mistaken. Which means if the Get has 5-6 Strength, they temporarily shoot up to Antedeluvian levels!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-13T09:43:46-08:00","id":1557549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557544#post1557544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Might of Thor doubles your Strength score, if I'm not mistaken. Which means if the Get has 5-6 Strength, they temporarily shoot up to Antedeluvian levels!</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, Fortitude will shrug that off<br /> You wantto go all-in?<br /> <b>Paws of the Newborn Cub:</b> The Garou prevents a target from using <i>any</i> special or supernatural abilities. She is as a &quot;newborn cub&quot;, with only mundane powers at her disposal. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-13T11:26:16-08:00","id":1557550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557549#post1557549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nah, Fortitude will shrug that off<br /> You wantto go all-in?<br /> <b>Paws of the Newborn Cub:</b> The Garou prevents a target from using <i>any</i> special or supernatural abilities. She is as a &quot;newborn cub&quot;, with only mundane powers at her disposal.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Of course the other tribes would use a rite that reduces their enemies to defenseless babies.<br /> <br /> Guys, this shit is why the Get of Fenris are your greatest warriors!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-13T11:44:47-08:00","id":1557553,"title":"","content":"What does any of this actually matter?<br /> <br /> While I don't broadly object to the &quot;multiverse fight!&quot; genre of online debate, it doesn't really work if we're not even trying to account for things like mechanical differences. A W20 Garou dropped in a D&amp;D setting isn't fairly being compared to anything when they get hit with a Str of 5, and only 9 in Crinos... most wizards in D&amp;D have better Str scores than that.<br /> <br /> I also have no idea when this actually says something about business decisions at Paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-13T12:02:54-08:00","id":1557554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557553#post1557553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does any of this actually matter?<br /> <br /> While I don't broadly object to the &quot;multiverse fight!&quot; genre of online debate, it doesn't really work if we're not even trying to account for things like mechanical differences. A W20 Garou dropped in a D&amp;D setting isn't fairly being compared to anything when they get hit with a Str of 5, and only 9 in Crinos... most wizards in D&amp;D have better Str scores than that.<br /> <br /> I also have no idea when this actually says something about business decisions at Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>5 dots on the character sheet is supposed to represent the peak of normal human capabilities.<br /> <br /> At 5 Strength, you can lift upwards of 650 pounds. Which in the world of D&amp;D would be equivalent to having a score of 17 (500 lbs).<br /> <br /> At 9 Strength, you can lift 1,200 pounds, which is equivalent to a score of 18 / 51-75 in D&amp;D (1,250 lbs).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-13T12:30:07-08:00","id":1557555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557554#post1557554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 5 dots on the character sheet is supposed to represent the peak of normal human capabilities.<br /> <br /> At 5 Strength, you can lift upwards of 650 pounds. Which in the world of D&amp;D would be equivalent to having a score of 17 (500 lbs).<br /> <br /> At 9 Strength, you can lift 1,200 pounds, which is equivalent to a score of 18 / 51-75 in D&amp;D (1,250 lbs).</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're going by current D&amp;D, lift is strength score x30 for a medium sized humanish being, so 650 pounds would be about.. str 22, and 1200 wouldn't really be possible to accomplish off pure strength total without some feat or species trait that doubles lift/carrying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-13T12:39:10-08:00","id":1557556,"title":"","content":"If Shadowrun can finally switch over to quadratic-scaled lift weights, any system can, and probably should at this point. Especially D&amp;D, because you're not getting XP for how much treasure you haul up anymore, and really haven't since AD&amp;D 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-13T14:45:06-08:00","id":1557560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557544#post1557544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering you'd need an elder vampire to have a realistic chance of bringing one down in single combat?<br /> <br /> Your deed name should be <i>&quot;Kills With One Punch.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Might of Thor doubles your Strength score, if I'm not mistaken. Which means if the Get has 5-6 Strength, they temporarily shoot up to Antedeluvian levels!</div> </div> </div> </div>So You're saying he's a one punch wolf? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557553#post1557553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does any of this actually matter?<br /> <br /> While I don't broadly object to the &quot;multiverse fight!&quot; genre of online debate, it doesn't really work if we're not even trying to account for things like mechanical differences. A W20 Garou dropped in a D&amp;D setting isn't fairly being compared to anything when they get hit with a Str of 5, and only 9 in Crinos... most wizards in D&amp;D have better Str scores than that.<br /> <br /> I also have no idea when this actually says something about business decisions at Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know what Fair. That's why I just made a new thread on Werewolf Forum: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5\">https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/...w20-wolf-in-w5</a><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-13T20:24:03-08:00","id":1557575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557560#post1557560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So You're saying he's a one punch wolf?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that was the joke. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557555#post1557555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you're going by current D&amp;D, lift is strength score x30 for a medium sized humanish being, so 650 pounds would be about.. str 22, and 1200 wouldn't really be possible to accomplish off pure strength total without some feat or species trait that doubles lift/carrying.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be equivalent to 40 Strength, which is something that only early edition Deities, and legendary boss monsters ever had access to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":". 01-13-2026, 11:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-14T04:55:25-08:00","id":1557588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557553#post1557553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A W20 Garou dropped in a D&amp;D setting isn't fairly being compared to anything when they get hit with a Str of 5, and only 9 in Crinos... most wizards in D&amp;D have better Str scores than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Strength in D&amp;D does not function on the same scale as Strength in WoD.<br /> <br /> In WoD, two (2) dots of Strength is considered the average for humans. Conversely, Strength 10 is average for humans in D&amp;D (the Str score of a Commoner).<br /> <br /> WoD Strength tops out at 5 dots for humans, while D&amp;D Strength tops out at 20 for mortals.<br /> <br /> Just going by that, I'd say D&amp;D Strength is about 4-5x WoD Strength for the same notional value. Don't quote me on that, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-14T05:51:05-08:00","id":1557592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557575#post1557575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would be equivalent to 40 Strength, which is something that only early edition Deities, and legendary boss monsters ever had access to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, no, not what I mean there.<br /> <br /> Okay, in the D&amp;D in use for the last 12 years or so, 5e, ability scores top out at 30 overall, just generally across the board. So for a medium sized humanoid, you basically can't build one with a lift over 900 pounds (30 times 30), without either a species trait like Goliaths have, or some class or feat effect that doubles carry/lift/etc.<br /> <br /> Otherwise you have to go up a size category to large, which doubles lift/carry/etc. values. So for example, for a large sized being, Str 20 would get you 1200, as 30 x20 is 600, and you then double that.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-29T01:22:27-08:00","id":1557982,"title":"","content":"The Year-End-Report has been <a href=\"https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/investors/financial-reports/year-end-report-january-december-2025\" target=\"_blank\">released</a>. Overall, not that many surprises. The grand-strategy-games have done well but Bloodlines 2 has turned out to be a failure. A <i>costly </i>failure to boot, which really dragged down Paradox's performance last year. <br /> <br /> Some excerpts from the CEO's comment on the state of things:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We closed the year with our most intense quarter in company history. With two new game releases, one remaster, and DLCs for most titles, we held a pace that truly demonstrates the strength of our organisation and our portfolio. The core business delivered strong performance with high revenues and solid cash flow. However, the results for the period were impacted by currency headwinds and the write-down of Vampire: The Masquerade \u2013 Bloodlines 2, as the game did not meet our commercial expectations. At the same time, this marks an important turning point: we are now strengthening our strategic focus, reallocating resources, and creating even better conditions for future investments where we have our greatest expertise and long-term potential.<br /> <br /> [ ... ]<br /> <br /> As we look ahead, we do so with clarity, focus, and strengthened confidence. Vampire: The Masquerade \u2013 Bloodlines 2 was the last major project in development that was outside of our core areas. As post-release work winds down, resources and focus are being redirected to projects where we know we can create the greatest value. Our future pipeline is now fully concentrated on deep strategy and management games, with the majority developed in our own studios which provides both creative strength and long-term profitability. </div> </div> </div>So the strategy seems to be: One, to focus on grand strategy and management games and two, to make sure that most of the time they work with developer-studios they own. I suspect the future will be low-budget stuff like visual novels and text-adventures for the WOD IP from here on out. And who knows how much they even care whether we get something like a Mage Fifth Edition or not. <br /> <br /> There will be an earnings-call later today and I will post the transcript here as soon as it's available. I'm sure there will be a bit more about any plans regarding the WOD-IP and the new White Wolf in that talk.<br /> <br /> By the way, White Wolf never even gets mentioned in the report. That shows how low it is on their priority-list. Especially now with their renewed focus on strategy and management games. Again, not that surprising, but I figure I would mention that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-29T10:02:30-08:00","id":1557987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557982#post1557982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Year-End-Report has been <a href=\"https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/investors/financial-reports/year-end-report-january-december-2025\" target=\"_blank\">released</a>. Overall, not that many surprises. The grand-strategy-games have done well but Bloodlines 2 has turned out to be a failure. A <i>costly </i>failure to boot, which really dragged down Paradox's performance last year.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anybody who was even remotely near the same zipcode of being surprised by Bloodlines 2 flopping was clearly not paying attention to its development cycle.<br /> <br /> It would have been better if they had just cancelled the game outright.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-29T11:57:33-08:00","id":1557989,"title":"","content":"While we all did see a flop as a very likely possibility based on the development costs and what the game was shaping up to be, cancelling isn't always the best idea. I know it's popular for a lot of companies to just cancel projects, but that really depends on their tax situation (not every project can get written off for a tax break) and their deal structure with TCR. The game did sell too, so there was some decrease in the hit from the sales, even if it was pretty much never going to make a profit in the end.<br /> <br /> While I don't know the applicable laws for Paradox, their record is to release over cancel for games that are mostly done even if not great. So I'd assume that means their books are setup in a fashion where the money from what sales they do get is better than whatever cancelling could get them elsewhere in the corporate schema.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-29T16:24:50-08:00","id":1558004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557989#post1557989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game did sell too, so there was some decrease in the hit from the sales, even if it was pretty much never going to make a profit in the end.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the game sold, but the majority of the player base stopped playing within the first 2 hours, because of how boring and repetitive the game was. Just the same three types of side quests over and over again. Also, it seems pretty widely agreed upon that we all <b>HATE</b> the Fabien portions of the game. So much, in fact, they released a new update that lets you skip them completely.<br /> <br /> It's tragic, because the original plan for the game looked like it would have actually been interesting. Playing as a Thinblood who eventually joins one of the clans would have been a better character progression than playing as a depowered Elder.<br /> <br /> The whole appeal of being an Elder in the first place, is you are a god among insects. If you're going to strip them of their power, then all you're left with is a blood sucker who's mentality is far outdated for the modern world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-29T16:57:02-08:00","id":1558005,"title":"","content":"OK... but what does that have to do with what I said? Unless a huge portion of people that bought the game got refunds, the copies sold are money to offset the loses Paradox is going to face once all the numbers settle. BL2 isn't a live service microtransaction game that needs a lot of players over a long period of time to make money. It needed a lot of sales in the first week, and it didn't hit those numbers (yes, the reception hurt that).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-30T02:27:45-08:00","id":1558014,"title":"","content":"Cancelling would've been better compared to where we are now. Or, for example, following the advice of that one Chinese Room developer and rename the game, so that you can have better (more accurate) marketing for the game. It's easy to be judgmental now, of course. Hindsight is 20/20, as they say. For me, the thing Paradox management still hasn't sufficiently explained is why they have put this much money towards these projects &quot;outside of their core areas&quot; as they call it. Same with Life By You, the Sims-like life-simulator that they eventually canceled. They were throwing tens of millions of dollars at these projects. I get the part that these failed due to a lack of expertise and understanding of managing games in these genres. But at the same time, where was that confidence coming from to spend this much money on these projects? In both cases, alarm-bells should've been going off way earlier, considering how much money they were spending there. With the type of money they were spending there, these weren't merely &quot;forays into news genres&quot; for Paradox, these turned into high-risk-gambits. And why would you make high-risk-gambits with games in genres that you have little experience in? And it's this type of bad judgment that's looming over Paradox and eroding investor-trust.<br /> <br /> __________________________________________________ ________________<br /> <br /> Here's a link to <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/article/4864194-paradox-interactive-ab-publ-prxxf-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript\" target=\"_blank\">a transcript of the earnings-call from yesterday (via SeekingAlpha)</a>. I will highlight the most relevant part for this thread as Fredrik Wester (CEO) talks about exploring IPs beyond videogames:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Alexander Bricca<br /> Chief Financial Officer<br /> <br /> Yes. Fred, this is for you. Many companies are expanding their IPs beyond games into other products and media. How does Paradox think about brand extension and additional revenue streams outside of traditional game development?<br /> <br /> Fredrik Wester<br /> Founder, Director &amp; CEO<br /> <br /> Yes. I mean we have been experimenting a bit with this. We do merchandising. We do board games. We do licenses to other video games companies for some of our IP, most notably White Wolf IP. But it's a great way to strengthen IP recognition. It hasn't had any significant impact on revenue or profit, but it's still a good way to keep the IP alive and to reach new target audiences. So this is something we're going to continue. I mean there are no -- just -- I think what they're after here is like a TV dealer equivalent. There's nothing like that on the table at the moment.<br /> <br /> But who knows in the future, but I think we need to work more on deepening and strengthening our IP as they are. We work a lot with history in our Grand Strategy games. We work with the fantasy IP in Age of Wonders. We work with Stellaris, for example, that are very strong or Stellaris and Age of Wonders are their own IP where we own everything. When you use history as your background, it's harder to sort of work with the IP, if you like. But also the White Wolf catalog offers a wide range of really interesting ways to expand into new universes of opportunities. </div> </div> </div>I think it really just reinforces what has already been said. White Wolf and the book-side of things is not that high on the priority-list. If footnotes could have footnotes, that's probably where Paradox would put all the book-stuff with the WOD-IP in a year-end-report. <br /> <br /> But regarding bad judgment, there's also been some new developments with Bloodlines 2. Namely, they've announced a revision of their release-schedule for the DLC (via <a href=\"https://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/bloodlines-2-2026-roadmap-moves-up-expansion-release-windows-slightly-and-yes-bloodlines-2-has-a-roadmap-for-2026/\" target=\"_blank\">PCGamer</a>):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First up is the Valentine's Update, set to go live on February 11 with &quot;new cosmetics, facial hair, enemy loot, [and] bug fixes.&quot; After that is the Loose Cannon expansion, initially expected to be out in Q2 2026 (so, sometime between April 1 and June 30), which is now slated for the maybe-possibly earlier Q1/Q2. Then comes The Flower and the Flame expansion, originally set for Q3 (July 1-September 30) and now targeting the similarly wider window of Q2/Q3. </div> </div> </div>Hopefully, this won't impact development too much. But when these DLCs are released and they turn out to be buggy, short, uninspired or anything like that, this will come up as an explanation as to why it might be like that, I'm sure. I get it, Paradox wants this over and done with as soon as possible but do we really need another wave of bad press here if the DLC comes out and it feels like development was rushed? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-30T09:19:15-08:00","id":1558021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1558014#post1558014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cancelling would've been better compared to where we are now. Or, for example, following the advice of that one Chinese Room developer and rename the game, so that you can have better (more accurate) marketing for the game. It's easy to be judgmental now, of course. Hindsight is 20/20, as they say. For me, the thing Paradox management still hasn't sufficiently explained is why they have put this much money towards these projects &quot;outside of their core areas&quot; as they call it. Same with Life By You, the Sims-like life-simulator that they eventually canceled. They were throwing tens of millions of dollars at these projects. I get the part that these failed due to a lack of expertise and understanding of managing games in these genres. But at the same time, where was that confidence coming from to spend this much money on these projects? In both cases, alarm-bells should've been going off way earlier, considering how much money they were spending there. With the type of money they were spending there, these weren't merely &quot;forays into news genres&quot; for Paradox, these turned into high-risk-gambits. And why would you make high-risk-gambits with games in genres that you have little experience in? And it's this type of bad judgment that's looming over Paradox and eroding investor-trust.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, it seems like Troika managed to capture lightning in a bottle when they made the first Bloodlines game.<br /> <br /> Almost every other attempt to tackle the franchise has either met with failure, or been a severe downgrade from what people were hoping for.<br /> <br /> <b>Heart of Gaia</b> - Cancelled<br /> <br /> <b>Earthblood</b> - generic hack and slash, which you can buy for 2 dollars during a Steam sale<br /> <br /> <b>Blood Hunt</b> - Fortnite Battle Royale<br /> <br /> <b>Swansong</b> - Detective Walking Simulator<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodlines 2</b> - Abysmal Disappointment<br /> <br /> <b>Afterlife</b> - Wraith Walking Simulator<br /> <br /> <b>Justice</b> - Decent VR game, but still a far cry from Bloodlines<br /> <br /> The only games which seem to do well are CYOA novels. It's easy to see why people say this IP is cursed. At this point, Paradox should probably just cut their losses and sell it to somebody else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":". 01-30-2026, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-30T09:31:56-08:00","id":1558022,"title":"","content":"I just read a transcript of the earnings call Paradox had yesterday and it looked like they\u2019re going with the keep the IP but just license it out option<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/article/4864194-paradox-interactive-ab-publ-prxxf-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript\" target=\"_blank\">https://seekingalpha.com/article/486...all-transcript</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":".  Added link to aforementioned transcript 01-30-2026, 12:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-30T12:56:32-08:00","id":1558028,"title":"","content":"Bloodhunt was (IS) a good game, simple and free. I never liked the aesthetics of the PCs though, that's the only thing I could point out. Of course, it could've been better.<br /> <br /> I really enjoyed Draw Distance's New York saga.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-30T13:17:56-08:00","id":1558029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1558028#post1558028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bloodhunt was (IS) a good game, simple and free. I never liked the aesthetics of the PCs though, that's the only thing I could point out. Of course, it could've been better.<br /> <br /> I really enjoyed Draw Distance's New York saga.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm willing to entertain the idea that the game might be good as a stand alone vampire Battle Royale.<br /> <br /> But as part of the World of Darkness franchise? It is absolute garbage!<br /> <br /> Blood Hunts are supposed to be a city wide manhunt for a designated target, NOT a free for all turf grab, in which every vampire tries to slaughter each other in the streets. What the fuck did the developers think MASQUERADE stood for?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-30T13:28:58-08:00","id":1558030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1558029#post1558029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm willing to entertain the idea that the game might be good as a stand alone vampire Battle Royale.<br /> <br /> But as part of the World of Darkness franchise? It is absolute garbage!<br /> <br /> Blood Hunts are supposed to be a city wide manhunt for a designated target, NOT a free for all turf grab, in which every vampire tries to slaughter each other in the streets. What the fuck did the developers think MASQUERADE stood for?</div> </div> </div> </div>I see your point, you're right there.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-30T15:52:16-08:00","id":1558033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1558021#post1558021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only games which seem to do well are CYOA novels. It's easy to see why people say this IP is cursed. At this point, Paradox should probably just cut their losses and sell it to somebody else.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, you skipped the four of the most commercially successful games in the IP's history (Redemption, and the Hunter trilogy), so it's going to look at lot worse. You also counted a game that got cancelled very early in development (Heart of Gaia) but skipped the far more development-intensive-but-still-cancelled MMO.<br /> <br /> I think it's also worth putting this into a wider perspective. Adapting existing IPs to video games has always been a pretty iffy thing with way more duds than successes. The most common issue is that adapting is a lot of work, and trying to create a new experience for customers to play is a lot of work... doing both is a nearly impossible amount of work. So most adaptations are just slapping an IP's coat of paint on an existing game and hoping the name recognition is good enough people will play something they've basically already played before but with IP assets on top.<br /> <br /> For a long time, that worked fine. But the video game industry has changed a lot and such efforts are increasingly less appealing to audiences. Games like Marvel Rivals have to be excellent games that would do well without the IP; where being Marvel only pushes them over the line into top-tier successful game. Nobody was expecting that big of a game out of Bloodlines 2 (then again, most people weren't expecting such a big game out of Marvel Rivals either), but the last 10 years of video games have solidly shown that IPs from other media don't sell copies if the game isn't good enough to be good without the IP.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1558028#post1558028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bloodhunt was (IS) a good game, simple and free.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Will have been&quot; is an unfortunately clunky tense form in English. Bloodhunt is in the abysmal situation of it's servers being shut down in three months but is still open anyway.<br /> <br /> That said, to build on what I was saying above, Bloodhunt didn't really do anything to help stand out in a very crowded sub-market of video games and one that is far more zero-sum than the rest. F2P live service BRs are a dime a dozen and new ones are constantly coming and going. It's not that all the new ones are bad, some are even just as good as the mainstays like Fortnight, but nobody that's playing Fortnight is dropping it to play something just as good. If you can't carve out a niche, or at least do better that someone that's in a specific niche to get people to switch over, it's a style of video game that's unsustainable without a large number of regular players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-30T16:43:58-08:00","id":1558034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1558033#post1558033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, you skipped the four of the most commercially successful games in the IP's history (Redemption, and the Hunter trilogy), so it's going to look at lot worse. You also counted a game that got cancelled very early in development (Heart of Gaia) but skipped the far more development-intensive-but-still-cancelled MMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't forget Redemption, I was listing the games which did poorly. Though I did forget about the cancelled MMO.<br /> <br /> As for the Hunter trilogy, I've heard about this game several times over the years, but I personally have never seen any footage of its gameplay, much less its existence. People say the game was good, but as I have no experience with it, I'll withhold my opinion.<br /> <br /> <br /> CYOA Novels though, seem to be doing alright. Though that might be the case of me having nostalgia, since I loved those kinds of books when I was a child.<br /> <br /> Parliament of Knives, Book of Hungry Names, and Night Road were all enjoyable.<br /> <br /> The <b>New York</b> trilogy was a fucking scam. I think GreatHornedRatkin pointed out in another thread how your choices have no impact on the story?<br /> <br /> <b>Heart of the Forest</b> didn't seem too bad, but the fact it was essentially a Session Zero story prevented me from buying it. You don't even get to pick your tribe until near the end of the story, and you don't have access to any gifts / rites.<br /> <br /> I haven't checked out <b>Purgatory </b>in great detail, so once again, I'll withhold my opinion. Though I'm given to understand you play a more experienced werewolf in that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":". 01-30-2026, 07:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-31T00:01:48-08:00","id":1558037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1558034#post1558034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The <b>New York</b> trilogy was a fucking scam. I think GreatHornedRatkin pointed out in another thread how your choices have no impact on the story?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, I did; and I continue to stand by that assessment.<br /> <br /> The only choice in Coteries that matters is whether or not you survive the trial scene. After that, it's smooth sailing all the way to the finish. I've heard that Shadows is supposed to have learned from its mistakes, but after my experience with Coteries, I wasn't going to take the risk of dropping money on it.<br /> <br /> IF they did learn, it seems they suffered a relapse in the third game. Because they went right back to ignoring the player's previous decisions in order to present their own 'official' take on how the story played out.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you want to sell me a game, make sure it's an actual game. If you want to sell me your fanfiction, just write a book!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-31T08:57:05-08:00","id":1558043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1558037#post1558037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes, I did; and I continue to stand by that assessment.<br /> <br /> The only choice in Coteries that matters is whether or not you survive the trial scene. After that, it's smooth sailing all the way to the finish. I've heard that Shadows is supposed to have learned from its mistakes, but after my experience with Coteries, I wasn't going to take the risk of dropping money on it.<br /> <br /> IF they did learn, it seems they suffered a relapse in the third game. Because they went right back to ignoring the player's previous decisions in order to present their own 'official' take on how the story played out.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you want to sell me a game, make sure it's an actual game. If you want to sell me your fanfiction, just write a book!</div> </div> </div> </div>To me Shadow of New York is worth it. I buy it really cheap at a steam discount. The visuals are really nice and the story is worth it. They only thing I'd like to point out was the intention of Julia Sowinski as a character. She seems to be an intention to erase Lucita out of the minds of the fans and make her THE Lasombra flag bearer, that I didn't like.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-31T09:21:36-08:00","id":1558044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1558037#post1558037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes, I did; and I continue to stand by that assessment.<br /> <br /> The only choice in Coteries that matters is whether or not you survive the trial scene. After that, it's smooth sailing all the way to the finish. I've heard that Shadows is supposed to have learned from its mistakes, but after my experience with Coteries, I wasn't going to take the risk of dropping money on it.<br /> <br /> IF they did learn, it seems they suffered a relapse in the third game. Because they went right back to ignoring the player's previous decisions in order to present their own 'official' take on how the story played out.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you want to sell me a game, make sure it's an actual game. If you want to sell me your fanfiction, just write a book!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Essentially and without spoilling, in terms of choices, you have a &quot;survive the trial&quot; choice, then the game railroad you into a series of situation in which you'll have choice based outcomes that raise an invisible meter in one of two &quot;side&quot; ND at the end of the game, whichever of those is higher determine your ending. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-01T05:55:32-08:00","id":1558054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1558043#post1558043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To me Shadow of New York is worth it. I buy it really cheap at a steam discount. The visuals are really nice and the story is worth it. They only thing I'd like to point out was the intention of Julia Sowinski as a character. She seems to be an intention to erase Lucita out of the minds of the fans and make her THE Lasombra flag bearer, that I didn't like.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>I found some of her monologues a little clunky and her dialogue a bit try hard. Plus like you said cam 'safe' lucita.<br /> <br /> Shes pretty cool but her presence is emblematic of deeper issues","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}